export const PACK = { id: "core-v2", json: "[{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A parallelogram has a base of 18 meters and an adjacent side of 13 meters. The height of the parallelogram, measured perpendicular to the base, is 11 meters. What is the area, in square meters, of the parallelogram?\",\"option_a\":\"$62$\",\"option_b\":\"$99$\",\"option_c\":\"$143$\",\"option_d\":\"$198$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The area of a parallelogram is base times height, where the height is perpendicular to the base: $18 \\\\cdot 11 = 198$ square meters. The slanted side length 13 is not used. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($62$) is the perimeter, $2(18 + 13)$. Choice B ($99$) uses the triangle formula $\\\\frac{1}{2}bh$. Choice C ($143$) multiplies the slanted side by the height, $13 \\\\cdot 11$, instead of the base by the height.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Parallelogramm yuzasi asos va unga perpendikulyar balandlik ko‘paytmasiga teng: $18 \\\\cdot 11 = 198$ kvadrat metr. Qiya tomon uzunligi 13 bu yerda kerak emas. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA ($62$) — bu perimetr, $2(18 + 13)$. B ($99$) — uchburchak formulasi $\\\\frac{1}{2}bh$ ishlatilgan. C ($143$) — asos o‘rniga qiya tomon balandlikka ko‘paytirilgan, $13 \\\\cdot 11$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"An aquarium is shaped like a rectangular prism. The inside of its base is 50 centimeters long and 30 centimeters wide, and the water in it is 20 centimeters deep. If 1 liter equals 1,000 cubic centimeters, how many liters of water are in the aquarium?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"30\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The water forms a rectangular prism, so its volume is $50 \\\\cdot 30 \\\\cdot 20 = 30{,}000$ cubic centimeters. Dividing by 1,000 converts to liters: $\\\\frac{30{,}000}{1{,}000} = 30$ liters.\\n\\nIf you entered 30000, you found the volume in cubic centimeters but did not convert to liters.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Suv to‘g‘ri burchakli parallelepiped shaklini egallaydi, uning hajmi $50 \\\\cdot 30 \\\\cdot 20 = 30{,}000$ kub santimetr. Litrga o‘tkazish uchun 1,000 ga bo‘lamiz: $\\\\frac{30{,}000}{1{,}000} = 30$ litr.\\n\\nAgar 30000 javob chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz hajmni kub santimetrda topgansiz, lekin litrga o‘tkazmagansiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A square tile has a perimeter of 36 centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the tile?\",\"option_a\":\"$36$\",\"option_b\":\"$81$\",\"option_c\":\"$324$\",\"option_d\":\"$1{,}296$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"A square has 4 equal sides, so each side is $\\\\frac{36}{4} = 9$ centimeters. The area is $9^2 = 81$ square centimeters. Choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($36$) repeats the perimeter. Choice C ($324$) divides the perimeter by 2 instead of 4, giving a side of 18 and $18^2 = 324$. Choice D ($1{,}296$) squares the perimeter, $36^2$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kvadratning 4 ta tomoni teng, demak har bir tomon $\\\\frac{36}{4} = 9$ santimetr. Yuza $9^2 = 81$ kvadrat santimetr. To‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA ($36$) — perimetrning o‘zi. C ($324$) — perimetr 4 ga emas, 2 ga bo‘lingan: tomon 18 va $18^2 = 324$. D ($1{,}296$) — perimetr kvadratga ko‘tarilgan, $36^2$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A metal plate is made from a rectangle that is 14 centimeters long and 8 centimeters wide. A semicircle is cut out of the plate; the diameter of the semicircle is one entire 8-centimeter side of the rectangle, and the semicircle lies inside the rectangle. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the remaining plate?\",\"option_a\":\"$112 - 32\\\\pi$\",\"option_b\":\"$112 - 16\\\\pi$\",\"option_c\":\"$112 - 8\\\\pi$\",\"option_d\":\"$112 + 8\\\\pi$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The rectangle has area $14 \\\\cdot 8 = 112$. The semicircle has diameter 8, so its radius is 4 and its area is $\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\pi(4)^2 = 8\\\\pi$. (It fits inside the rectangle because its radius, 4, is less than the length, 14.) The remaining area is $112 - 8\\\\pi$ square centimeters. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($112 - 32\\\\pi$) uses 8 as the radius of the semicircle. Choice B ($112 - 16\\\\pi$) subtracts a full circle of radius 4 instead of half of one. Choice D ($112 + 8\\\\pi$) adds the semicircle instead of removing it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"To‘g‘ri to‘rtburchak yuzasi $14 \\\\cdot 8 = 112$. Yarim doiraning diametri 8, demak radiusi 4 va yuzasi $\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\pi(4)^2 = 8\\\\pi$. (U to‘rtburchak ichiga sig‘adi, chunki radius 4 uzunlik 14 dan kichik.) Qolgan yuza $112 - 8\\\\pi$ kvadrat santimetr. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($112 - 32\\\\pi$) — 8 radius deb olingan. B ($112 - 16\\\\pi$) — yarim doira o‘rniga radiusi 4 bo‘lgan butun doira ayirilgan. D ($112 + 8\\\\pi$) — yarim doira ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A right circular cone has a volume of $96\\\\pi$ cubic inches and a base radius of 6 inches. What is the height, in inches, of the cone?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"8\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The volume of a cone is $V = \\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi r^2 h$. Substituting gives $96\\\\pi = \\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi(6)^2 h = 12\\\\pi h$, so $h = \\\\frac{96}{12} = 8$ inches.\\n\\nIf you got $\\\\frac{8}{3}$, you used the cylinder formula $\\\\pi r^2 h$ and forgot the factor $\\\\frac{1}{3}$. If you got 2, you used the diameter, 12, in place of the radius.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Konus hajmi $V = \\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi r^2 h$. Qiymatlarni qo‘yamiz: $96\\\\pi = \\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\pi(6)^2 h = 12\\\\pi h$, demak $h = \\\\frac{96}{12} = 8$ dyuym.\\n\\nAgar $\\\\frac{8}{3}$ chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz silindr formulasini $\\\\pi r^2 h$ ishlatgansiz va $\\\\frac{1}{3}$ ko‘paytuvchini unutgansiz. Agar 2 chiqqan bo‘lsa, radius o‘rniga diametr (12) olingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A gift box is shaped like a rectangular prism with a square base and a height of 10 inches. The volume of the box is 360 cubic inches. The four side faces of the box (not the top or the bottom) will be covered with paper. What is the total area, in square inches, of the four side faces?\",\"option_a\":\"$240$\",\"option_b\":\"$276$\",\"option_c\":\"$312$\",\"option_d\":\"$360$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $s$ be the side length of the square base. Then $s^2 \\\\cdot 10 = 360$, so $s^2 = 36$ and $s = 6$ inches. Each side face is a 6-by-10 rectangle with area 60, so the four side faces have a total area of $4 \\\\cdot 60 = 240$ square inches. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B ($276$) adds one square base, $240 + 36$. Choice C ($312$) is the total surface area including both the top and the bottom. Choice D ($360$) is the volume, not an area.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kvadrat asos tomonini $s$ deb olamiz. U holda $s^2 \\\\cdot 10 = 360$, demak $s^2 = 36$ va $s = 6$ dyuym. Har bir yon yog‘ 6 ga 10 o‘lchamli to‘g‘ri to‘rtburchak, yuzasi 60. To‘rtta yon yog‘ning umumiy yuzasi $4 \\\\cdot 60 = 240$ kvadrat dyuym. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB ($276$) — bitta kvadrat asos qo‘shilgan, $240 + 36$. C ($312$) — ust va pastki asoslar bilan birga to‘liq sirt yuzasi. D ($360$) — bu hajm, yuza emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Cylinder $A$ and cylinder $B$ are similar right circular cylinders. The ratio of the total surface area of cylinder $A$ to the total surface area of cylinder $B$ is $9 : 25$. The volume of cylinder $A$ is $54\\\\pi$ cubic centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of cylinder $B$?\",\"option_a\":\"$90\\\\pi$\",\"option_b\":\"$150\\\\pi$\",\"option_c\":\"$250\\\\pi$\",\"option_d\":\"$750\\\\pi$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"For similar solids, areas scale by the square of the length ratio and volumes by the cube. Since $\\\\frac{9}{25} = \\\\left(\\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\right)^2$, the length ratio of $A$ to $B$ is $3 : 5$, so the volume ratio is $3^3 : 5^3 = 27 : 125$. Therefore the volume of $B$ is $54\\\\pi \\\\cdot \\\\frac{125}{27} = 250\\\\pi$ cubic centimeters. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($90\\\\pi$) multiplies by the length ratio $\\\\frac{5}{3}$ instead of its cube. Choice B ($150\\\\pi$) multiplies by the area ratio $\\\\frac{25}{9}$. Choice D ($750\\\\pi$) multiplies by $\\\\frac{125}{9}$, mixing the cube of 5 with the square of 3.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"O‘xshash jismlarda yuzalar uzunliklar nisbatining kvadrati bo‘yicha, hajmlar esa kubi bo‘yicha o‘zgaradi. $\\\\frac{9}{25} = \\\\left(\\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\right)^2$ bo‘lgani uchun $A$ va $B$ uzunliklari nisbati $3 : 5$, hajmlar nisbati esa $3^3 : 5^3 = 27 : 125$. Demak $B$ ning hajmi $54\\\\pi \\\\cdot \\\\frac{125}{27} = 250\\\\pi$ kub santimetr. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($90\\\\pi$) — uzunliklar nisbati $\\\\frac{5}{3}$ ga ko‘paytirilgan, uning kubiga emas. B ($150\\\\pi$) — yuzalar nisbati $\\\\frac{25}{9}$ ga ko‘paytirilgan. D ($750\\\\pi$) — $\\\\frac{125}{9}$ ga ko‘paytirilgan, ya’ni 5 ning kubi va 3 ning kvadrati aralashtirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"area_volume\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A rectangular tank has an inside base that is 48 centimeters long and 24 centimeters wide, and an inside height of 40 centimeters. The tank contains water to a depth of 20 centimeters. A solid metal cube with an edge length of 12 centimeters is placed in the tank and sinks to the bottom, where it is completely under water. No water spills out. By how many centimeters does the water level rise?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"1.5\",\"3/2\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The cube pushes aside a volume of water equal to its own volume, $12^3 = 1{,}728$ cubic centimeters. That extra volume spreads over the base of the tank, which has area $48 \\\\cdot 24 = 1{,}152$ square centimeters. The rise $h$ satisfies $1{,}152h = 1{,}728$, so $h = 1.5$ centimeters. The new depth, 21.5 centimeters, is more than 12, so the cube is indeed fully under water, and it is less than 40, so nothing spills. Enter 1.5 or 3/2.\\n\\nIf you got 21.5, you gave the new depth instead of the rise. If you got 0.125 (that is, $\\\\frac{144}{1{,}152}$), you used the area of one face of the cube, $12^2$, in place of its volume.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kub o‘z hajmiga teng hajmdagi suvni siqib chiqaradi: $12^3 = 1{,}728$ kub santimetr. Bu qo‘shimcha hajm idish asosi bo‘ylab tarqaladi, asos yuzasi $48 \\\\cdot 24 = 1{,}152$ kvadrat santimetr. Ko‘tarilish $h$ uchun $1{,}152h = 1{,}728$, demak $h = 1.5$ santimetr. Yangi chuqurlik 21.5 santimetr 12 dan katta, ya’ni kub haqiqatan to‘liq suv ostida, va 40 dan kichik, ya’ni suv to‘kilmaydi. 1.5 yoki 3/2 kiriting.\\n\\nAgar 21.5 chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz ko‘tarilish o‘rniga yangi chuqurlikni yozgansiz. Agar 0.125 (ya’ni $\\\\frac{144}{1{,}152}$) chiqqan bo‘lsa, kub hajmi o‘rniga uning bitta yog‘i yuzasi $12^2$ olingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"A honeybee that has found a rich patch of flowers returns to its hive and performs a so-called waggle ______ angle of the dance tells the other bees which direction to fly.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"dance, the\",\"option_b\":\"dance the\",\"option_c\":\"dance, then the\",\"option_d\":\"dance. The\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"“A honeybee … performs a so-called waggle dance” and “The angle of the dance tells the other bees which direction to fly” are both independent clauses. Choice D correctly separates them into two sentences with a period.\\n\\nChoice A joins the two independent clauses with only a comma, creating a comma splice. Choice B joins them with no punctuation at all, creating a run-on sentence. Choice C is also a comma splice: “then” is an adverb, not a conjunction, so “then the angle of the dance tells…” is still an independent clause joined to the first with only a comma.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“A honeybee … performs a so-called waggle dance” va “The angle of the dance tells the other bees which direction to fly” — ikkalasi ham mustaqil gap. D ularni nuqta yordamida ikki alohida gapga to‘g‘ri ajratadi.\\n\\nA — ikki mustaqil gapni faqat vergul bilan bog‘laydi, bu “comma splice” xatosi. B — ularni hech qanday tinish belgisiz qo‘shib yuboradi, bu “run-on” gap. C — bu ham “comma splice”: “then” bog‘lovchi emas, ravish, shuning uchun “then the angle of the dance tells…” baribir mustaqil gap va birinchi gapga faqat vergul bilan ulangan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"When the first heavy snow of the season falls on the Chimgan ______ ski instructors begin grooming the slopes and repairing the lifts for winter visitors.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"mountains;\",\"option_b\":\"mountains,\",\"option_c\":\"mountains:\",\"option_d\":\"mountains—\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sentence begins with a dependent clause, “When the first heavy snow of the season falls on the Chimgan mountains,” followed by the main clause, “ski instructors begin….” A comma is the standard way to separate an introductory dependent clause from the main clause, so choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A's semicolon should join two independent clauses, but the “When” clause cannot stand alone. Choice C's colon must follow an independent clause, and the “When” clause is not one. Choice D's single dash is not used to separate an introductory clause from the main clause.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gap tobe gap bilan boshlanadi: “When the first heavy snow of the season falls on the Chimgan mountains”, so‘ngra bosh gap keladi: “ski instructors begin….” Kirish tobe gapni bosh gapdan ajratishning standart usuli — vergul, shuning uchun B to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nA — nuqtali vergul ikki mustaqil gapni bog‘lashi kerak, ammo “When” bilan boshlangan qism mustaqil gap emas. C — ikki nuqta mustaqil gapdan keyin kelishi kerak, “When” qismi esa mustaqil emas. D — bitta tire kirish qismini bosh gapdan ajratish uchun ishlatilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"This year, the regional science fair will award prizes in three ______ biology, engineering, and computer science. Winners in each category will receive a scholarship for a summer research program.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"categories:\",\"option_b\":\"categories;\",\"option_c\":\"categories\",\"option_d\":\"categories, and\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The clause “the regional science fair will award prizes in three categories” is complete, and the list that follows names those categories. A colon correctly introduces a list that explains what comes before it, so choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B's semicolon must join two independent clauses, but “biology, engineering, and computer science” is not a clause. Choice C runs the list straight into “categories” with no punctuation, which is confusing and nonstandard. Choice D's “and” makes the list read as something added to the categories rather than as the names of the categories.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“The regional science fair will award prizes in three categories” — to‘liq gap, undan keyingi ro‘yxat esa o‘sha yo‘nalishlarni nomlaydi. Ikki nuqta oldingi qismni tushuntiruvchi ro‘yxatni to‘g‘ri kiritadi, shuning uchun A to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nB — nuqtali vergul ikki mustaqil gapni bog‘lashi kerak, ammo “biology, engineering, and computer science” gap emas. C — ro‘yxat “categories” so‘ziga tinish belgisiz qo‘shilib ketadi, bu chalkash va nostandart. D — “and” ro‘yxatni yo‘nalishlarning nomi emas, balki ularga qo‘shimcha narsa sifatida ko‘rsatadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"On their journey, the merchants passed through three historic trading cities: Merv, in present-day ______ Herat, in Afghanistan; and Samarkand, in Uzbekistan.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"Turkmenistan,\",\"option_b\":\"Turkmenistan:\",\"option_c\":\"Turkmenistan;\",\"option_d\":\"Turkmenistan\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Each item in this list contains its own comma (“Merv, in present-day Turkmenistan”). When list items already contain commas, semicolons are used to separate the items, as the text does before “and Samarkand.” Choice C supplies the matching semicolon after the first item.\\n\\nChoice A uses a comma, which would make it unclear where one item ends and the next begins and would be inconsistent with the semicolon later in the list. Choice B's colon would wrongly introduce “Herat” as an explanation of Turkmenistan. Choice D leaves no punctuation between the first and second items.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bu ro‘yxatdagi har bir element o‘z ichida vergulga ega (“Merv, in present-day Turkmenistan”). Ro‘yxat elementlarida vergul bo‘lsa, elementlar nuqtali vergul bilan ajratiladi — matnda “and Samarkand” oldidan ham shunday qilingan. C birinchi elementdan keyin mos nuqtali vergulni qo‘yadi.\\n\\nA — vergul bitta element qayerda tugab, keyingisi qayerda boshlanishini noaniq qiladi va ro‘yxatdagi keyingi nuqtali vergulga mos kelmaydi. B — ikki nuqta “Herat”ni Turkmanistonning izohi sifatida noto‘g‘ri kiritadi. D — birinchi va ikkinchi element orasida hech qanday tinish belgisi qoldirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Marine biologist and underwater ______ has spent the past decade tracking humpback whales as they migrate along the eastern coast of Madagascar.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"photographer Ines Rakoto\",\"option_b\":\"photographer, Ines Rakoto,\",\"option_c\":\"photographer, Ines Rakoto\",\"option_d\":\"photographer Ines Rakoto,\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"“Marine biologist and underwater photographer” is a title placed directly before the name “Ines Rakoto,” with no article such as “the.” Such a title is essential to identifying the subject and should not be separated from the name by commas. The full subject “Marine biologist and underwater photographer Ines Rakoto” then leads directly to the verb “has spent,” so choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B sets the name off with commas, which would leave the title without an article and break the subject apart. Choice C places a comma between the title and the name. Choice D places a comma between the subject and its verb, “has spent.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“Marine biologist and underwater photographer” — “the” kabi artiklsiz, to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri “Ines Rakoto” ismidan oldin kelgan unvon. Bunday unvon egani aniqlash uchun zarur va ismdan vergul bilan ajratilmaydi. Butun ega “Marine biologist and underwater photographer Ines Rakoto” to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri “has spent” kesimiga o‘tadi, shuning uchun A to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nB — ismni vergullar bilan ajratadi, natijada unvon artiklsiz qolib, ega bo‘linib ketadi. C — unvon va ism orasiga vergul qo‘yadi. D — ega va uning kesimi “has spent” orasiga vergul qo‘yadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The saiga, an antelope whose large, drooping nose filters out dust in summer and warms frigid air in ______ roams the dry grasslands of Kazakhstan, Mongolia, and southern Russia.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"winter;\",\"option_b\":\"winter—\",\"option_c\":\"winter:\",\"option_d\":\"winter,\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The phrase “an antelope whose large, drooping nose … in winter” is a nonessential appositive describing “The saiga.” It begins with a comma after “saiga,” so it must end with a matching comma before the verb “roams.” Choice D provides that comma.\\n\\nChoice A's semicolon would separate the subject “The saiga” from its verb “roams.” Choice B closes the appositive with a dash, but an element that opens with a comma must close with a comma. Choice C's colon would also wrongly separate the subject from its verb.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“An antelope whose large, drooping nose … in winter” iborasi “The saiga”ni tasvirlovchi qo‘shimcha (nonessential) izoh. U “saiga” dan keyingi vergul bilan boshlangan, demak “roams” kesimidan oldin xuddi shunday vergul bilan yopilishi kerak. D aynan shu vergulni beradi.\\n\\nA — nuqtali vergul “The saiga” egasini “roams” kesimidan ajratib qo‘yadi. B — izohni tire bilan yopadi, ammo vergul bilan boshlangan izoh vergul bilan yopilishi shart. C — ikki nuqta ham egani kesimdan noto‘g‘ri ajratadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The council's decision to turn the abandoned cotton mill on the edge of town into a public library, a café, and a set of artists' ______ surprised residents who had assumed the building would be torn down.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"studios,\",\"option_b\":\"studios;\",\"option_c\":\"studios\",\"option_d\":\"studios—\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The subject of this sentence is the long noun phrase “The council's decision to turn the abandoned cotton mill … into a public library, a café, and a set of artists' studios,” and its verb is “surprised.” No punctuation should separate a subject from its verb, so choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A is tempting because the list inside the subject contains commas, but a comma after “studios” would separate the subject from “surprised.” Choice B's semicolon would also split the subject from its verb, leaving two fragments. Choice D's dash would do the same, and there is no opening dash for it to pair with.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bu gapning egasi uzun ot birikmasi: “The council's decision to turn the abandoned cotton mill … into a public library, a café, and a set of artists' studios”, kesimi esa “surprised”. Ega va kesim orasida hech qanday tinish belgisi bo‘lmasligi kerak, shuning uchun C to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nA — jozibali, chunki ega ichidagi ro‘yxatda vergullar bor, ammo “studios” dan keyingi vergul egani “surprised” dan ajratib qo‘yadi. B — nuqtali vergul ham egani kesimdan ajratadi va ikki to‘liqsiz gap hosil qiladi. D — tire ham xuddi shunday qiladi, buning ustiga u juftlanadigan ochuvchi tire yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"boundaries\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The first field trials of the new drought-resistant wheat were disappointing, producing yields no better than those of the standard variety. The second round of trials, ______ produced yields nearly 20 percent higher, largely because the seeds were planted earlier in the spring.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"however;\",\"option_b\":\"however,\",\"option_c\":\"however\",\"option_d\":\"however:\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"“However” is inserted in the middle of the clause “The second round of trials … produced yields nearly 20 percent higher.” Because it interrupts the clause between the subject and verb, it must be set off by a pair of commas. The text supplies the first comma after “trials,” so choice B supplies the second.\\n\\nChoice A's semicolon would separate the subject “The second round of trials” from its verb “produced,” leaving two fragments. Choice C omits the closing comma, so the interrupting word is not properly set off. Choice D's colon would also wrongly separate the subject from its verb.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“However” so‘zi “The second round of trials … produced yields nearly 20 percent higher” gapining o‘rtasiga — ega va kesim orasiga qo‘yilgan. Gapni bo‘lib turgan bunday so‘z ikki tomondan vergul bilan ajratilishi kerak. Matnda birinchi vergul “trials” dan keyin bor, B esa ikkinchisini qo‘yadi.\\n\\nA — nuqtali vergul “The second round of trials” egasini “produced” kesimidan ajratib, ikki to‘liqsiz gap hosil qiladi. C — yopuvchi vergulni tushirib qoldiradi, natijada gapni bo‘luvchi so‘z to‘g‘ri ajratilmaydi. D — ikki nuqta ham egani kesimdan noto‘g‘ri ajratadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In 2018, the public library in the mountain town of Sarvon began lending seeds as well as books. In spring, gardeners borrow packets of local bean, squash and pepper seeds; in the fall, they return seeds saved from the plants they grew. Librarian Nodira Qosimova says the program has done more than supply gardens: vegetable varieties that only a few elderly farmers still grew are now planted in dozens of yards across town.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"The Sarvon library stopped lending books in order to make room for its seed collection.\",\"option_b\":\"The Sarvon library's seed-lending program supplies gardeners and has helped spread local vegetable varieties that were becoming rare.\",\"option_c\":\"Most gardeners in Sarvon do not return seeds to the library after borrowing them.\",\"option_d\":\"Elderly farmers in Sarvon have refused to share their seeds with the library.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text explains how the library's seed program works and then reports Qosimova's point that the program has done \\\"more than supply gardens\\\": rare local varieties are now grown in dozens of yards. Choice B combines both parts.\\n\\nChoice A is wrong because the library lends seeds \\\"as well as books\\\"; it did not stop lending books. Choice C is unsupported: the text says gardeners return saved seeds and never suggests that most fail to. Choice D is unsupported: the text says nothing about farmers refusing to share seeds.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda kutubxonaning urug‘ berish dasturi qanday ishlashi tushuntiriladi, so‘ng Qosimovaning fikri keltiriladi: dastur faqat bog‘larni urug‘ bilan ta’minlash bilan cheklanmagan — kamyob bo‘lib qolgan mahalliy navlar endi o‘nlab hovlilarda ekilmoqda. B javob ikkala qismni ham birlashtiradi.\\n\\nA noto‘g‘ri: kutubxona urug‘larni kitoblar bilan bir qatorda (“as well as books”) beradi, kitob berishni to‘xtatmagan. C asossiz: matnda bog‘bonlar yig‘ib olgan urug‘larni qaytarishi aytiladi, ko‘pchilik qaytarmasligi haqida gap yo‘q. D asossiz: fermerlar urug‘ berishdan bosh tortgani haqida hech narsa aytilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In the coastal deserts of southwestern Africa, rain almost never falls, but fog rolls in from the ocean on many mornings. Some darkling beetles survive there by \\\"fog basking.\\\" A beetle climbs to the top of a sand dune, faces into the wind and tilts its body forward. Tiny droplets of fog collect on its back, merge into larger drops and roll down toward its mouth.\",\"stem\":\"According to the text, how do some darkling beetles obtain water?\",\"option_a\":\"By digging down to moist sand beneath the dunes\",\"option_b\":\"By drinking rainwater that collects at the bottoms of dunes\",\"option_c\":\"By eating plants that store water from the ocean\",\"option_d\":\"By positioning their bodies so that fog droplets collect and roll toward their mouths\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text describes \\\"fog basking\\\": a beetle faces into the wind and tilts forward so that fog droplets collect on its back and roll down toward its mouth. Choice D restates this process.\\n\\nChoice A is never mentioned; the beetles climb to the top of dunes, not dig beneath them. Choice B contradicts the text, which says that rain \\\"almost never falls\\\" there. Choice C is never mentioned: the text says nothing about the beetles eating plants.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda “fog basking” jarayoni tasvirlanadi: qo‘ng‘iz shamolga qarab turadi va oldinga egiladi, natijada tuman tomchilari uning orqasida yig‘ilib, og‘ziga qarab oqib tushadi. D javob aynan shu jarayonni ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA haqida matnda gap yo‘q: qo‘ng‘izlar qumtepalar ostini qazimaydi, aksincha, cho‘qqisiga chiqadi. B matnga zid: u yerda yomg‘ir deyarli yog‘maydi (“almost never falls”). C ham tilga olinmagan: matnda qo‘ng‘izlar o‘simlik yeyishi haqida hech narsa aytilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is adapted from a short story.\\n\\nFor weeks Dilnoza had practiced the speech she would give at her school's graduation, reciting it to the mirror, to the cat, to the kettle as it boiled. But when she stepped onto the stage and saw the rows of faces, every word she had memorized vanished. She found her mother in the third row, took a breath and began to talk simply about what the school had meant to her. Afterward, several teachers told her it was the best graduation speech they had heard in years.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Although Dilnoza forgets her prepared speech, she succeeds by speaking simply and sincerely.\",\"option_b\":\"Dilnoza decides that practicing a speech in advance is a waste of time.\",\"option_c\":\"Dilnoza's mother helps her remember the words of her prepared speech.\",\"option_d\":\"The teachers are surprised that Dilnoza was chosen to speak at graduation.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Dilnoza practices for weeks, forgets every memorized word on stage, then speaks simply about what the school meant to her, and teachers call it the best speech in years. Choice A captures this turn from a problem to an unexpected success.\\n\\nChoice B goes beyond the text, which never shows Dilnoza drawing any conclusion about practice. Choice C is unsupported: she looks at her mother, but nothing suggests her mother helps her recall the prepared words; in fact, she gives a different speech. Choice D is unsupported: the teachers praise the speech, and nothing suggests surprise that she was chosen.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Dilnoza bir necha hafta mashq qiladi, sahnada yodlagan hamma so‘zlarini unutib qo‘yadi, so‘ng maktab u uchun nimani anglatgani haqida oddiygina gapiradi va o‘qituvchilar buni yillar davomidagi eng yaxshi nutq deb aytadi. A javob muammodan kutilmagan muvaffaqiyatga o‘tishni ifodalaydi.\\n\\nB matn doirasidan chiqadi: Dilnoza mashq qilish haqida biror xulosa chiqargani ko‘rsatilmagan. C asossiz: u onasiga qaraydi, lekin onasi unga tayyorlangan so‘zlarni eslatgani aytilmagan; aslida u boshqacha nutq so‘zlaydi. D asossiz: o‘qituvchilar nutqni maqtaydi, uning tanlanganidan hayron bo‘lgani haqida gap yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Biologists have long known that birds living in noisy cities often sing at higher pitches than members of the same species living in quiet forests, likely because higher notes are easier to hear over the low rumble of traffic. Ecologist Farid Aliyev wanted to know whether this difference is learned or inherited. He raised chicks from city and forest populations of the same species in identical quiet aviaries. As adults, birds from both populations sang at nearly the same pitch.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Birds in quiet forests sing at higher pitches than city birds because forests contain more obstacles to sound.\",\"option_b\":\"Aliyev found that city birds are born with a tendency to sing at higher pitches than forest birds.\",\"option_c\":\"Aliyev's study suggests that city birds' higher-pitched songs are a response to their noisy surroundings rather than an inherited trait.\",\"option_d\":\"Traffic noise has caused some bird species to disappear from cities entirely.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Aliyev raised city and forest chicks in the same quiet conditions, and as adults they sang at nearly the same pitch. If the higher pitch were inherited, the city-born birds should still have sung higher; because they did not, the difference appears to come from the noisy environment. Choice C states this main finding.\\n\\nChoice A reverses the pattern in the text, in which city birds sing higher. Choice B is the opposite of what the study suggests, since city-born birds raised in quiet did not sing higher. Choice D is never discussed in the text.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Aliyev shahar va o‘rmon qushlarining jo‘jalarini bir xil sokin sharoitda boqqan, ular katta bo‘lgach deyarli bir xil balandlikda sayragan. Agar baland ovoz irsiy bo‘lganida, shahar qushlarining avlodi baribir balandroq sayrashi kerak edi; bunday bo‘lmagani farq shovqinli muhit ta’sirida paydo bo‘lishini ko‘rsatadi. C javob shu asosiy natijani ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA matndagi holatni teskari qiladi: matnga ko‘ra balandroq sayraydiganlar — shahar qushlari. B tadqiqot ko‘rsatgan narsaning aksi, chunki sokin sharoitda o‘sgan shahar qushlari balandroq sayramagan. D haqida matnda umuman gap yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Historians have generally assumed that the weaving workshops of nineteenth-century Lorvan were run by men, since the workshops' licenses were issued in men's names. But historian Aru Bekova examined the workshops' daily account books and found that most entries recording purchases of thread, payments to workers and sales to merchants were written and signed by women. Bekova concludes that women often managed the everyday business of the workshops even when men held the licenses.\",\"stem\":\"According to the text, what did Bekova find in the workshops' account books?\",\"option_a\":\"Most of the workshops' licenses had been issued in women's names.\",\"option_b\":\"Most records of the workshops' purchases, payments and sales were written and signed by women.\",\"option_c\":\"Women who worked in the workshops were paid more than men.\",\"option_d\":\"Merchants were unwilling to buy cloth from workshops managed by women.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text states that in the account books, \\\"most entries recording purchases of thread, payments to workers and sales to merchants were written and signed by women.\\\" Choice B restates this finding.\\n\\nChoice A contradicts the text, which says the licenses were issued in men's names. Choice C confuses who wrote the payment records with how much workers were paid; the text compares no wages. Choice D is unsupported: the books record sales to merchants, and nothing suggests merchants refused to buy.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda hisob daftarlarida ip xaridi, ishchilarga to‘lov va savdogarlarga sotuv haqidagi yozuvlarning ko‘pchiligi ayollar tomonidan yozilgani va imzolangani aytiladi. B javob aynan shu topilmani takrorlaydi.\\n\\nA matnga zid: litsenziyalar erkaklar nomiga berilgan. C to‘lov yozuvlarini kim yozganini ishchilarga qancha haq to‘langani bilan adashtiradi; matnda maoshlar solishtirilmaydi. D asossiz: daftarlarda savdogarlarga sotuvlar qayd etilgan, ular sotib olishdan bosh tortgani haqida gap yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is from a poem. The speaker is describing the first snowfall of the year in a city.\\n\\nAll night the snow came down without a sound\\nand filled the potholes, softened every curb,\\nlaid equal white on mansion roof and shed,\\non the mayor's car and on the junk dealer's cart.\\nBy morning no one could have told the rich street\\nfrom the poor one; the whole city lay\\nunder a single blanket, as if, for one day,\\nit had agreed to be one place.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"The speaker resents the snow for making travel through the city difficult.\",\"option_b\":\"The city's wealthy residents clear the snow from their streets before poorer residents can.\",\"option_c\":\"The snowfall reveals how much the city has changed over the years.\",\"option_d\":\"The snowfall briefly hides the differences between parts of the city, making the city seem unified.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The speaker notes that the snow fell \\\"equal\\\" on mansion and shed, on the mayor's car and the junk dealer's cart, so that by morning \\\"no one could have told the rich street / from the poor one.\\\" The poem ends with the city seeming, \\\"for one day,\\\" to be \\\"one place.\\\" Choice D states this central idea.\\n\\nChoice A is unsupported: the speaker never complains about travel or expresses resentment. Choice B contradicts the poem, which stresses that the snow treated all streets alike. Choice C is unsupported: the poem describes a single night and morning, not changes over the years.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Shoir qor saroy tomiga ham, shiyponga ham, hokimning mashinasiga ham, eskifurushning aravasiga ham “teng” yoqqanini, ertalab esa boy ko‘chani kambag‘al ko‘chadan ajratib bo‘lmay qolganini aytadi. She’r shahar “bir kunga” go‘yo “bitta joy” bo‘lishga rozi bo‘lgandek tuyulishi bilan tugaydi. D javob shu markaziy g‘oyani ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA asossiz: shoir yo‘l qiyinchiligidan shikoyat qilmaydi va norozilik bildirmaydi. B she’rga zid: unda qor barcha ko‘chalarga bir xil yoqqani ta’kidlanadi. C asossiz: she’rda yillar davomidagi o‘zgarishlar emas, bir kecha va bir tong tasvirlanadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"For decades, governments measured the success of programs that pay farmers to plant trees by counting how many saplings were planted. Economist Rustam Haydarov argues that this measure can be misleading. In the region he studied, more than a million saplings were planted under such programs between 2005 and 2010, yet satellite images show that total tree cover barely changed. Many farmers, he found, had cut down older trees elsewhere on their land to make room for the new plantings, which were the only trees for which they received payment.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Counting saplings can overstate how much tree-planting programs increase tree cover, since farmers may remove existing trees to make room for paid plantings.\",\"option_b\":\"Tree-planting programs fail mainly because most saplings die before they grow large enough to appear in satellite images.\",\"option_c\":\"Farmers in Haydarov's region planted far fewer saplings than the programs reported.\",\"option_d\":\"Satellite images are a less reliable way to measure tree cover than counts of saplings planted.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Haydarov argues that sapling counts can mislead: over a million saplings were planted, but total tree cover barely changed because farmers cut older trees to make room for the paid plantings. Choice A states both the claim and the reason he gives for it.\\n\\nChoice B offers a plausible explanation that the text never gives; Haydarov attributes the lack of change to farmers removing older trees, not to saplings dying. Choice C is unsupported: the text never questions the number of saplings planted. Choice D reverses Haydarov's reasoning, which relies on satellite images to show that sapling counts are misleading.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Haydarovning fikricha, ko‘chatlar sonini sanash chalg‘itishi mumkin: milliondan ortiq ko‘chat ekilgan, lekin umumiy daraxt qoplami deyarli o‘zgarmagan, chunki fermerlar haq to‘lanadigan yangi ko‘chatlarga joy ochish uchun eski daraxtlarni kesgan. A javob ham da’voni, ham uning sababini ifodalaydi.\\n\\nB ishonarli tuyulsa-da, matnda keltirilmagan izoh beradi: Haydarov o‘zgarish yo‘qligini ko‘chatlar qurib qolgani bilan emas, fermerlar eski daraxtlarni kesgani bilan izohlaydi. C asossiz: matnda ekilgan ko‘chatlar soni shubha ostiga olinmaydi. D Haydarovning mulohazasini teskari qiladi: u aynan sun’iy yo‘ldosh suratlariga tayanib, ko‘chatlar sonini sanash chalg‘itishini ko‘rsatadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"central_ideas_details\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is adapted from a novel. Teodor, a retired watchmaker, is visiting the shop he once owned.\\n\\nThe new owner had replaced the dark wooden counters with glass and steel, and the clocks that once ticked from every wall were gone; a single screen now listed the prices of repairs. Teodor had expected to feel wounded. Instead, watching a young woman bend over a customer's watch with the same narrowed eyes and steady fingers he had once had, he found himself smiling. The room was a stranger to him, but the work, he saw, was the same.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Teodor regrets selling his shop and wishes he could buy it back.\",\"option_b\":\"Teodor disapproves of the changes to his old shop but hides his feelings from the new owner.\",\"option_c\":\"Although the shop looks very different, Teodor is reassured to see that the craft he practiced continues there.\",\"option_d\":\"Teodor realizes that modern watch repair requires skills he never learned.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Teodor notices how much the shop's appearance has changed and expects to be hurt, but seeing a young woman repair a watch with the same care he once showed makes him smile: \\\"the work, he saw, was the same.\\\" Choice C captures this contrast between the changed room and the continuing craft.\\n\\nChoice A is unsupported: Teodor expresses no regret about selling. Choice B misreads the passage; he expected to feel wounded, but \\\"instead\\\" he smiles, and nothing suggests he is hiding disapproval. Choice D contradicts the final sentence, which stresses that the work has not changed.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Teodor do‘kon ko‘rinishi qanchalik o‘zgarganini ko‘radi va ranjishini kutadi, ammo yosh ayol soatni xuddi o‘zi kabi diqqat bilan ta’mirlayotganini ko‘rib jilmayadi: ish esa o‘sha-o‘sha ekan (“the work, he saw, was the same”). C javob o‘zgargan xona va davom etayotgan hunar o‘rtasidagi shu qarama-qarshilikni ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA asossiz: Teodor do‘konni sotganidan afsuslanmaydi. B parchani noto‘g‘ri talqin qiladi: u ranjishni kutgan edi, lekin buning o‘rniga (“instead”) jilmayadi; noroziligini yashirayotgani haqida hech qanday ishora yo‘q. D oxirgi jumlaga zid: unda ish o‘zgarmagani ta’kidlanadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A round table top has a diameter of 18 inches. What is the area, in square inches, of the table top?\",\"option_a\":\"$9\\\\pi$\",\"option_b\":\"$18\\\\pi$\",\"option_c\":\"$81\\\\pi$\",\"option_d\":\"$324\\\\pi$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The radius is half the diameter: $r = \\\\frac{18}{2} = 9$ inches. The area is $\\\\pi r^2 = \\\\pi(9)^2 = 81\\\\pi$ square inches. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($9\\\\pi$) is $\\\\pi r$, with the radius not squared. Choice B ($18\\\\pi$) is the circumference, $\\\\pi d$. Choice D ($324\\\\pi$) squares the diameter instead of the radius.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Radius diametrning yarmiga teng: $r = \\\\frac{18}{2} = 9$ dyuym. Doira yuzasi $\\\\pi r^2 = \\\\pi(9)^2 = 81\\\\pi$ kvadrat dyuym. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($9\\\\pi$) — bu $\\\\pi r$, radius kvadratga ko‘tarilmagan. B ($18\\\\pi$) — bu aylana uzunligi, $\\\\pi d$. D ($324\\\\pi$) — radius o‘rniga diametr kvadratga ko‘tarilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, a circle has the equation $(x - 4)^2 + (y + 1)^2 = 36$. What is the diameter of the circle?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The equation has the form $(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2$, so $r^2 = 36$ and the radius is $r = 6$. The diameter is $2r = 12$.\\n\\nIf you entered 6, you gave the radius. If you entered 36 or 72, you treated $r^2$ as the radius.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tenglama $(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2$ ko‘rinishida, demak $r^2 = 36$ va radius $r = 6$. Diametr $2r = 12$.\\n\\nAgar 6 kiritgan bo‘lsangiz, siz radiusni yozgansiz. Agar 36 yoki 72 chiqqan bo‘lsa, $r^2$ radius deb olingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"An angle measures $240^\\\\circ$. What is the measure of the angle in radians?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{4\\\\pi}{3}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{3}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{8\\\\pi}{3}$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Multiply by $\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{180^\\\\circ}$: $240^\\\\circ \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{180^\\\\circ} = \\\\frac{240\\\\pi}{180} = \\\\frac{4\\\\pi}{3}$. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B ($\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{3}$) converts only $60^\\\\circ$, the amount by which $240^\\\\circ$ exceeds $180^\\\\circ$. Choice C ($\\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{3}$) divides by $360^\\\\circ$ instead of $180^\\\\circ$, as if $\\\\pi$ radians were a full turn. Choice D ($\\\\frac{8\\\\pi}{3}$) divides by $90^\\\\circ$ instead of $180^\\\\circ$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{180^\\\\circ}$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $240^\\\\circ \\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{180^\\\\circ} = \\\\frac{240\\\\pi}{180} = \\\\frac{4\\\\pi}{3}$. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB ($\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{3}$) — faqat $60^\\\\circ$ o‘tkazilgan, ya’ni $240^\\\\circ$ ning $180^\\\\circ$ dan ortig‘i. C ($\\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{3}$) — $180^\\\\circ$ o‘rniga $360^\\\\circ$ ga bo‘lingan, go‘yo $\\\\pi$ radian to‘liq aylanishdek. D ($\\\\frac{8\\\\pi}{3}$) — $180^\\\\circ$ o‘rniga $90^\\\\circ$ ga bo‘lingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A circle has a radius of 8 meters. A sector of the circle has a central angle of $135^\\\\circ$. What is the area, in square meters, of the sector?\",\"option_a\":\"$6\\\\pi$\",\"option_b\":\"$24\\\\pi$\",\"option_c\":\"$40\\\\pi$\",\"option_d\":\"$64\\\\pi$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sector is $\\\\frac{135}{360} = \\\\frac{3}{8}$ of the circle. The whole circle has area $\\\\pi(8)^2 = 64\\\\pi$, so the sector has area $\\\\frac{3}{8} \\\\cdot 64\\\\pi = 24\\\\pi$ square meters. Choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($6\\\\pi$) is the arc length of the sector, $\\\\frac{3}{8} \\\\cdot 16\\\\pi$. Choice C ($40\\\\pi$) is the area of the other sector, with central angle $225^\\\\circ$. Choice D ($64\\\\pi$) is the area of the whole circle.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Sektor doiraning $\\\\frac{135}{360} = \\\\frac{3}{8}$ qismini tashkil qiladi. Butun doira yuzasi $\\\\pi(8)^2 = 64\\\\pi$, demak sektor yuzasi $\\\\frac{3}{8} \\\\cdot 64\\\\pi = 24\\\\pi$ kvadrat metr. To‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA ($6\\\\pi$) — sektor yoyining uzunligi, $\\\\frac{3}{8} \\\\cdot 16\\\\pi$. C ($40\\\\pi$) — markaziy burchagi $225^\\\\circ$ bo‘lgan qolgan sektorning yuzasi. D ($64\\\\pi$) — butun doira yuzasi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the points $(-2, 5)$ and $(6, -1)$ are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle. The area of the circle is $k\\\\pi$. What is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"25\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The length of the diameter is $\\\\sqrt{(6 - (-2))^2 + (-1 - 5)^2} = \\\\sqrt{64 + 36} = \\\\sqrt{100} = 10$. So the radius is 5, and the area is $\\\\pi(5)^2 = 25\\\\pi$. Therefore $k = 25$.\\n\\nIf you got 100, you used the diameter as the radius. If you got 10 or 5, you stopped before computing the area.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Diametr uzunligi $\\\\sqrt{(6 - (-2))^2 + (-1 - 5)^2} = \\\\sqrt{64 + 36} = \\\\sqrt{100} = 10$. Demak radius 5, yuza $\\\\pi(5)^2 = 25\\\\pi$. Shuning uchun $k = 25$.\\n\\nAgar 100 chiqqan bo‘lsa, diametr radius deb olingan. Agar 10 yoki 5 chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz yuzani hisoblashdan oldin to‘xtagansiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A circle with center $O$ has a radius of 13 centimeters. Chord $\\\\overline{AB}$ of the circle is 5 centimeters from $O$; that is, the perpendicular segment from $O$ to $\\\\overline{AB}$ has length 5. What is the length, in centimeters, of chord $\\\\overline{AB}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$8$\",\"option_b\":\"$12$\",\"option_c\":\"$24$\",\"option_d\":\"$2\\\\sqrt{194}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $M$ be the point where the perpendicular from $O$ meets $\\\\overline{AB}$. A perpendicular from the center bisects the chord, so $AM = MB$. In right triangle $OMA$, $OA = 13$ is the hypotenuse and $OM = 5$, so $AM = \\\\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = \\\\sqrt{144} = 12$. The chord has length $2 \\\\cdot 12 = 24$ centimeters. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($8$) subtracts the lengths, $13 - 5$. Choice B ($12$) is only half of the chord. Choice D ($2\\\\sqrt{194}$) adds the squares, $13^2 + 5^2$, instead of subtracting them.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$O$ dan tushirilgan perpendikulyar $\\\\overline{AB}$ ni kesgan nuqtani $M$ deb olamiz. Markazdan tushirilgan perpendikulyar vatarni teng ikkiga bo‘ladi, ya’ni $AM = MB$. $OMA$ to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchakda $OA = 13$ gipotenuza va $OM = 5$, demak $AM = \\\\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = \\\\sqrt{144} = 12$. Vatar uzunligi $2 \\\\cdot 12 = 24$ santimetr. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($8$) — uzunliklar ayirilgan, $13 - 5$. B ($12$) — bu vatarning faqat yarmi. D ($2\\\\sqrt{194}$) — kvadratlar ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan, $13^2 + 5^2$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Point $P$ lies outside a circle with center $O$ and radius 6. Two lines through $P$ are tangent to the circle, one at point $A$ and the other at point $B$. The distance from $O$ to $P$ is 10. What is the area of quadrilateral $OAPB$?\",\"option_a\":\"$24$\",\"option_b\":\"$30$\",\"option_c\":\"$40$\",\"option_d\":\"$48$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"A tangent line is perpendicular to the radius at the point of tangency, so angles $OAP$ and $OBP$ are right angles. In right triangle $OAP$, the hypotenuse is $OP = 10$ and $OA = 6$, so $AP = \\\\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8$. The area of triangle $OAP$ is $\\\\frac{1}{2}(6)(8) = 24$. Triangle $OBP$ is congruent to triangle $OAP$, so quadrilateral $OAPB$ has area $2 \\\\cdot 24 = 48$. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($24$) is the area of only one of the two triangles. Choice B ($30$) uses $\\\\frac{1}{2}(6)(10)$, treating $OP$ as a leg. Choice C ($40$) uses $\\\\frac{1}{2}(8)(10)$, again treating the hypotenuse as a leg.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Urinma urinish nuqtasida radiusga perpendikulyar, demak $OAP$ va $OBP$ burchaklar to‘g‘ri burchak. $OAP$ to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchakda gipotenuza $OP = 10$ va $OA = 6$, shuning uchun $AP = \\\\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8$. $OAP$ uchburchak yuzasi $\\\\frac{1}{2}(6)(8) = 24$. $OBP$ uchburchak $OAP$ ga teng, demak $OAPB$ to‘rtburchak yuzasi $2 \\\\cdot 24 = 48$. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA ($24$) — ikki uchburchakdan faqat bittasining yuzasi. B ($30$) — $\\\\frac{1}{2}(6)(10)$, ya’ni $OP$ katet deb olingan. C ($40$) — $\\\\frac{1}{2}(8)(10)$, bunda ham gipotenuza katet deb olingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"circles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of $x^2 + y^2 - 10x - 6y + 9 = 0$ is a circle. The point $(9, k)$ lies on the circle, where $k > 0$. What is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"6\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Complete the square in each variable: $(x^2 - 10x + 25) + (y^2 - 6y + 9) = -9 + 25 + 9$, so $(x - 5)^2 + (y - 3)^2 = 25$. Substituting $x = 9$ gives $16 + (k - 3)^2 = 25$, so $(k - 3)^2 = 9$ and $k - 3 = 3$ or $k - 3 = -3$. Thus $k = 6$ or $k = 0$. Since $k > 0$, $k = 6$.\\n\\nIf you got 0, you chose the other intersection point, which does not satisfy $k > 0$. You can also substitute directly: $81 + k^2 - 90 - 6k + 9 = 0$ gives $k^2 - 6k = 0$, so $k(k - 6) = 0$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir o‘zgaruvchi bo‘yicha to‘la kvadrat ajratamiz: $(x^2 - 10x + 25) + (y^2 - 6y + 9) = -9 + 25 + 9$, demak $(x - 5)^2 + (y - 3)^2 = 25$. $x = 9$ ni qo‘yamiz: $16 + (k - 3)^2 = 25$, ya’ni $(k - 3)^2 = 9$ va $k - 3 = 3$ yoki $k - 3 = -3$. Demak $k = 6$ yoki $k = 0$. $k > 0$ bo‘lgani uchun $k = 6$.\\n\\nAgar 0 chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz $k > 0$ shartini qanoatlantirmaydigan ikkinchi nuqtani tanlagansiz. To‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri qo‘yish ham mumkin: $81 + k^2 - 90 - 6k + 9 = 0$ dan $k^2 - 6k = 0$, ya’ni $k(k - 6) = 0$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Engineering student Kamila Yusupova tested how long four types of rechargeable batteries could keep the same flashlight lit on a single charge. She claims that the lithium-ion battery performed better than every other battery she tested.\\n\\n**Hours of light from one full charge**\\n\\n| Battery type | Hours of light |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| Nickel-cadmium | 6.5 |\\n| Nickel-metal hydride | 9.0 |\\n| Lithium-ion | 14.5 |\\n| Lead-acid | 4.0 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Yusupova's claim?\",\"option_a\":\"The nickel-metal hydride battery kept the flashlight lit for 9.0 hours.\",\"option_b\":\"The lithium-ion battery kept the flashlight lit for 14.5 hours, longer than any of the other three batteries.\",\"option_c\":\"The nickel-cadmium battery kept the flashlight lit longer than the lead-acid battery did.\",\"option_d\":\"The lead-acid battery kept the flashlight lit for only 4.0 hours.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Yusupova claims that the lithium-ion battery outperformed every other battery. The table shows that it lasted 14.5 hours, more than any other battery (the next best was 9.0 hours), so choice B supports the claim.\\n\\nChoice A gives an accurate figure for a different battery and says nothing about the lithium-ion battery. Choice C is accurate but compares two other batteries. Choice D shows that the lead-acid battery performed worst, which does not show that the lithium-ion battery performed best.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Yusupova litiy-ion batareya boshqa barcha batareyalardan yaxshiroq ishlaganini da’vo qiladi. Jadvalga ko‘ra u 14,5 soat ishlagan — bu boshqa har qanday batareyadan ko‘p (keyingi eng yaxshi natija 9,0 soat). Demak, B javob da’voni qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi.\\n\\nA boshqa batareya haqidagi to‘g‘ri raqamni beradi, litiy-ion batareya haqida esa hech narsa demaydi. C ham to‘g‘ri, lekin boshqa ikki batareyani solishtiradi. D qo‘rg‘oshin-kislotali batareya eng yomon natija ko‘rsatganini bildiradi, bu esa litiy-ion batareya eng yaxshi ekanini isbotlamaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"A school in the city of Termez asked 400 students to name their favorite after-school activity. The survey found that sports was the most popular choice, named by ______\\n\\n**Favorite after-school activity**\\n\\n| Activity | Number of students |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| Sports | 186 |\\n| Music | 94 |\\n| Robotics | 71 |\\n| Drama | 49 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"94 students, nearly twice as many as named drama.\",\"option_b\":\"71 students, more than named music.\",\"option_c\":\"186 students, fewer than named music.\",\"option_d\":\"186 students, about twice as many as named music, the next most popular activity.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The table shows that 186 students named sports and 94 named music, the second most popular activity; 186 is about twice 94. Choice D reports these figures accurately.\\n\\nChoice A gives the number for music (94), not sports. Choice B gives the number for robotics, and 71 is not more than the 94 who named music. Choice C gives the correct number for sports but wrongly says it is fewer than the number for music.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Jadvalga ko‘ra 186 nafar o‘quvchi sportni, 94 nafari esa ikkinchi eng ommabop mashg‘ulot — musiqani tanlagan; 186 taxminan 94 ning ikki baravari. D javob bu raqamlarni to‘g‘ri beradi.\\n\\nA sport emas, musiqa uchun raqamni (94) beradi. B robototexnika raqamini beradi, 71 esa musiqani tanlagan 94 nafardan ko‘p emas. C sport uchun to‘g‘ri raqamni beradi, lekin uni musiqadan kam deb noto‘g‘ri aytadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Marine biologist Selin Arslan counted sea turtle nests on Kavak Beach every other year from 2016 to 2024. At the end of 2020, the town dimmed the streetlights along the beach, since bright lights can confuse nesting turtles. Arslan claims that the number of nests increased after the lights were dimmed.\\n\\n**Sea turtle nests on Kavak Beach**\\n\\n| Year | Number of nests |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| 2016 | 41 |\\n| 2018 | 38 |\\n| 2020 | 44 |\\n| 2022 | 79 |\\n| 2024 | 96 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Arslan's claim?\",\"option_a\":\"The beach had 44 nests in 2020 and 96 nests in 2024.\",\"option_b\":\"The beach had 41 nests in 2016 and 38 nests in 2018.\",\"option_c\":\"The beach had fewer nests in 2016 than in 2020.\",\"option_d\":\"The beach had 79 nests in 2022.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Arslan claims that nests increased after the lights were dimmed at the end of 2020. Choice A compares the 2020 count (44, before the change took effect) with the 2024 count (96, after it), showing a large increase.\\n\\nChoice B compares two years before the lights were dimmed, and it shows a decrease. Choice C also compares only years before the lights were dimmed. Choice D gives a single figure from after the change without any earlier figure to compare it with, so it does not show an increase.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Arslan chiroqlar 2020-yil oxirida xiralashtirilgandan keyin uyalar soni ko‘payganini da’vo qiladi. A javob 2020-yilgi (o‘zgarishdan oldingi) 44 ta uyani 2024-yilgi (o‘zgarishdan keyingi) 96 ta uya bilan solishtiradi va katta o‘sishni ko‘rsatadi.\\n\\nB chiroqlar xiralashtirilishidan oldingi ikki yilni solishtiradi va hatto kamayishni ko‘rsatadi. C ham faqat o‘zgarishdan oldingi yillarni solishtiradi. D o‘zgarishdan keyingi bitta raqamni beradi, lekin solishtirish uchun oldingi raqam yo‘q, shuning uchun o‘sishni ko‘rsatmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Agricultural researchers grew tomatoes in test plots using four irrigation methods and recorded how much water each method used and how many kilograms of tomatoes each plot produced. They found that drip irrigation used the least water for each kilogram of tomatoes, but it did not produce the highest yield: ______\\n\\n**Tomato yield and water use by irrigation method**\\n\\n| Irrigation method | Water used per kg of tomatoes (liters) | Yield per plot (kg) |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Flood | 210 | 48 |\\n| Furrow | 160 | 52 |\\n| Sprinkler | 140 | 55 |\\n| Drip | 90 | 51 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"drip irrigation used 90 liters of water per kilogram of tomatoes, compared with 210 liters for flood irrigation.\",\"option_b\":\"drip-irrigated plots yielded 51 kg of tomatoes, more than the 48 kg yielded by flood-irrigated plots.\",\"option_c\":\"drip-irrigated plots yielded 51 kg of tomatoes, less than the 55 kg yielded by sprinkler-irrigated plots.\",\"option_d\":\"sprinkler irrigation used 140 liters of water per kilogram of tomatoes, more than drip irrigation used.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The blank must show that drip irrigation \\\"did not produce the highest yield.\\\" Choice C does this: drip plots yielded 51 kg, less than the 55 kg from sprinkler plots.\\n\\nChoices A and D are accurate, but they describe water use, which supports the first part of the statement rather than the part after the colon. Choice B is accurate, but showing that drip beat flood irrigation does not show that drip failed to produce the highest yield.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bo‘sh joy tomchilatib sug‘orish eng yuqori hosil bermaganini (“did not produce the highest yield”) ko‘rsatishi kerak. C javob aynan shuni qiladi: tomchilatib sug‘orilgan maydonlar 51 kg hosil bergan, bu yomg‘irlatib sug‘orilgan maydonlardagi 55 kg dan kam.\\n\\nA va D to‘g‘ri ma’lumot beradi, lekin ular suv sarfi haqida, ya’ni ikki nuqtadan keyingi qismni emas, gapning birinchi qismini tasdiqlaydi. B ham to‘g‘ri, ammo tomchilatib sug‘orish bostirib sug‘orishdan yaxshiroq ekani uning eng yuqori hosil bermaganini ko‘rsatmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Ecologist Javohir Ergashev recorded how many blossoms grew on each plant and how often bees visited four garden plants. He argues that gardeners who want to help bees should choose native wildflowers over popular ornamental flowers, because in his study the native plants attracted far more bee visits even though they produced fewer blossoms.\\n\\n**Blossoms and bee visits for four garden plants**\\n\\n| Plant | Type | Blossoms per plant | Bee visits per hour |\\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Purple coneflower | Native | 22 | 31 |\\n| Petunia | Ornamental | 40 | 6 |\\n| Wild bergamot | Native | 18 | 27 |\\n| Begonia | Ornamental | 35 | 4 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Ergashev's argument?\",\"option_a\":\"Wild bergamot had fewer blossoms per plant than petunia did (18 versus 40) but received far more bee visits per hour (27 versus 6).\",\"option_b\":\"Petunia had more blossoms per plant than any other plant in the study.\",\"option_c\":\"Purple coneflower had more blossoms per plant than wild bergamot did (22 versus 18).\",\"option_d\":\"Begonia received fewer bee visits per hour than petunia did (4 versus 6).\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Ergashev argues that native plants attracted more bee visits than ornamentals despite producing fewer blossoms. Choice A compares a native plant with an ornamental one on both measures: wild bergamot had fewer blossoms (18 versus 40) but many more visits (27 versus 6).\\n\\nChoice B mentions only blossoms and says nothing about bee visits. Choice C compares two native plants, so it says nothing about natives versus ornamentals. Choice D compares two ornamental plants and likewise leaves out the native plants.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ergashev mahalliy o‘simliklar kamroq gul ochishiga qaramay, manzarali gullarga qaraganda ko‘proq asalari jalb qilganini ta’kidlaydi. A javob mahalliy va manzarali o‘simlikni ikkala ko‘rsatkich bo‘yicha solishtiradi: yovvoyi bergamotda gul kamroq (18 ga qarshi 40), lekin asalari tashriflari ancha ko‘p (27 ga qarshi 6).\\n\\nB faqat gullar sonini aytadi, asalari tashriflari haqida hech narsa demaydi. C ikki mahalliy o‘simlikni solishtiradi, mahalliy va manzarali o‘simliklar farqini ko‘rsatmaydi. D ikki manzarali o‘simlikni solishtiradi va mahalliy o‘simliklarni chetda qoldiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Geographer Nilufar Saidova measured how far four mountain glaciers retreated between 2000 and 2020. She found that larger glaciers tended to retreat less than smaller ones: the Torva Glacier, the largest of the four, retreated ______\\n\\n**Glacier size and retreat, 2000–2020**\\n\\n| Glacier | Area in 2000 (km²) | Retreat, 2000–2020 (meters) |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Torva | 48 | 210 |\\n| Ilsk | 12 | 540 |\\n| Brenn | 20 | 390 |\\n| Kaldo | 7 | 615 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"615 meters, while the Kaldo Glacier, the smallest, retreated 210 meters.\",\"option_b\":\"210 meters, while the Brenn Glacier, the smallest, retreated 390 meters.\",\"option_c\":\"540 meters, more than any other glacier in the study.\",\"option_d\":\"210 meters, while the Kaldo Glacier, the smallest, retreated 615 meters.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The Torva Glacier (48 km²) retreated 210 meters, and the smallest glacier, Kaldo (7 km²), retreated 615 meters. Choice D reports these figures correctly and illustrates the pattern that larger glaciers retreated less.\\n\\nChoice A swaps the two retreat figures. Choice B gives Torva's figure correctly but calls Brenn the smallest glacier, although Kaldo is smaller. Choice C gives Ilsk's figure for Torva, and the largest retreat actually belongs to Kaldo.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Torva muzligi (48 km²) 210 metr chekingan, eng kichik muzlik — Kaldo (7 km²) esa 615 metr chekingan. D javob bu raqamlarni to‘g‘ri beradi va kattaroq muzliklar kamroq chekinganini ko‘rsatadi.\\n\\nA ikki raqamning o‘rnini almashtiradi. B Torva raqamini to‘g‘ri beradi, lekin Brennni eng kichik muzlik deb ataydi, holbuki Kaldo undan kichikroq. C Torva uchun Ilsk raqamini beradi, eng ko‘p chekinish esa aslida Kaldoga tegishli.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Agricultural scientist Malika Nurova tested whether planting marigolds near cabbages reduces damage from cabbage-eating caterpillars. She argues that the marigolds' effect depends on distance: marigolds substantially reduced damage only when they were planted within one meter of the cabbages.\\n\\n**Percentage of cabbage leaves damaged by caterpillars**\\n\\n| Planting arrangement | 2023 | 2024 |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| No marigolds | 42% | 47% |\\n| Marigolds 0.5 m from cabbages | 15% | 18% |\\n| Marigolds 1 m from cabbages | 19% | 21% |\\n| Marigolds 3 m from cabbages | 40% | 44% |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Nurova's argument?\",\"option_a\":\"In both years, plots with marigolds 0.5 m from the cabbages had less damage than plots with marigolds 1 m from the cabbages.\",\"option_b\":\"In both years, plots with marigolds 0.5 m or 1 m from the cabbages had far less damage than plots without marigolds, while plots with marigolds 3 m away had nearly as much damage as plots without marigolds.\",\"option_c\":\"In plots without marigolds, the percentage of damaged leaves rose from 42% in 2023 to 47% in 2024.\",\"option_d\":\"In 2024, plots with marigolds 3 m from the cabbages had less damage (44%) than plots without marigolds (47%).\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Nurova's argument has two parts: marigolds within one meter substantially reduced damage, and marigolds farther away did not. Choice B supports both: damage at 0.5 m and 1 m (15–21%) was far below damage without marigolds (42–47%), while damage at 3 m (40–44%) was nearly the same as without marigolds.\\n\\nChoice A is accurate but compares only two distances within one meter, so it says nothing about whether farther marigolds failed to help. Choice C describes only the plots without marigolds. Choice D is accurate but highlights a small benefit at 3 m, which, if anything, works against the claim that only nearby marigolds helped.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Nurova argumenti ikki qismdan iborat: bir metr ichida ekilgan tagetes (marigold) zararni sezilarli kamaytirgan, uzoqroqdagilar esa kamaytirmagan. B javob ikkalasini ham tasdiqlaydi: 0,5 m va 1 m masofada zarar (15–21%) tagetessiz maydonlardagidan (42–47%) ancha past, 3 m masofada esa (40–44%) tagetessiz maydonlardagiga deyarli teng.\\n\\nA to‘g‘ri, lekin faqat bir metr ichidagi ikki masofani solishtiradi, uzoqroqdagi tageteslar foyda bermaganini ko‘rsatmaydi. C faqat tagetessiz maydonlarni tasvirlaydi. D ham to‘g‘ri, ammo 3 m masofadagi kichik foydani ta’kidlaydi, bu esa faqat yaqin tageteslar foyda bergani haqidagi da’voga, aksincha, zid ishlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_quantitative\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Between 2010 and 2020, enrollment in children's music schools rose in some regions of the country of Valmora. Demographer Ilyos Rashidov found that rising enrollment was not simply the result of a growing number of children: in at least one region, enrollment rose even as the number of school-age children fell. For example, ______\\n\\n**Children and music-school students by region**\\n\\n| Region | Children aged 7–15, 2010 | Children aged 7–15, 2020 | Music-school students, 2010 | Music-school students, 2020 |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| Northern | 84,000 | 79,000 | 2,100 | 3,400 |\\n| Eastern | 61,000 | 70,000 | 1,500 | 2,600 |\\n| Southern | 95,000 | 88,000 | 3,000 | 2,700 |\\n| Western | 52,000 | 58,000 | 1,800 | 1,600 |\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?\",\"option_a\":\"in the Eastern region, music-school enrollment rose from 1,500 to 2,600 while the number of children aged 7–15 rose from 61,000 to 70,000.\",\"option_b\":\"in the Southern region, the number of children aged 7–15 fell from 95,000 to 88,000, and music-school enrollment fell from 3,000 to 2,700.\",\"option_c\":\"in the Northern region, the number of children aged 7–15 fell from 84,000 to 79,000, but music-school enrollment rose from 2,100 to 3,400.\",\"option_d\":\"in the Western region, the number of children aged 7–15 rose from 52,000 to 58,000, but music-school enrollment fell from 1,800 to 1,600.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The example must show a region where the number of children fell while music-school enrollment rose. Only the Northern region fits: children fell from 84,000 to 79,000, and enrollment rose from 2,100 to 3,400. Choice C reports this.\\n\\nChoice A describes a region where both numbers rose, which is consistent with enrollment growing simply because there were more children. Choice B describes a region where both numbers fell. Choice D describes the reverse pattern: children increased while enrollment decreased.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Misol bolalar soni kamaygan, musiqa maktabidagi o‘quvchilar soni esa oshgan hududni ko‘rsatishi kerak. Faqat Shimoliy hudud mos keladi: bolalar 84 000 dan 79 000 gacha kamaygan, o‘quvchilar esa 2 100 dan 3 400 gacha ko‘paygan. C javob aynan shuni beradi.\\n\\nA ikkala ko‘rsatkich ham oshgan hududni tasvirlaydi — bu o‘sish shunchaki bolalar ko‘paygani bilan izohlanishi mumkin. B ikkala ko‘rsatkich ham kamaygan hududni tasvirlaydi. D teskari holatni ko‘rsatadi: bolalar ko‘paygan, o‘quvchilar esa kamaygan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Certain acacia trees on the grasslands of East Africa have swollen, hollow thorns in which colonies of ants live. Ecologist Grace Mwangi hypothesizes that the ants protect the trees from large plant-eating animals, such as giraffes, by swarming over and biting any animal that begins to eat the leaves.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Mwangi's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"The ants living in the acacia thorns feed on a sugary liquid that the trees produce.\",\"option_b\":\"Giraffes spend more time feeding during the dry season than during the rainy season.\",\"option_c\":\"Giraffes ate far fewer leaves from acacia trees with ant colonies than from acacia trees whose ants had been removed.\",\"option_d\":\"Acacia trees with hollow thorns grow in many parts of East Africa.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Mwangi's hypothesis is that the ants protect the trees from plant-eating animals. Choice C compares trees with and without ants and shows that giraffes ate far fewer leaves from trees with ants, which is exactly what the hypothesis predicts.\\n\\nChoice A explains what the ants get from the trees, not whether they protect the trees. Choice B concerns when giraffes feed, not whether ants affect their feeding. Choice D concerns where the trees grow and says nothing about the ants' effect on giraffes.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Mwangi gipotezasiga ko‘ra, chumolilar daraxtlarni o‘txo‘r hayvonlardan himoya qiladi. C javob chumolili va chumolisiz daraxtlarni solishtiradi va jirafalar chumolili daraxtlardan ancha kam barg yeganini ko‘rsatadi — gipoteza aynan shuni bashorat qiladi.\\n\\nA chumolilar daraxtdan nima olishini tushuntiradi, ular daraxtni himoya qiladimi-yo‘qmi, buni emas. B jirafalar qachon oziqlanishi haqida, chumolilar bunga ta’sir qilishi haqida emas. D daraxtlar qayerda o‘sishi haqida, chumolilarning jirafalarga ta’siri haqida hech narsa demaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"*The Salt Road* is a 1971 novel by Mirela Dace. In the novel, the narrator describes her aunt Vesna as a restless person who can hardly stay still.\",\"stem\":\"Which quotation from *The Salt Road* most effectively illustrates the claim?\",\"option_a\":\"“Even at dinner, Aunt Vesna was up three times before the soup was finished, straightening a picture, opening a window, moving the bread from one end of the table to the other.”\",\"option_b\":\"“Aunt Vesna had lived in the same stone house by the harbor for forty years.”\",\"option_c\":\"“Her letters, when they came, were short and always written in green ink.”\",\"option_d\":\"“Everyone in the village agreed that Aunt Vesna made the best plum jam on the coast.”\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The claim is that Aunt Vesna is restless and can hardly stay still. Choice A shows her getting up three times during a single dinner to do small tasks, a clear illustration of restlessness.\\n\\nChoice B describes her living in one house for forty years, which, if anything, suggests stability. Choice C describes her letters, not her restlessness. Choice D describes her skill at making jam.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Da’voga ko‘ra, Vesna xola bezovta, bir joyda tinch o‘tira olmaydigan odam. A javob uning bitta kechki ovqat davomida mayda ishlar uchun uch marta o‘rnidan turganini ko‘rsatadi — bu bezovtalikning yaqqol misoli.\\n\\nB uning qirq yil bir uyda yashaganini aytadi, bu esa, aksincha, barqarorlikni bildiradi. C bezovtaligini emas, maktublarini tasvirlaydi. D uning murabbo pishirish mahoratini tasvirlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Urban planner Akmal Hamidov hypothesizes that installing benches along a shopping street makes older residents more likely to walk there, since they can stop and rest whenever they need to.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Hamidov's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"Older residents said that they preferred shopping streets lined with trees.\",\"option_b\":\"The benches on the street were used most often by teenagers in the evening.\",\"option_c\":\"Most of the shops on the street were owned by residents over the age of 65.\",\"option_d\":\"After benches were installed on the street, the number of residents over 65 who walked there each week rose sharply, while it stayed the same on a similar street without new benches.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Hamidov's hypothesis connects benches with how often older residents walk on a street. Choice D shows that older residents' walking rose sharply on the street that got benches but not on a similar street that did not, directly supporting the hypothesis.\\n\\nChoice A concerns trees, not benches. Choice B concerns teenagers, not older residents. Choice C concerns who owns the shops, not who walks on the street.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Hamidov gipotezasi o‘rindiqlarni keksa aholining ko‘chada qanchalik ko‘p yurishi bilan bog‘laydi. D javob o‘rindiq o‘rnatilgan ko‘chada keksalarning yurishi keskin ko‘payganini, o‘rindiq qo‘yilmagan o‘xshash ko‘chada esa o‘zgarmaganini ko‘rsatadi — bu gipotezani bevosita tasdiqlaydi.\\n\\nA o‘rindiqlar emas, daraxtlar haqida. B keksalar emas, o‘smirlar haqida. C ko‘chada kim yurishi emas, do‘konlar kimga tegishli ekani haqida.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"At the Bronze Age site of Ural Tepe, archaeologists have found hundreds of small clay cones, spheres and disks. Archaeologist Kamol Rashidov hypothesizes that the objects were pieces used in a board game, noting that they come in a few standard shapes and sizes, much like the pieces of known ancient games.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken Rashidov's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"Similar clay objects have been found at several other Bronze Age sites in the region.\",\"option_b\":\"The objects were found almost exclusively inside sealed storage jars, alongside clay tablets recording amounts of grain and oil.\",\"option_c\":\"A carved stone board marked with a grid of squares was found in one of the houses at Ural Tepe.\",\"option_d\":\"Many of the objects show the kind of wear that comes from frequent handling.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"If the objects were game pieces, they would be expected where people played games, not sealed away in storage. Choice B places them almost exclusively in sealed storage jars beside records of grain and oil, which points to a different use, such as keeping track of goods, and so weakens the hypothesis.\\n\\nChoice A says nothing about how the objects were used. Choice C would support the hypothesis, since a game board suggests that games were played at the site. Choice D is consistent with game pieces, which are handled often, so it does not weaken the hypothesis.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Agar bu buyumlar o‘yin donalari bo‘lganida, ular o‘yin o‘ynalgan joylarda topilishi kutilardi, omborda muhrlab qo‘yilgan holda emas. B javobga ko‘ra ular deyarli faqat muhrlangan saqlash ko‘zalarida, don va yog‘ miqdori yozilgan sopol lavhalar yonida topilgan. Bu boshqa vazifani — masalan, mahsulotlarni hisobga olishni ko‘rsatadi va gipotezani zaiflashtiradi.\\n\\nA buyumlar nima uchun ishlatilgani haqida hech narsa demaydi. C aksincha gipotezani qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi, chunki o‘yin taxtasi u yerda o‘yin o‘ynalganini bildiradi. D o‘yin donalariga mos keladi, chunki ular tez-tez qo‘lda ushlanadi, shuning uchun gipotezani zaiflashtirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"“Lantern Hours” is a 1927 poem by Ilse Carrow. In the poem, the speaker describes feeling lonely even when surrounded by other people.\",\"stem\":\"Which quotation from “Lantern Hours” most effectively illustrates the claim?\",\"option_a\":\"“The city's lamps came on along the quay, / one, then another, like a slow-spoken word.”\",\"option_b\":\"“I walked alone across the empty field / and heard no voice except the wind's.”\",\"option_c\":\"“My friends and I would laugh till morning came, / and every window glowed with our delight.”\",\"option_d\":\"“The room was loud with dancing and with talk, / and still I stood as if on some far shore.”\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The claim has two parts: the speaker feels lonely, and this happens while surrounded by people. In choice D, the room is \\\"loud with dancing and with talk,\\\" yet the speaker stands \\\"as if on some far shore,\\\" an image of isolation in the middle of a crowd.\\n\\nChoice A describes lamps coming on and involves neither people nor loneliness. Choice B shows the speaker alone, but in an \\\"empty field,\\\" not among other people. Choice C shows the speaker among friends but feeling joy, not loneliness.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Da’vo ikki qismdan iborat: shoir o‘zini yolg‘iz his qiladi va bu odamlar orasida bo‘lganda sodir bo‘ladi. D javobda xona “raqs va suhbatdan shovqinli”, ammo shoir go‘yo “olis qirg‘oqda” turgandek — bu olomon ichidagi yolg‘izlik timsoli.\\n\\nA chiroqlar yonishini tasvirlaydi, unda na odamlar, na yolg‘izlik bor. B shoirni yolg‘iz ko‘rsatadi, lekin odamlar orasida emas, “bo‘m-bo‘sh dalada” (“empty field”). C shoirni do‘stlari orasida ko‘rsatadi, ammo u yolg‘izlik emas, quvonch his qiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Sleep researcher Timur Valiev hypothesizes that a short afternoon nap improves people's ability to learn a new physical skill only if the nap includes a stage of deep sleep.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Valiev's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"Participants whose naps included deep sleep improved at a new typing task more than participants whose naps of the same length contained no deep sleep.\",\"option_b\":\"Participants who napped reported feeling more alert afterward than participants who did not nap.\",\"option_c\":\"Participants who napped for 20 minutes and participants who napped for 60 minutes improved equally at a new typing task.\",\"option_d\":\"Participants learned a new typing task faster in the morning than in the evening.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Valiev's hypothesis links improvement in learning a physical skill to whether a nap contains deep sleep. Choice A compares naps of the same length that differ only in whether they include deep sleep and shows greater improvement with deep sleep, directly supporting the hypothesis.\\n\\nChoice B concerns alertness, not skill learning. Choice C compares nap lengths but says nothing about deep sleep, so it cannot show that deep sleep matters. Choice D concerns the time of day, not napping.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Valiev gipotezasi jismoniy ko‘nikmani o‘rganishdagi yaxshilanishni uyquda chuqur uyqu bosqichi bor-yo‘qligi bilan bog‘laydi. A javob bir xil davomiylikdagi, faqat chuqur uyqu bor-yo‘qligi bilan farq qiladigan uyqularni solishtiradi va chuqur uyquda yaxshilanish ko‘proq ekanini ko‘rsatadi — bu gipotezani bevosita tasdiqlaydi.\\n\\nB ko‘nikma o‘rganish emas, tetiklik haqida. C uyqu davomiyligini solishtiradi, lekin chuqur uyqu haqida hech narsa demaydi, shuning uchun uning ahamiyatini ko‘rsata olmaydi. D uyqu emas, kunning vaqti haqida.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Female Corsan finches often weave fresh leaves of aromatic herbs, such as wild mint, into their nests. Some researchers have proposed that the leaves simply help keep the nest warm. Ecologist Dina Morales, however, hypothesizes that chemicals released by the herbs reduce the number of blood-feeding mites in the nest.\",\"stem\":\"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Morales's hypothesis?\",\"option_a\":\"Nests containing aromatic herbs had fewer mites and stayed warmer than nests to which no leaves had been added.\",\"option_b\":\"Corsan finches added more herbs to their nests during the colder weeks of the breeding season.\",\"option_c\":\"Nests in which researchers replaced the herbs with an equal amount of fresh, nonaromatic leaves had many more mites than nests that kept their herbs, even though nest temperatures were the same.\",\"option_d\":\"Mites are more common in Corsan finch nests than in the nests of other songbirds in the same area.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Morales's hypothesis is that chemicals from the aromatic herbs reduce mites. Choice C keeps the amount of leaf material and the nest temperature the same and changes only whether the leaves are aromatic; the nests with nonaromatic leaves had many more mites. This isolates the herbs' chemical effect and rules out warmth as the explanation.\\n\\nChoice A shows fewer mites in herb nests, but those nests were also warmer and simply had more material, so the result fits the insulation idea as well and does not specifically support Morales. Choice B supports the competing idea that herbs provide warmth. Choice D compares finches with other birds and says nothing about the herbs' effect.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Morales gipotezasiga ko‘ra, xushbo‘y o‘tlardan ajraladigan kimyoviy moddalar kanalar sonini kamaytiradi. C javobda barg miqdori va uya harorati bir xil saqlanadi, faqat barglarning xushbo‘y yoki xushbo‘y emasligi o‘zgaradi; xushbo‘y bo‘lmagan bargli uyalarda kanalar ancha ko‘p bo‘lgan. Bu o‘tlarning kimyoviy ta’sirini ajratib ko‘rsatadi va issiqlik izohini istisno qiladi.\\n\\nA o‘tli uyalarda kanalar kamligini ko‘rsatadi, lekin bu uyalar issiqroq ham bo‘lgan va ularda shunchaki ko‘proq material bo‘lgan; demak, natija issiqlik g‘oyasiga ham mos keladi va aynan Moralesni qo‘llab-quvvatlamaydi. B o‘tlar issiqlik beradi degan raqib g‘oyani qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi. D Corsan qushlarini boshqa qushlar bilan solishtiradi va o‘tlarning ta’siri haqida hech narsa demaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"command_of_evidence_textual\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"*The Lamplighter's Daughter* is a 1949 novel by Corin Ashby. In the novel, the narrator, Anouk, suggests that her mother's apparent indifference to Anouk's career as a pianist concealed a quiet pride in her achievements.\",\"stem\":\"Which quotation from *The Lamplighter's Daughter* most effectively illustrates the narrator's suggestion?\",\"option_a\":\"“When I won the conservatory prize, Mother said only, ‘Good. Now perhaps you will stop practicing so late at night.’”\",\"option_b\":\"“She never once spoke to me about my playing, yet after she died I found the program from every one of my concerts folded neatly in her sewing box.”\",\"option_c\":\"“My teacher told me that I had a rare gift, and I believed her more readily than I believed anyone at home.”\",\"option_d\":\"“It was years before I learned that Mother, as a girl, had dreamed of becoming a pianist herself.”\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The narrator's suggestion has two parts: her mother seemed indifferent, but she was secretly proud. Choice B shows both: the mother \\\"never once spoke\\\" about Anouk's playing (apparent indifference), yet she had saved the program from every concert (quiet pride).\\n\\nChoice A shows only the apparent indifference, with no sign of hidden pride. Choice C concerns the teacher's view, not the mother's. Choice D reveals a hidden fact about the mother, but a past dream of her own does not show that she was proud of Anouk's achievements; it could just as easily suggest envy or regret.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Hikoyachining fikri ikki qismdan iborat: onasi befarq ko‘ringan, lekin ichida faxrlangan. B javob ikkalasini ham ko‘rsatadi: ona Anukning ijrosi haqida “hech qachon gapirmagan” (tashqi befarqlik), ammo uning har bir konserti dasturini saqlab qo‘ygan (yashirin faxr).\\n\\nA faqat tashqi befarqlikni ko‘rsatadi, yashirin faxrga ishora yo‘q. C onaning emas, o‘qituvchining fikri haqida. D ona haqidagi yashirin bir faktni ochadi, lekin uning yoshlikdagi orzusi Anukning yutuqlaridan faxrlanganini ko‘rsatmaydi; bu hasad yoki afsusni ham anglatishi mumkin.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nIt is often said that goldfish have a memory span of only a few seconds. According to this popular belief, a goldfish swimming around its bowl finds everything new each time it completes a lap.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nBiologist Hana Kovač trained goldfish to push a small lever to receive food. She then removed the lever for three months. When the lever was returned, most of the fish pushed it within minutes, much faster than untrained fish learned to do so. Kovač concludes that goldfish can remember what they have learned for months.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Kovač (Text 2) most likely respond to the popular belief described in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"She would reject it, since her goldfish remembered a learned behavior after three months.\",\"option_b\":\"She would accept it, since her goldfish forgot how to use the lever within a few seconds.\",\"option_c\":\"She would argue that it is true of wild goldfish but not of goldfish kept in bowls.\",\"option_d\":\"She would claim that goldfish remember sounds but not actions.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Text 1 describes the belief that goldfish remember things for only a few seconds. In Kovač's study, trained goldfish still knew how to use the lever after three months, so she would reject the belief, as choice A says.\\n\\nChoice B contradicts her results. Choice C is unsupported: Text 2 does not discuss wild goldfish. Choice D is unsupported: Text 2 says nothing about sounds, and the fish clearly remembered an action.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Text 1 da oltin baliqlar narsalarni faqat bir necha soniya eslab qoladi degan tushuncha keltirilgan. Kovač tadqiqotida esa o‘rgatilgan baliqlar uch oydan keyin ham richagdan foydalanishni eslab qolgan. Demak, u bu tushunchani rad etardi — to‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB uning natijalariga zid. C asossiz: Text 2 da yovvoyi oltin baliqlar haqida gap yo‘q. D ham asossiz: Text 2 da tovushlar haqida hech narsa aytilmagan, baliqlar esa harakatni aniq eslab qolgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nArchitect Lola Nematova supports covering city rooftops with soil and plants. Such green roofs, she argues, are worth their cost mainly because they keep buildings cooler in summer, reducing the energy needed for air conditioning.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nEngineer Paolo Ricci agrees that green roofs are worth building but emphasizes a different benefit. During heavy rain, the soil and plants on a green roof absorb much of the water, reducing the amount that rushes into city drains and helping prevent street flooding.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, Nematova (Text 1) and Ricci (Text 2) would most likely agree with which statement?\",\"option_a\":\"Green roofs increase the amount of rainwater that flows into city drains.\",\"option_b\":\"Green roofs have little effect on how much energy buildings use.\",\"option_c\":\"Green roofs provide benefits that justify building them.\",\"option_d\":\"Reducing the cost of cooling buildings is the most important benefit of green roofs.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Nematova says green roofs are \\\"worth their cost,\\\" and Ricci \\\"agrees that green roofs are worth building,\\\" though each stresses a different benefit. Both would therefore accept choice C.\\n\\nChoice A contradicts Ricci, who says green roofs reduce the water flowing into drains. Choice B contradicts Nematova, who says green roofs reduce the energy needed for air conditioning. Choice D reflects only Nematova's emphasis; Ricci stresses a different benefit.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Nematova yashil tomlar o‘z narxiga arziydi (“worth their cost”) deydi, Ricci ham yashil tomlar qurishga arziydi degan fikrga qo‘shiladi, garchi har biri turli foydani ta’kidlasa ham. Demak, ikkalasi ham C fikriga rozi bo‘ladi.\\n\\nA Riccining fikriga zid: u yashil tomlar kanalizatsiyaga oqadigan suvni kamaytiradi deydi. B Nematovaning fikriga zid: u yashil tomlar konditsioner uchun kerakli energiyani kamaytiradi deydi. D faqat Nematovaning urg‘usini aks ettiradi; Ricci boshqa foydani ta’kidlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nWhen photography was invented in the nineteenth century, many art critics refused to consider it an art form. A camera, they argued, simply records whatever is placed in front of it, so a photograph is a mechanical copy rather than a creative work.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nHistorian Leila Ortiz points out that early photographers made many decisions that shaped their images. They chose what to include in the frame, arranged lighting, decided how long to expose each plate and experimented with chemicals during developing to darken or soften parts of a picture.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Ortiz (Text 2) most likely respond to the critics' argument in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"By agreeing that early photographs were merely mechanical copies of their subjects\",\"option_b\":\"By pointing out that photographers made many choices that shaped how their images looked\",\"option_c\":\"By arguing that nineteenth-century paintings were less accurate than photographs\",\"option_d\":\"By claiming that photography became popular only after critics praised it\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The critics in Text 1 argue that photographs are mechanical copies rather than creative works. Ortiz describes the many decisions early photographers made about framing, lighting, exposure and developing, so she would respond as choice B says.\\n\\nChoice A is the opposite of her point. Choice C is unsupported: Text 2 never compares the accuracy of paintings and photographs. Choice D is unsupported: Text 2 does not discuss photography's popularity or any praise from critics.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Text 1 dagi tanqidchilar fotosuratni ijodiy asar emas, mexanik nusxa deb hisoblaydi. Ortiz esa ilk fotograflar kadrga nimani olish, yorug‘lik, ekspozitsiya va suratni ochiltirish bo‘yicha ko‘plab qarorlar qabul qilganini tasvirlaydi. Demak, u B javobdagidek javob berardi.\\n\\nA uning fikrining aksi. C asossiz: Text 2 da rasmlar va fotosuratlarning aniqligi solishtirilmaydi. D ham asossiz: Text 2 da fotografiyaning ommabopligi yoki tanqidchilar maqtovi haqida gap yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nA fast-growing vine introduced from overseas now covers long stretches of the riverbanks along the Zarin River, smothering native shrubs. Ecologist Daniel Moss argues that clearing the vine will allow the native warblers that once nested in those shrubs to return.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nEcologist Ayesha Karimi studied riverbank sites where the same vine had been cleared five years earlier. At sites that were simply cleared, the bare banks eroded and were quickly taken over by weedy grasses, and warblers did not return. Warblers returned only at sites where native shrubs had been planted after the vine was removed.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Karimi (Text 2) most likely respond to Moss's argument in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"She would agree that clearing the vine is enough by itself to bring warblers back.\",\"option_b\":\"She would argue that the vine benefits warblers and should be left in place.\",\"option_c\":\"She would claim that warblers never nested along the Zarin River.\",\"option_d\":\"She would argue that clearing the vine is unlikely to bring warblers back unless native shrubs are also planted.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Moss argues that clearing the vine will let warblers return. Karimi found that warblers did not return to sites that were simply cleared but did return where native shrubs were planted after clearing. She would therefore say that clearing alone is not enough, as choice D says.\\n\\nChoice A contradicts her finding about sites that were simply cleared. Choice B goes too far: Karimi studies what happens after the vine is removed and never suggests the vine helps warblers. Choice C is unsupported and conflicts with her finding that warblers returned to some sites.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Moss chirmovuqni tozalash qushlarning qaytishiga imkon beradi deb hisoblaydi. Karimi esa shunchaki tozalangan joylarga qushlar qaytmaganini, tozalangandan keyin mahalliy butalar ekilgan joylarga esa qaytganini aniqlagan. Demak, u faqat tozalashning o‘zi yetarli emas deb aytardi — to‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA uning shunchaki tozalangan joylar haqidagi topilmasiga zid. B haddan oshib ketadi: Karimi chirmovuq olib tashlangandan keyin nima bo‘lishini o‘rganadi, chirmovuq qushlarga foyda keltiradi demaydi. C asossiz va qushlar ba’zi joylarga qaytgani haqidagi topilmaga zid.\",\"estimated_seconds\":77,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nThe early poems of Rasa Ilmen are long, crowded with images and full of difficult allusions. Her late poems, by contrast, are short and use plain, everyday words. Critic Owen Hart sees this change as evidence that Ilmen's ambition declined as she aged and that she no longer wished to challenge herself.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nScholar Farhod Mirzaev has examined the drafts of Ilmen's late poems. Many began as pages-long works that Ilmen revised for years, cutting lines and replacing rare words with common ones, until only a few short stanzas remained. In her notebooks, she called this process \\\"the hardest work I have done.\\\"\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Mirzaev (Text 2) most likely respond to Hart's view in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"He would argue that the simplicity of the late poems reflects careful, demanding work rather than a decline in ambition.\",\"option_b\":\"He would agree that Ilmen wrote her late poems quickly and with little effort.\",\"option_c\":\"He would argue that Ilmen's early poems were also short and simple.\",\"option_d\":\"He would claim that the late poems were most likely written by someone other than Ilmen.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Hart reads the late poems' simplicity as a sign of declining ambition. Mirzaev shows that the poems became simple through years of deliberate revision, which Ilmen herself called \\\"the hardest work I have done.\\\" He would therefore argue as choice A says.\\n\\nChoice B contradicts the evidence of long, difficult revision. Choice C contradicts both texts: Text 1 describes the early poems as long and complex, and Text 2 does not dispute this. Choice D is unsupported: Mirzaev studies Ilmen's own drafts and notebooks.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Hart kech davr she’rlarining soddaligini intilish susaygani belgisi deb biladi. Mirzaev esa she’rlar yillar davomida ongli ravishda qayta ishlash orqali soddalashganini ko‘rsatadi; Ilmenning o‘zi buni “qilgan eng og‘ir ishim” deb atagan. Demak, u A javobdagidek fikr bildirardi.\\n\\nB uzoq va mashaqqatli tahrir haqidagi dalillarga zid. C ikkala matnga ham zid: Text 1 da ilk she’rlar uzun va murakkab deb tasvirlanadi, Text 2 esa buni inkor etmaydi. D asossiz: Mirzaev Ilmenning o‘z qoralamalari va daftarlarini o‘rgangan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":77,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nThe ancient city of Varesh was largely abandoned by about 930 CE. Sediment cores from a nearby lake show that the region experienced a severe, decades-long drought beginning around 880. Many researchers conclude that this drought caused the city's decline by making it impossible to grow enough food.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nArchaeologist Selma Duran has dated the abandonment of houses throughout Varesh. She finds that the city's population began falling around 820 and had already dropped by half by 870, as trade routes shifted away from the city. The drought, Duran argues, may have hastened the end of a city that was already in decline.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Duran (Text 2) most likely respond to the conclusion described in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"She would agree that the drought was the main reason the population of Varesh began to fall.\",\"option_b\":\"She would argue that the drought could not have started the city's decline, since the population was already falling decades before the drought began.\",\"option_c\":\"She would argue that the lake sediments do not actually show a drought in the region.\",\"option_d\":\"She would claim that the trade routes shifted away from Varesh because of the drought.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Text 1 says the drought, beginning around 880, caused Varesh's decline. Duran finds that the population started falling around 820 and had halved by 870, before the drought. She would therefore say the drought cannot have started the decline, though it may have sped it up, as choice B says.\\n\\nChoice A contradicts her timeline. Choice C is wrong because Duran does not dispute that a drought occurred; she says it \\\"may have hastened\\\" the city's end. Choice D is impossible given her timeline: the trade routes shifted while the population was falling from 820 on, before the drought began.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Text 1 ga ko‘ra, taxminan 880-yilda boshlangan qurg‘oqchilik Vareshning tanazzuliga sabab bo‘lgan. Duran esa aholi taxminan 820-yildan kamaya boshlaganini va 870-yilga kelib, ya’ni qurg‘oqchilikdan oldin, ikki baravar qisqarganini aniqlagan. Demak, u qurg‘oqchilik tanazzulni boshlab bera olmagan, faqat uni tezlashtirgan bo‘lishi mumkin der edi — to‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA uning xronologiyasiga zid. C noto‘g‘ri: Duran qurg‘oqchilik bo‘lganini inkor etmaydi, aksincha, u shahar oxirini “tezlashtirgan bo‘lishi mumkin” deydi. D uning xronologiyasiga ko‘ra imkonsiz: savdo yo‘llari aholi 820-yildan boshlab kamayayotgan paytda, qurg‘oqchilikdan oldin o‘zgargan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":77,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nIn a recent trial, sixty companies moved their employees to a four-day workweek with no reduction in pay. After six months, output per employee at most of the companies was the same as or higher than before. Economist Aziz Salimov argues that the results show that most businesses could adopt a four-day workweek without losing productivity.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nEconomist Marta Lindgren notes that the companies in the trial chose to take part, and nearly all were small firms whose work is done mainly at computers. Businesses that expected a shorter week to cause problems, such as factories and hospitals that must be staffed at all hours, generally declined to join. Lindgren does not dispute the trial's measurements, but she cautions against drawing broad conclusions from them.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Lindgren (Text 2) most likely respond to Salimov's argument in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"She would argue that his conclusion rests on inaccurate measurements of employees' output.\",\"option_b\":\"She would agree with his conclusion but add that small firms benefited the most from the shorter week.\",\"option_c\":\"She would argue that the trial shows that a four-day workweek reduces productivity at factories and hospitals.\",\"option_d\":\"She would argue that the trial's results do not justify his conclusion about most businesses, since the companies that took part were not typical of businesses in general.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Salimov generalizes from the trial to \\\"most businesses.\\\" Lindgren points out that the participants chose to join and were mostly small computer-based firms, while businesses expecting problems stayed out, and she warns against broad conclusions. She would therefore say the results do not support his claim about most businesses, as choice D says.\\n\\nChoice A is wrong because the text states that Lindgren \\\"does not dispute the trial's measurements.\\\" Choice B is wrong because she questions his conclusion rather than agreeing with it. Choice C is wrong because factories and hospitals generally did not take part, so the trial provides no evidence about them either way.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Salimov sinov natijalarini “ko‘pchilik korxonalar”ga umumlashtiradi. Lindgren esa ishtirokchilar o‘z ixtiyori bilan qatnashganini va ular asosan kompyuterda ishlaydigan kichik firmalar bo‘lganini, muammo kutgan korxonalar esa qatnashmaganini ta’kidlaydi va keng xulosa chiqarishdan ogohlantiradi. Demak, u natijalar ko‘pchilik korxonalar haqidagi da’voni oqlamaydi der edi — to‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA noto‘g‘ri, chunki matnda Lindgren sinov o‘lchovlariga e’tiroz bildirmasligi (“does not dispute the trial's measurements”) aytilgan. B noto‘g‘ri: u Salimovning xulosasiga qo‘shilmaydi, aksincha, uni shubha ostiga oladi. C noto‘g‘ri: zavod va shifoxonalar asosan qatnashmagan, shuning uchun sinov ular haqida hech qanday dalil bermaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":93,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"cross_text_connections\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"**Text 1**\\n\\nFor thirty years, Hanna Ruel, a farmer's wife in the village of Osterby, kept a diary of daily life: harvests, weddings, illnesses, prices at market. Historian Kerem Aslan prizes the diary as a record of eighteenth-century village life, arguing that because Ruel wrote each entry as events happened, her account is free of the reshaping that memory brings.\\n\\n**Text 2**\\n\\nAnalyzing the diary's ink and paper, scholar Ivana Petrov found that the entries for 1760 to 1775 were copied out in the 1790s, when Ruel was elderly, and that some of these entries refer to events that had not yet happened on the dates they bear. Petrov nonetheless considers the diary valuable, especially as evidence of how Ruel, late in life, understood her own past.\",\"stem\":\"Based on the texts, how would Petrov (Text 2) most likely respond to Aslan's reasoning in Text 1?\",\"option_a\":\"She would agree that the diary is an unaltered record of daily life in Osterby.\",\"option_b\":\"She would argue that the diary has little value to historians because parts of it were rewritten.\",\"option_c\":\"She would argue that at least some entries were not written as events happened and so may reflect the kind of reshaping by memory that Aslan says the diary is free of.\",\"option_d\":\"She would argue that the diary was most likely written by someone other than Ruel.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Aslan's reasoning depends on the assumption that each entry was written as events happened. Petrov found that many entries were copied out decades later and that some mention events that had not yet occurred on their dates, so these entries could have been reshaped by memory. Choice C states this response.\\n\\nChoice A contradicts her findings. Choice B misrepresents her view: Petrov \\\"nonetheless considers the diary valuable.\\\" Choice D is unsupported: she describes the entries as copied out by Ruel herself when she was elderly.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Aslanning mulohazasi har bir yozuv voqealar sodir bo‘lgan paytda yozilgan degan farazga tayanadi. Petrov esa ko‘plab yozuvlar o‘n yillar o‘tib qayta ko‘chirilganini va ularning ba’zilarida ko‘rsatilgan sanada hali sodir bo‘lmagan voqealar tilga olinganini aniqlagan; demak, bu yozuvlar xotira ta’sirida o‘zgargan bo‘lishi mumkin. C javob aynan shu javobni ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA uning topilmalariga zid. B uning fikrini buzib ko‘rsatadi: Petrov shunga qaramay kundalikni qimmatli deb biladi (“nonetheless considers the diary valuable”). D asossiz: u yozuvlarni Ruelning o‘zi keksaygan chog‘ida ko‘chirib yozgan deb tasvirlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":93,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which expression is equivalent to $(2x^2 - 5x + 3) - (x^2 + 4x - 6)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$x^2 - x - 3$\",\"option_b\":\"$3x^2 - x - 3$\",\"option_c\":\"$x^2 - 9x + 9$\",\"option_d\":\"$x^2 - 9x - 3$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute the negative sign to every term of the second polynomial: $2x^2 - 5x + 3 - x^2 - 4x + 6$. Combine like terms: $(2x^2 - x^2) + (-5x - 4x) + (3 + 6) = x^2 - 9x + 9$.\\n\\nChoice A comes from subtracting only $x^2$ and keeping $+4x - 6$ unchanged. Choice B adds the $x^2$ terms instead of subtracting them. Choice D subtracts $-6$ incorrectly, writing $3 - 6$ instead of $3 + 6$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkinchi ko‘phadning har bir hadiga minus ishorasini tarqatamiz: $2x^2 - 5x + 3 - x^2 - 4x + 6$. O‘xshash hadlarni birlashtiramiz: $(2x^2 - x^2) + (-5x - 4x) + (3 + 6) = x^2 - 9x + 9$.\\n\\nA variant — faqat $x^2$ ayirilib, $+4x - 6$ o‘zgarmay qolgandagi natija. B variantda $x^2$ hadlari ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan. D variantda $-6$ ni ayirish noto‘g‘ri bajarilgan: $3 + 6$ o‘rniga $3 - 6$ yozilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which expression is equivalent to $(2x + 5)^2$?\",\"option_a\":\"$4x^2 + 20x + 25$\",\"option_b\":\"$4x^2 + 25$\",\"option_c\":\"$4x^2 + 10x + 25$\",\"option_d\":\"$2x^2 + 20x + 25$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Write the square as a product and expand: $(2x + 5)(2x + 5) = 4x^2 + 10x + 10x + 25 = 4x^2 + 20x + 25$. This matches the pattern $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$ with $a = 2x$ and $b = 5$.\\n\\nChoice B squares each term separately and drops the middle term $2ab$. Choice C includes the middle term only once ($10x$) instead of twice. Choice D forgets to square the coefficient $2$ in $(2x)^2$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kvadratni ko‘paytma ko‘rinishida yozib, qavslarni ochamiz: $(2x + 5)(2x + 5) = 4x^2 + 10x + 10x + 25 = 4x^2 + 20x + 25$. Bu $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$ formulasiga mos keladi, bunda $a = 2x$, $b = 5$.\\n\\nB variantda har bir had alohida kvadratga oshirilib, o‘rta had $2ab$ tashlab yuborilgan. C variantda o‘rta had ikki marta emas, bir marta ($10x$) olingan. D variantda $(2x)^2$ dagi $2$ koeffitsiyent kvadratga oshirilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The expression $5x(x - 4) + 3x$ is equivalent to $ax^2 + bx$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants. What is the value of $b$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-17\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute $5x$: $5x(x - 4) = 5x^2 - 20x$. Then add $3x$: $5x^2 - 20x + 3x = 5x^2 - 17x$. So $a = 5$ and $b = -17$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $-23$, which comes from treating $+3x$ as $-3x$, or entering $-20$, which forgets to combine the $3x$ term at all.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$5x$ ni qavs ichiga ko‘paytiramiz: $5x(x - 4) = 5x^2 - 20x$. So‘ng $3x$ ni qo‘shamiz: $5x^2 - 20x + 3x = 5x^2 - 17x$. Demak, $a = 5$ va $b = -17$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xatolar: $+3x$ ni $-3x$ deb olib, $-23$ ni kiritish yoki $3x$ hadini umuman qo‘shmay, $-20$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"For $x > 0$, which of the following is equivalent to $\\\\sqrt[3]{x^2} \\\\cdot \\\\sqrt{x}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$x^{\\\\frac{1}{3}}$\",\"option_b\":\"$x^{\\\\frac{7}{6}}$\",\"option_c\":\"$x^{\\\\frac{3}{5}}$\",\"option_d\":\"$x^{\\\\frac{5}{6}}$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Rewrite each radical as a rational exponent: $\\\\sqrt[3]{x^2} = x^{\\\\frac{2}{3}}$ and $\\\\sqrt{x} = x^{\\\\frac{1}{2}}$. When multiplying powers with the same base, add the exponents: $\\\\frac{2}{3} + \\\\frac{1}{2} = \\\\frac{4}{6} + \\\\frac{3}{6} = \\\\frac{7}{6}$. So the expression equals $x^{\\\\frac{7}{6}}$.\\n\\nChoice A multiplies the exponents ($\\\\frac{2}{3} \\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}$) instead of adding them. Choice C adds numerators and denominators separately ($\\\\frac{2 + 1}{3 + 2}$). Choice D uses $x^{\\\\frac{1}{3}}$ for $\\\\sqrt[3]{x^2}$, ignoring the square inside the cube root.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir ildizni kasr daraja ko‘rinishida yozamiz: $\\\\sqrt[3]{x^2} = x^{\\\\frac{2}{3}}$ va $\\\\sqrt{x} = x^{\\\\frac{1}{2}}$. Asoslari bir xil darajalar ko‘paytirilganda ko‘rsatkichlar qo‘shiladi: $\\\\frac{2}{3} + \\\\frac{1}{2} = \\\\frac{4}{6} + \\\\frac{3}{6} = \\\\frac{7}{6}$. Demak, ifoda $x^{\\\\frac{7}{6}}$ ga teng.\\n\\nA variantda ko‘rsatkichlar qo‘shilish o‘rniga ko‘paytirilgan ($\\\\frac{2}{3} \\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}$). C variantda surat va maxrajlar alohida qo‘shilgan ($\\\\frac{2 + 1}{3 + 2}$). D variantda $\\\\sqrt[3]{x^2}$ o‘rniga $x^{\\\\frac{1}{3}}$ olingan, ya’ni ildiz ostidagi kvadrat e’tiborga olinmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the equation $(3x + k)(x - 2) = 3x^2 + 7x - 26$, $k$ is a constant. If the equation is true for all values of $x$, what is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"13\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Expand the left side: $(3x + k)(x - 2) = 3x^2 - 6x + kx - 2k = 3x^2 + (k - 6)x - 2k$. Matching coefficients with $3x^2 + 7x - 26$ gives $k - 6 = 7$ and $-2k = -26$. Both equations give $k = 13$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $1$, which comes from writing the $x$-coefficient as $k + 6$ (losing the negative sign in $-2 \\\\cdot 3x$). Another is entering $-13$ from mishandling the sign in $-2k = -26$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Chap tomonni ochamiz: $(3x + k)(x - 2) = 3x^2 - 6x + kx - 2k = 3x^2 + (k - 6)x - 2k$. Koeffitsiyentlarni $3x^2 + 7x - 26$ bilan tenglashtiramiz: $k - 6 = 7$ va $-2k = -26$. Ikkalasidan ham $k = 13$ chiqadi.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $x$ oldidagi koeffitsiyentni $k + 6$ deb yozib ($-2 \\\\cdot 3x$ dagi minusni yo‘qotib), $1$ ni kiritish. Yana bir xato — $-2k = -26$ dagi ishorani noto‘g‘ri olib, $-13$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following is equivalent to $\\\\dfrac{x^2 - 16}{x^2 + 2x - 8}$ for $x \\\\ne -4$ and $x \\\\ne 2$?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\dfrac{x + 4}{x - 2}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\dfrac{-16}{2x - 8}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\dfrac{x - 4}{x + 2}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\dfrac{x - 4}{x - 2}$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Factor the numerator as a difference of squares: $x^2 - 16 = (x - 4)(x + 4)$. Factor the denominator: $x^2 + 2x - 8 = (x + 4)(x - 2)$, since $4 \\\\cdot (-2) = -8$ and $4 + (-2) = 2$. Cancel the common factor $x + 4$: $\\\\dfrac{(x - 4)(x + 4)}{(x + 4)(x - 2)} = \\\\dfrac{x - 4}{x - 2}$.\\n\\nChoice A cancels the wrong factor, keeping $x + 4$ in the numerator. Choice B \\\"cancels\\\" the $x^2$ terms, which is not allowed because they are terms, not factors. Choice C factors the denominator with the wrong signs, as $(x + 4)(x + 2)$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Suratni kvadratlar ayirmasi sifatida ko‘paytuvchilarga ajratamiz: $x^2 - 16 = (x - 4)(x + 4)$. Maxrajni ajratamiz: $x^2 + 2x - 8 = (x + 4)(x - 2)$, chunki $4 \\\\cdot (-2) = -8$ va $4 + (-2) = 2$. Umumiy ko‘paytuvchi $x + 4$ ga qisqartiramiz: $\\\\dfrac{(x - 4)(x + 4)}{(x + 4)(x - 2)} = \\\\dfrac{x - 4}{x - 2}$.\\n\\nA variantda noto‘g‘ri ko‘paytuvchi qisqartirilib, suratda $x + 4$ qolgan. B variantda $x^2$ hadlari “qisqartirilgan” — bu mumkin emas, chunki ular ko‘paytuvchi emas, qo‘shiluvchi. C variantda maxraj noto‘g‘ri ishoralar bilan $(x + 4)(x + 2)$ deb ajratilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":95,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In the equation $(ax + 3)(2x - b) = 6x^2 + cx - 15$, $a$, $b$, and $c$ are constants. If the equation is true for all values of $x$, what is the value of $c$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-9$\",\"option_b\":\"$9$\",\"option_c\":\"$-21$\",\"option_d\":\"$21$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Expand the left side: $(ax + 3)(2x - b) = 2ax^2 - abx + 6x - 3b = 2ax^2 + (6 - ab)x - 3b$.\\n\\nMatch coefficients with $6x^2 + cx - 15$:\\n- $x^2$ terms: $2a = 6$, so $a = 3$.\\n- Constant terms: $-3b = -15$, so $b = 5$.\\n- $x$ terms: $c = 6 - ab = 6 - 3(5) = -9$.\\n\\nChoice B reverses the sign of the result, using $ab - 6$. Choice C subtracts both parts of the middle term, using $-ab - 6$. Choice D adds both parts, using $ab + 6$, which forgets that the $-b$ makes $-abx$ negative.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Chap tomonni ochamiz: $(ax + 3)(2x - b) = 2ax^2 - abx + 6x - 3b = 2ax^2 + (6 - ab)x - 3b$.\\n\\nKoeffitsiyentlarni $6x^2 + cx - 15$ bilan tenglashtiramiz:\\n- $x^2$ hadlari: $2a = 6$, demak $a = 3$.\\n- Ozod hadlar: $-3b = -15$, demak $b = 5$.\\n- $x$ hadlari: $c = 6 - ab = 6 - 3(5) = -9$.\\n\\nB variantda natijaning ishorasi teskari olingan ($ab - 6$). C variantda o‘rta hadning ikkala qismi ham ayirilgan ($-ab - 6$). D variantda ikkala qism qo‘shilgan ($ab + 6$), ya’ni $-b$ tufayli $-abx$ manfiy ekani unutilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"equivalent_expressions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The expression $2x^2 - 12x + 23$ can be written in the form $a(x - h)^2 + k$, where $a$, $h$, and $k$ are constants. What is the value of $a + h + k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"10\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The leading coefficient gives $a = 2$. Factor $2$ out of the $x$ terms: $2x^2 - 12x + 23 = 2(x^2 - 6x) + 23$. Complete the square inside the parentheses by adding and subtracting $9$: $2(x^2 - 6x + 9 - 9) + 23 = 2(x - 3)^2 - 18 + 23 = 2(x - 3)^2 + 5$.\\n\\nSo $a = 2$, $h = 3$, $k = 5$, and $a + h + k = 10$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $19$: it comes from subtracting only $9$ instead of $2 \\\\cdot 9 = 18$ outside the parentheses, which gives $k = 14$. Another is entering $4$, which uses $h = -3$ by misreading the sign in $(x - h)^2$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bosh koeffitsiyentdan $a = 2$. $x$ li hadlardan $2$ ni qavsdan tashqariga chiqaramiz: $2x^2 - 12x + 23 = 2(x^2 - 6x) + 23$. Qavs ichida $9$ ni qo‘shib-ayirib, to‘liq kvadrat ajratamiz: $2(x^2 - 6x + 9 - 9) + 23 = 2(x - 3)^2 - 18 + 23 = 2(x - 3)^2 + 5$.\\n\\nDemak, $a = 2$, $h = 3$, $k = 5$ va $a + h + k = 10$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $19$ ni kiritish: qavs tashqarisida $2 \\\\cdot 9 = 18$ o‘rniga faqat $9$ ayirilsa, $k = 14$ chiqadi. Yana bir xato — $(x - h)^2$ dagi ishorani noto‘g‘ri o‘qib, $h = -3$ olish va $4$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":140,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A fitness app posted a survey for its users. Of the 2,000 users who chose to respond, 80% said they exercise every day. Based on these results, the app's developers claim that about 80% of all adults in the country exercise every day. Which of the following is the best reason this claim is not justified?\",\"option_a\":\"The survey had fewer than 5,000 responses.\",\"option_b\":\"The respondents were app users who chose to respond, so they are not a random sample of all adults in the country.\",\"option_c\":\"Some of the respondents may have exercised more than once a day.\",\"option_d\":\"The survey asked about exercise instead of about diet.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"To generalize to all adults in the country, the sample should be selected at random from that population. Here the respondents were app users (people already interested in fitness) who chose to answer, so the sample is likely biased toward people who exercise. Choice A is not the main problem: 2,000 responses is a large sample, and a larger biased sample is still biased. Choice C does not affect whether someone exercises every day. Choice D is irrelevant to the claim, which is about exercise.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Mamlakatdagi barcha kattalarga umumlashtirish uchun tanlanma shu aholi orasidan tasodifiy tanlanishi kerak. Bu yerda javob berganlar — ilova foydalanuvchilari (sport bilan allaqachon qiziqadigan odamlar) va ular javob berishni o‘zlari tanlagan, shuning uchun tanlanma, ehtimol, mashq qiladiganlar tomon og‘gan. A javob asosiy muammo emas: 2,000 ta javob — katta tanlanma, noxolis tanlanmani kattalashtirish esa uni xolis qilmaydi. C javob odam har kuni mashq qilish-qilmasligiga ta’sir qilmaydi. D javob da’voga aloqasi yo‘q, chunki da’vo mashq haqida.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A researcher selected a random sample of 300 households from a list of all households in Samarkand city. The households in the sample used an average of 210 kilowatt-hours of electricity in January. To which of the following groups can the results of this study most appropriately be generalized?\",\"option_a\":\"Only the 300 households in the sample\",\"option_b\":\"All households in Uzbekistan\",\"option_c\":\"All households in Samarkand city\",\"option_d\":\"All households in the world\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Because the sample was selected at random from all households in Samarkand city, the results can be generalized to that population: all households in Samarkand city. Choice A is too narrow; the purpose of a random sample is to learn about the whole population it was drawn from. Choices B and D are too broad, because households outside Samarkand city had no chance of being selected and may use different amounts of electricity.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlanma Samarqand shahridagi barcha xonadonlar orasidan tasodifiy olingani uchun natijalarni shu aholiga — Samarqand shahridagi barcha xonadonlarga umumlashtirish mumkin. A javob juda tor: tasodifiy tanlanmaning maqsadi — u olingan butun aholi haqida ma’lumot olish. B va D javoblar juda keng, chunki Samarqand shahridan tashqaridagi xonadonlar tanlanish imkoniga ega bo‘lmagan va ular boshqacha miqdorda elektr ishlatishi mumkin.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In an experiment, 120 volunteers with mild back pain were randomly assigned to two groups of 60. One group did a daily stretching routine, and the other group did not. After 4 weeks, 42 people in the stretching group and 27 people in the other group reported less back pain. The percentage of the stretching group who reported less back pain was how many percentage points greater than the percentage of the other group who reported less back pain?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"25\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Stretching group: $\\\\frac{42}{60} = 0.70$, or 70%. Other group: $\\\\frac{27}{60} = 0.45$, or 45%. The difference is $70 - 45 = 25$ percentage points. Because the volunteers were **randomly assigned** to the groups, this difference can reasonably be attributed to the stretching routine for people like these volunteers. Entering 15, the difference in counts $42 - 27$, does not give percentage points. Enter 25.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Cho‘zilish mashqlari guruhi: $\\\\frac{42}{60} = 0.70$, ya’ni 70%. Ikkinchi guruh: $\\\\frac{27}{60} = 0.45$, ya’ni 45%. Farq $70 - 45 = 25$ foiz punkti. Ko‘ngillilar guruhlarga **tasodifiy taqsimlangani** uchun bu farqni shunday ko‘ngillilarga o‘xshash odamlar uchun mashqlar ta’siri deb hisoblash mumkin. 15 (sonlar farqi $42 - 27$) deb yozish foiz punktini bermaydi. Javob maydoniga 25 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A researcher recruited 80 university students who volunteered for a study. The researcher randomly assigned 40 of the students to drink a cup of green tea every day for 8 weeks and the other 40 to drink no green tea. At the end of the study, the students who drank green tea had lower blood pressure, on average, than the students who did not, and the difference was large enough that it is unlikely to be due to chance. Which of the following conclusions is most appropriate?\",\"option_a\":\"Drinking green tea daily causes lower blood pressure for students like those in the study.\",\"option_b\":\"Drinking green tea daily causes lower blood pressure for all adults in the country.\",\"option_c\":\"Drinking green tea daily is associated with lower blood pressure, but no cause-and-effect conclusion can be made.\",\"option_d\":\"No conclusion can be made, because the students were volunteers.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Random assignment to the two groups allows a cause-and-effect conclusion: since the groups were alike except for the tea, the difference in blood pressure can be attributed to the tea. However, the students were volunteers, not a random sample of a larger population, so the conclusion applies only to students like those in the study. Choice B generalizes too far, to a population that was not sampled. Choice C ignores that random assignment supports causation. Choice D is too strong: volunteers limit how far the results generalize, but they do not prevent a conclusion about people like them.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikki guruhga tasodifiy taqsimlash sabab-oqibat xulosasiga imkon beradi: guruhlar choydan tashqari hamma jihatdan o‘xshash bo‘lgani uchun qon bosimidagi farqni choyga bog‘lash mumkin. Ammo talabalar ko‘ngillilar bo‘lgan, kattaroq aholidan tasodifiy tanlanmagan, shuning uchun xulosa faqat tadqiqotdagilarga o‘xshash talabalarga tegishli. B javob xulosani tanlanma olinmagan aholiga juda keng umumlashtirgan. C javob tasodifiy taqsimlash sababiylikni tasdiqlashini e’tiborsiz qoldirgan. D javob haddan tashqari qat’iy: ko‘ngillilik natijalarni qanchalik keng umumlashtirishni cheklaydi, lekin ularga o‘xshash odamlar haqida xulosa chiqarishga to‘sqinlik qilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A researcher surveyed a random sample of 1,000 adults in a region. The adults who reported eating breakfast every day also reported higher energy levels at work, on average, than the adults who reported not eating breakfast every day. Which of the following conclusions is best supported by this study?\",\"option_a\":\"Eating breakfast every day causes adults in the region to have higher energy levels at work.\",\"option_b\":\"Among adults in the region, eating breakfast every day is associated with higher energy levels at work.\",\"option_c\":\"Eating breakfast every day causes higher energy levels at work for adults everywhere.\",\"option_d\":\"The results apply only to the 1,000 adults who were surveyed.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Because the sample was selected at random from adults in the region, the results can be generalized to adults in the region. However, this is an observational study: the adults chose for themselves whether to eat breakfast, so other differences between the groups (such as sleep or work schedules) could explain the result. Therefore the study shows an association, not cause and effect. Choices A and C claim causation, which would require random assignment; choice C also generalizes beyond the region. Choice D is too narrow, since a random sample supports conclusions about the population it was drawn from.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlanma mintaqadagi kattalar orasidan tasodifiy olingani uchun natijalarni mintaqadagi kattalarga umumlashtirish mumkin. Ammo bu kuzatuv tadqiqoti: kattalar nonushta qilish-qilmaslikni o‘zlari tanlagan, shuning uchun guruhlar orasidagi boshqa farqlar (masalan, uyqu yoki ish jadvali) natijani tushuntirishi mumkin. Demak, tadqiqot sabab-oqibatni emas, bog‘liqlikni ko‘rsatadi. A va C javoblar sababiylikni da’vo qiladi, buning uchun esa tasodifiy taqsimlash kerak; C javob bundan tashqari mintaqadan tashqariga umumlashtirgan. D javob juda tor, chunki tasodifiy tanlanma u olingan aholi haqida xulosa chiqarishga imkon beradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A shop owner wants to know how satisfied all of the shop's customers are with its service. On one Saturday morning, the owner asked every 10th customer leaving the shop to rate the service. Which of the following changes would most likely make the results more representative of all of the shop's customers?\",\"option_a\":\"Asking every 5th customer leaving the shop on the same Saturday morning\",\"option_b\":\"Asking only customers who have shopped there for more than a year\",\"option_c\":\"Asking customers who choose to fill out a comment card at the checkout\",\"option_d\":\"Selecting customers at random from those who shop on all days of the week and at all times of day\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Customers who shop on Saturday mornings may differ from customers who shop at other times (for example, in their schedules or in how crowded the shop is when they visit). Selecting customers at random across all days and times gives every customer a chance to be selected, which makes the sample more representative. Choice A increases the sample size but keeps the same Saturday-morning bias. Choice B leaves out newer customers. Choice C creates a voluntary-response sample, which tends to overrepresent customers with strong opinions.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Shanba kuni ertalab xarid qiladigan mijozlar boshqa vaqtlarda keladigan mijozlardan farq qilishi mumkin (masalan, ish jadvali yoki ular kelganda do‘kon qanchalik gavjum ekani bo‘yicha). Haftaning barcha kunlari va kunning barcha vaqtlaridan mijozlarni tasodifiy tanlash har bir mijozga tanlanish imkonini beradi, bu esa tanlanmani vakilliroq qiladi. A javob tanlanma hajmini oshiradi, lekin shanba ertalabi bilan bog‘liq noxolislik saqlanib qoladi. B javob yangi mijozlarni chetda qoldiradi. C javob ixtiyoriy javob tanlanmasini hosil qiladi, unda kuchli fikrga ega mijozlar ortiqcha ulushda bo‘ladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Two studies examined whether listening to music while studying affects test performance.\\n\\nStudy 1: A random sample of 500 high school students in a city was surveyed. Students who reported listening to music while studying had lower test scores, on average, than students who reported studying in silence.\\n\\nStudy 2: A teacher recruited 60 student volunteers from her school and randomly assigned half to study a lesson with music and half to study it in silence. The music group had lower test scores, on average, and the difference was unlikely to be due to chance.\\n\\nWhich of the following statements is best supported by these studies?\",\"option_a\":\"Study 1 shows that listening to music while studying causes lower test scores for high school students in the city.\",\"option_b\":\"Study 2 shows that listening to music while studying causes lower test scores for all high school students in the city.\",\"option_c\":\"Study 1 supports an association that can be generalized to high school students in the city, and Study 2 supports a cause-and-effect conclusion for students like the volunteers.\",\"option_d\":\"Neither study supports any conclusion beyond the students who participated.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Study 1 used random **sampling** but no random assignment, so its association can be generalized to high school students in the city, but it cannot show cause and effect (students chose whether to listen to music). Study 2 used random **assignment** but not random sampling, so it supports a causal conclusion only for students like the volunteers. Choice A claims causation from an observational study. Choice B generalizes a volunteer sample to the whole city. Choice D ignores what each design does allow.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"1-tadqiqotda tasodifiy **tanlash** bor, lekin tasodifiy taqsimlash yo‘q, shuning uchun undagi bog‘liqlikni shahardagi o‘rta maktab o‘quvchilariga umumlashtirish mumkin, ammo sabab-oqibatni ko‘rsatib bo‘lmaydi (musiqa tinglashni o‘quvchilar o‘zlari tanlagan). 2-tadqiqotda tasodifiy **taqsimlash** bor, lekin tasodifiy tanlash yo‘q, shuning uchun u sabab-oqibat xulosasini faqat ko‘ngillilarga o‘xshash o‘quvchilar uchun tasdiqlaydi. A javob kuzatuv tadqiqotidan sababiylik xulosasini chiqargan. B javob ko‘ngillilar tanlanmasini butun shaharga umumlashtirgan. D javob har bir tadqiqot dizayni nimaga imkon berishini e’tiborsiz qoldirgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"evaluating_statistical_claims\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A town has three secondary schools. School A has 420 tenth-grade students, School B has 380 tenth-grade students, and School C has 300 tenth-grade students. A researcher combined the lists of all tenth-grade students at School A and School B and selected 200 students at random from the combined list. No students from School C were selected. To how many students in total can the results of this survey most appropriately be generalized?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"800\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Results from a random sample can be generalized only to the population the sample was drawn from. The sample was drawn at random from the combined list of tenth-grade students at Schools A and B, so that population has $420 + 380 = 800$ students. Students at School C had no chance of being selected, so they are not part of this population. Entering 1100 ($420 + 380 + 300$) incorrectly includes School C, and entering 200 limits the results to the sample itself. Enter 800.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tasodifiy tanlanma natijalarini faqat u olingan aholiga umumlashtirish mumkin. Tanlanma A va B maktablardagi 10-sinf o‘quvchilarining birlashtirilgan ro‘yxatidan tasodifiy olingan, demak bu aholida $420 + 380 = 800$ nafar o‘quvchi bor. C maktab o‘quvchilari tanlanish imkoniga ega bo‘lmagan, shuning uchun ular bu aholiga kirmaydi. 1100 ($420 + 380 + 300$) deb yozish C maktabni noto‘g‘ri qo‘shadi, 200 esa natijalarni faqat tanlanmaning o‘zi bilan cheklaydi. Javob maydoniga 800 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Archaeologists working near the city of Termez have uncovered a small clay jar filled with ancient silver coins. Each of the coins ______ a portrait of a ruler on one side and a horse on the other.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"shows\",\"option_b\":\"show\",\"option_c\":\"are showing\",\"option_d\":\"have shown\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The subject of the verb is “Each,” which is singular; “of the coins” is a prepositional phrase that does not change the number of the subject. A singular subject needs a singular verb, so “shows” is correct.\\n\\nChoices B, C and D are all plural verb forms (“show,” “are showing,” “have shown”), which would agree with “coins” rather than with the actual subject, “Each.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kesimning egasi — “Each” (har biri), u birlikda. “Of the coins” predlogli birikma bo‘lib, eganing sonini o‘zgartirmaydi. Birlikdagi egaga birlikdagi kesim kerak, shuning uchun “shows” to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nB, C va D — ko‘plikdagi fe’l shakllari (“show”, “are showing”, “have shown”); ular haqiqiy ega “Each” bilan emas, “coins” bilan moslashgan bo‘lardi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Researchers placed motion-activated cameras along a mountain ridge to study the five snow leopards that live there. By comparing the ______ routes over several months, they learned that the animals rarely used the same paths at the same time.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"cat's\",\"option_b\":\"cats\",\"option_c\":\"cats's\",\"option_d\":\"cats'\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The routes belong to the five snow leopards, so the blank needs a plural possessive. The plural noun is “cats,” and a plural noun ending in “s” forms its possessive by adding only an apostrophe: “cats'.”\\n\\nChoice A, “cat's,” is singular possessive, but the text discusses five animals. Choice B, “cats,” is plural but not possessive, so it cannot show that the routes belong to the cats. Choice C, “cats's,” is not a standard form.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Yo‘nalishlar beshta qor qoploniga tegishli, shuning uchun bo‘sh joyga ko‘plikdagi qaratqich (egalik) shakli kerak. Ko‘plik shakli “cats”, “s” bilan tugaydigan ko‘plikdagi ot egalik shaklini faqat apostrof qo‘shib hosil qiladi: “cats'”.\\n\\nA — “cat's” birlikdagi egalik shakli, matnda esa beshta hayvon haqida gap boradi. B — “cats” ko‘plikda, lekin egalikni bildirmaydi. C — “cats's” standart shakl emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In 1957, the Soviet Union ______ Sputnik 1, the first artificial satellite, into orbit around Earth. The small metal sphere sent radio signals back to the ground for about three weeks.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"launches\",\"option_b\":\"will launch\",\"option_c\":\"launched\",\"option_d\":\"has launched\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text describes an event that was completed at a specific time in the past, “In 1957,” and the next sentence uses the past tense (“sent”). The simple past tense, “launched,” is therefore correct.\\n\\nChoice A is present tense and choice B is future tense; neither fits an event in 1957. Choice D, the present perfect “has launched,” is not used with a specific completed past time such as “In 1957.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda o‘tmishda aniq bir vaqtda — “In 1957” yilda — tugallangan voqea tasvirlanadi, keyingi gapda ham o‘tgan zamon (“sent”) ishlatilgan. Shuning uchun oddiy o‘tgan zamon “launched” to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nA — hozirgi zamon, B — kelasi zamon; ikkalasi ham 1957 yildagi voqeaga mos kelmaydi. D — “has launched” (present perfect) “In 1957” kabi aniq o‘tgan vaqt bilan ishlatilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The sand dunes of the Kyzylkum Desert may look permanent, but strong winds constantly reshape ______, moving some of the largest dunes several meters each year.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"it\",\"option_b\":\"them\",\"option_c\":\"its\",\"option_d\":\"itself\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The pronoun refers to “The sand dunes,” a plural noun, and it is the object of the verb “reshape.” The plural object pronoun “them” is therefore correct.\\n\\nChoice A, “it,” is singular and does not agree with “dunes.” Choice C, “its,” is a possessive form and cannot serve as the object of “reshape” on its own. Choice D, “itself,” is a singular reflexive pronoun, which would wrongly suggest that the winds reshape themselves.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Olmosh ko‘plikdagi “The sand dunes” (qum barxanlari) otiga ishora qiladi va “reshape” fe’lining to‘ldiruvchisi vazifasida keladi. Shuning uchun ko‘plikdagi obyekt olmoshi “them” to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nA — “it” birlikda, “dunes” bilan moslashmaydi. C — “its” egalik shakli va o‘zi yolg‘iz “reshape” ning to‘ldiruvchisi bo‘la olmaydi. D — “itself” birlikdagi o‘zlik olmoshi bo‘lib, shamollar o‘zini o‘zi o‘zgartiradi degan noto‘g‘ri ma’noni beradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Flowing more than 2,000 kilometers from the mountains of Kyrgyzstan to the remains of the Aral Sea, ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"farmers and cities along its banks have long depended on the Syr Darya for water.\",\"option_b\":\"the Syr Darya's banks have long been home to farms and cities that depend on its water.\",\"option_c\":\"the Syr Darya has long supplied water to farms and cities along its banks.\",\"option_d\":\"people have long used the Syr Darya to supply their farms and cities with water.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The introductory phrase “Flowing more than 2,000 kilometers from the mountains of Kyrgyzstan to the remains of the Aral Sea” describes a river. A modifying phrase like this must be placed directly before the noun it describes, so the sentence must continue with “the Syr Darya,” as in choice C.\\n\\nChoice A makes it seem that the farmers and cities flow 2,000 kilometers. Choice B makes the modifier describe “the Syr Darya's banks,” which do not flow, and in choice D the modifier describes “people.” Each of these is a dangling modifier.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“Flowing more than 2,000 kilometers from the mountains of Kyrgyzstan to the remains of the Aral Sea” kirish iborasi daryoni tasvirlaydi. Bunday aniqlovchi ibora o‘zi tasvirlayotgan otdan darhol oldin kelishi kerak, shuning uchun gap C dagidek “the Syr Darya” bilan davom etishi lozim.\\n\\nA — go‘yo dehqonlar va shaharlar 2000 kilometr oqib o‘tgandek ko‘rsatadi. B — iborani daryoning o‘ziga emas, oqmaydigan “the Syr Darya's banks” (qirg‘oqlar) ga bog‘laydi, D da esa ibora “people” ni tasvirlaydi. Bularning har biri “dangling modifier” (osilib qolgan aniqlovchi) xatosi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Hidden in a narrow canyon in the mountains of southern Uzbekistan is a shallow rock shelter. Along its back wall ______ dozens of red-brown paintings of hunters, wild bulls, and dogs, some of which may be thousands of years old.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"are\",\"option_b\":\"is\",\"option_c\":\"was\",\"option_d\":\"has been\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"This sentence is inverted: the subject, “dozens of red-brown paintings,” comes after the verb. Because the subject is plural, the verb must be plural, so “are” is correct. The present tense also matches the surrounding text (“is a shallow rock shelter”).\\n\\nChoices B, C and D are all singular verbs (“is,” “was,” “has been”), which might seem to agree with the nearby singular noun “wall,” but “wall” is part of the prepositional phrase “Along its back wall,” not the subject.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bu gapda so‘z tartibi teskari: ega — “dozens of red-brown paintings” — kesimdan keyin keladi. Ega ko‘plikda bo‘lgani uchun kesim ham ko‘plikda bo‘lishi kerak, shuning uchun “are” to‘g‘ri. Hozirgi zamon matnning qolgan qismiga (“is a shallow rock shelter”) ham mos keladi.\\n\\nB, C va D — birlikdagi fe’llar (“is”, “was”, “has been”). Ular yaqindagi birlikdagi “wall” so‘zi bilan moslashgandek tuyulishi mumkin, ammo “wall” ega emas, “Along its back wall” predlogli birikmasining qismi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The climbers spent the morning waiting out high winds at their camp below the summit. If the team had left camp just an hour earlier, it ______ the peak before the storm arrived and been back in camp by nightfall.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"will reach\",\"option_b\":\"would have reached\",\"option_c\":\"reaches\",\"option_d\":\"would reach\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sentence describes an unreal past situation: the team did not leave an hour earlier. The “if” clause uses the past perfect (“had left”), so the result clause needs “would have” plus a past participle. The sentence also continues with “and been back in camp,” which only works with “would have … been,” confirming that “would have reached” is correct.\\n\\nChoice A, “will reach,” is used for real future possibilities, not imagined past ones. Choice C, “reaches,” is present tense. Choice D, “would reach,” refers to an imagined present or future result, and it cannot combine with “and been back in camp.”\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gap o‘tmishdagi real bo‘lmagan vaziyatni tasvirlaydi: guruh bir soat oldin yo‘lga chiqmagan. “If” qismida past perfect (“had left”) ishlatilgan, shuning uchun natija qismiga “would have” + uchinchi shakl (past participle) kerak. Gap “and been back in camp” bilan davom etadi, bu faqat “would have … been” bilan mos keladi — bu “would have reached” to‘g‘ri ekanini tasdiqlaydi.\\n\\nA — “will reach” real kelajakdagi imkoniyatlar uchun ishlatiladi, o‘tmishdagi xayoliy vaziyat uchun emas. C — “reaches” hozirgi zamon. D — “would reach” hozirgi yoki kelajakdagi xayoliy natijani bildiradi va “and been back in camp” bilan birika olmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"form_structure_sense\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The collection of letters, diaries, and travel sketches that the nineteenth-century explorer left to the national library ______ historians a rare look at daily life along the caravan routes of Central Asia.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\",\"option_a\":\"offer\",\"option_b\":\"have offered\",\"option_c\":\"are offering\",\"option_d\":\"offers\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The subject of the sentence is “The collection,” which is singular. Everything between “collection” and the blank (“of letters, diaries, and travel sketches that the nineteenth-century explorer left to the national library”) is a modifier that does not change the subject's number. A singular subject needs a singular verb, so “offers” is correct.\\n\\nChoices A, B and C are plural forms (“offer,” “have offered,” “are offering”). They are tempting because the plural nouns “letters,” “diaries” and “sketches” appear near the blank, but none of those nouns is the subject.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gapning egasi — birlikdagi “The collection” (to‘plam). “Collection” va bo‘sh joy orasidagi hamma narsa (“of letters, diaries, and travel sketches that the nineteenth-century explorer left to the national library”) aniqlovchi bo‘lib, eganing sonini o‘zgartirmaydi. Birlikdagi egaga birlikdagi kesim kerak, shuning uchun “offers” to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nA, B va C — ko‘plik shakllari (“offer”, “have offered”, “are offering”). Ular jozibali, chunki bo‘sh joy yaqinida ko‘plikdagi “letters”, “diaries” va “sketches” otlari bor, ammo bu otlarning hech biri ega emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A random sample of 400 high school students in a region was asked whether they plan to study at a university after graduating. Based on the sample, it is estimated that 62% of all high school students in the region plan to study at a university, with a margin of error of 5 percentage points. Which of the following gives the plausible values for the percentage of all high school students in the region who plan to study at a university?\",\"option_a\":\"From 60% to 64%\",\"option_b\":\"From 57% to 67%\",\"option_c\":\"From 52% to 72%\",\"option_d\":\"From 62% to 67%\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The plausible values are the estimate plus or minus the margin of error: $62 - 5 = 57$ and $62 + 5 = 67$, so from 57% to 67%. Choice D adds the margin of error but does not subtract it. Choice C uses twice the margin of error on each side. Choice A uses a margin of error of only 2 percentage points.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ishonchli qiymatlar — baho plyus-minus xatolik chegarasi: $62 - 5 = 57$ va $62 + 5 = 67$, ya’ni 57% dan 67% gacha. D javob xatolik chegarasini qo‘shgan, lekin ayirmagan. C javob har tomonga xatolik chegarasining ikki baravarini olgan. A javob xatolik chegarasini atigi 2 foiz punkti deb olgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A shipment contains 3,000 boxes of tomatoes. An inspector selected a random sample of 120 boxes from the shipment and found that 9 of the sampled boxes contained damaged tomatoes. Based on the sample, what is the best estimate of the number of boxes in the entire shipment that contain damaged tomatoes?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"225\"],\"explanation_en\":\"In the sample, $\\\\frac{9}{120} = 0.075$, or 7.5%, of the boxes contained damaged tomatoes. Because the sample was selected at random, the same proportion is the best estimate for the whole shipment: $0.075 \\\\times 3{,}000 = 225$ boxes. Entering 9 gives only the number in the sample. Enter 225.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlanmadagi qutilarning $\\\\frac{9}{120} = 0.075$ qismida, ya’ni 7.5% ida shikastlangan pomidor bo‘lgan. Tanlanma tasodifiy olingani uchun butun partiya uchun eng yaxshi baho ham shu ulush: $0.075 \\\\times 3{,}000 = 225$ quti. 9 deb yozish faqat tanlanmadagi sonni beradi. Javob maydoniga 225 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A random sample of 250 adults in a city was asked how much water they drink each day. The sample mean was 2.1 liters, with an associated margin of error of 0.3 liter. Which of the following is a plausible value for the mean amount of water, in liters, that all adults in the city drink each day?\",\"option_a\":\"$1.6$\",\"option_b\":\"$1.75$\",\"option_c\":\"$2.25$\",\"option_d\":\"$2.5$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Plausible values for the population mean lie from $2.1 - 0.3 = 1.8$ liters to $2.1 + 0.3 = 2.4$ liters. Of the choices, only 2.25 is between 1.8 and 2.4. Choices A and B are less than 1.8, and choice D is greater than 2.4, so they are outside the interval of plausible values.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Aholi o‘rta qiymati uchun ishonchli qiymatlar $2.1 - 0.3 = 1.8$ litrdan $2.1 + 0.3 = 2.4$ litrgacha. Javoblardan faqat 2.25 1.8 va 2.4 orasida. A va B javoblar 1.8 dan kichik, D javob esa 2.4 dan katta, demak ular ishonchli qiymatlar oralig‘idan tashqarida.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A random sample of voters in a city was asked whether they support a plan to build a new stadium. Based on the sample, it is estimated that 47% of all voters in the city support the plan, with a margin of error of 4 percentage points. Which of the following conclusions is best supported by these results?\",\"option_a\":\"Fewer than half of all voters in the city support the plan.\",\"option_b\":\"Exactly 47% of all voters in the city support the plan.\",\"option_c\":\"It is plausible that more than half of all voters in the city support the plan, and it is also plausible that fewer than half do.\",\"option_d\":\"More than half of all voters in the city support the plan.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The plausible values for the percentage of all voters who support the plan are from $47 - 4 = 43\\\\%$ to $47 + 4 = 51\\\\%$. This interval includes values below 50% and values above 50%, so the results do not show whether a majority supports the plan; both possibilities are plausible. Choice A is too certain, because values from 50% to 51% are plausible. Choice B treats the sample estimate as the exact population value. Choice D is not supported, because most of the plausible values are below 50%.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Rejani qo‘llab-quvvatlovchi saylovchilar foizi uchun ishonchli qiymatlar $47 - 4 = 43\\\\%$ dan $47 + 4 = 51\\\\%$ gacha. Bu oraliqda 50% dan kichik va 50% dan katta qiymatlar bor, shuning uchun natijalar ko‘pchilik rejani qo‘llashini ham, qo‘llamasligini ham isbotlamaydi — ikkala holat ham ishonchli. A javob haddan tashqari qat’iy, chunki 50% dan 51% gacha bo‘lgan qiymatlar ham ishonchli. B javob tanlanma bahosini aholining aniq qiymati deb olgan. D javob asoslanmagan, chunki ishonchli qiymatlarning aksariyati 50% dan kichik.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A random sample of 90 smartphones of one model was tested to estimate the mean battery life, in hours, of all smartphones of that model. Based on the sample, plausible values for the mean battery life of all smartphones of that model are from 18.4 hours to 19.2 hours. What is the margin of error, in hours, associated with this estimate?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"0.4\",\".4\",\"2/5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The interval of plausible values is centered at the estimate and extends the margin of error on each side. The estimate is the midpoint, $\\\\frac{18.4 + 19.2}{2} = 18.8$ hours, and the margin of error is half the width of the interval: $\\\\frac{19.2 - 18.4}{2} = 0.4$ hour. Entering 0.8, the full width of the interval, double-counts the margin of error. Enter 0.4, .4, or 2/5.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ishonchli qiymatlar oralig‘ining markazi — baho, u har tomonga xatolik chegarasi miqdorida cho‘ziladi. Baho — o‘rta nuqta: $\\\\frac{18.4 + 19.2}{2} = 18.8$ soat, xatolik chegarasi esa oraliq kengligining yarmi: $\\\\frac{19.2 - 18.4}{2} = 0.4$ soat. 0.8 (oraliqning to‘liq kengligi) deb yozish xatolik chegarasini ikki marta hisoblash bo‘ladi. Javob maydoniga 0.4, .4 yoki 2/5 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A researcher plans to estimate the mean number of hours per week that students at a large university spend on homework. Which of the following changes to the study would most likely produce an estimate with a **smaller** margin of error, assuming the same method and confidence level are used?\",\"option_a\":\"Selecting a larger random sample of students from the university\",\"option_b\":\"Selecting a smaller random sample of students from the university\",\"option_c\":\"Surveying only students who volunteer to answer an online form\",\"option_d\":\"Surveying only students who live in one dormitory\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"When everything else stays the same, a larger random sample tends to give a smaller margin of error, because estimates from larger samples vary less from sample to sample. Choice B would tend to **increase** the margin of error. Choices C and D create samples that are not random and may be biased; a biased sample does not give a more trustworthy estimate of the whole university's mean.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Boshqa shartlar o‘zgarmaganda, kattaroq tasodifiy tanlanma odatda kichikroq xatolik chegarasini beradi, chunki katta tanlanmalardan olingan baholar bir tanlanmadan boshqasiga kamroq o‘zgaradi. B javob xatolik chegarasini odatda **oshiradi**. C va D javoblar tasodifiy bo‘lmagan, noxolis bo‘lishi mumkin bo‘lgan tanlanmalarni hosil qiladi; noxolis tanlanma butun universitet o‘rta qiymati uchun ishonchliroq baho bermaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Researchers estimated the mean daily screen time of teenagers in two cities. A random sample of teenagers was selected in each city. In City A, the sample mean was 7.2 hours, with a margin of error of 0.5 hour. In City B, the sample mean was 6.3 hours, with a margin of error of 0.3 hour. Which of the following statements is best supported by these results?\",\"option_a\":\"The mean daily screen time of all teenagers in City A is exactly 0.9 hour greater than in City B.\",\"option_b\":\"It is plausible that the mean daily screen time of all teenagers in City A is equal to that of all teenagers in City B.\",\"option_c\":\"The estimate for City B is less accurate than the estimate for City A because its margin of error is smaller.\",\"option_d\":\"The mean daily screen time of all teenagers in City A is likely greater than that of all teenagers in City B.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Plausible values for City A are from $7.2 - 0.5 = 6.7$ to $7.2 + 0.5 = 7.7$ hours; for City B they are from $6.3 - 0.3 = 6.0$ to $6.3 + 0.3 = 6.6$ hours. The intervals do not overlap, and every plausible value for City A is greater than every plausible value for City B, so City A's mean is likely greater. Choice B is wrong because no value is plausible for both cities. Choice A treats the sample means as exact population values. Choice C is backward: a smaller margin of error indicates a more precise estimate.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"A shahar uchun ishonchli qiymatlar $7.2 - 0.5 = 6.7$ dan $7.2 + 0.5 = 7.7$ soatgacha; B shahar uchun $6.3 - 0.3 = 6.0$ dan $6.3 + 0.3 = 6.6$ soatgacha. Oraliqlar kesishmaydi va A shahar uchun har bir ishonchli qiymat B shahar uchun har bir ishonchli qiymatdan katta, demak A shahardagi o‘rta qiymat katta bo‘lishi ehtimoli yuqori. B javob noto‘g‘ri, chunki ikkala shahar uchun ham ishonchli bo‘lgan qiymat yo‘q. A javob tanlanma o‘rta qiymatlarini aholining aniq qiymatlari deb olgan. C javob teskari: kichikroq xatolik chegarasi aniqroq bahoni bildiradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inference_margin_of_error\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A town has 15,000 households. A random sample of the town's households was surveyed, and based on the sample, it is estimated that 38% of all households in the town own a bicycle. When the margin of error is applied to this estimate, the least plausible number of households in the town that own a bicycle is 5,100. What is the margin of error, in percentage points, associated with the estimate?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Convert the least plausible number to a percentage of all households: $\\\\frac{5{,}100}{15{,}000} = 0.34$, or 34%. The least plausible percentage is the estimate minus the margin of error, so $38 - m = 34$ and $m = 4$ percentage points. Entering 34 gives the least plausible percentage, not the margin of error. Entering 600 gives the difference in numbers of households, $0.38 \\\\times 15{,}000 - 5{,}100 = 5{,}700 - 5{,}100$, rather than percentage points. Enter 4.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Eng kichik ishonchli sonni barcha xonadonlarga nisbatan foizga aylantiramiz: $\\\\frac{5{,}100}{15{,}000} = 0.34$, ya’ni 34%. Eng kichik ishonchli foiz — baho minus xatolik chegarasi, demak $38 - m = 34$ va $m = 4$ foiz punkti. 34 deb yozish xatolik chegarasini emas, eng kichik ishonchli foizni beradi. 600 deb yozish foiz punktini emas, xonadonlar soni farqini beradi: $0.38 \\\\times 15{,}000 - 5{,}100 = 5{,}700 - 5{,}100$. Javob maydoniga 4 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Gardeners in the village of Terek noticed that deer ate the lettuce in almost every garden except those surrounded by rows of garlic. Once the garlic had been harvested in midsummer, however, deer began eating the lettuce in those gardens as well. This suggests that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"deer prefer the taste of garlic to the taste of lettuce.\",\"option_b\":\"lettuce grown next to garlic tastes better to people.\",\"option_c\":\"gardens without garlic produce more lettuce than gardens with garlic.\",\"option_d\":\"the growing garlic helped keep deer away from the lettuce.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Deer avoided the lettuce only in gardens surrounded by garlic and began eating it there once the garlic was harvested. The most logical conclusion is that the garlic itself kept the deer away, as choice D says.\\n\\nChoice A contradicts the text: the deer stayed away from gardens with garlic rather than eating it. Choice B concerns people's taste, which the text never mentions. Choice C is unsupported: the text describes which gardens deer ate from, not how much lettuce each garden produced.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bug‘ular faqat sarimsoq bilan o‘ralgan bog‘lardagi salatga tegmagan, sarimsoq yig‘ib olingach esa u yerdagi salatni ham yeya boshlagan. Eng mantiqiy xulosa — bug‘ularni sarimsoqning o‘zi uzoqlashtirib turgan. To‘g‘ri javob — D.\\n\\nA matnga zid: bug‘ular sarimsoqni yemagan, aksincha, sarimsoqli bog‘lardan uzoq turgan. B odamlarning ta’mi haqida, matnda bu haqda gap yo‘q. C asossiz: matnda qaysi bog‘dagi salat qancha hosil bergani emas, bug‘ular qaysi bog‘dan oziqlangani aytiladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In a letter written in 1903, the traveler Ines Morrow described a tall tower of black stone standing beside the village of Kelt. No such tower stands there today. However, the walls of Kelt's schoolhouse, built in 1925, are made of a black stone that matches no rock found in the surrounding hills, and local records show no black stone being brought to the village from elsewhere. Taken together, these facts suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Morrow never actually visited the village of Kelt.\",\"option_b\":\"the tower had been destroyed by an earthquake before 1903.\",\"option_c\":\"the stone used to build Kelt's schoolhouse may have come from the tower that Morrow described.\",\"option_d\":\"black stone was quarried in the hills around Kelt in the 1920s.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"A black stone tower stood in Kelt in 1903 and is gone today; the 1925 schoolhouse is built of black stone that does not come from the local hills and was not brought from elsewhere. The most logical explanation is that the schoolhouse was built with stone from the vanished tower, as choice C says.\\n\\nChoice A is unsupported: nothing in the text casts doubt on Morrow's visit. Choice B contradicts the text, since Morrow saw the tower standing in 1903. Choice D contradicts the statement that the stone matches no rock found in the surrounding hills.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"1903-yilda Keltda qora toshdan qurilgan minora bo‘lgan, bugun esa u yo‘q; 1925-yilda qurilgan maktab esa mahalliy tepaliklarda uchramaydigan va boshqa joydan keltirilmagan qora toshdan qurilgan. Eng mantiqiy izoh — maktab yo‘qolgan minoraning toshidan qurilgan. To‘g‘ri javob — C.\\n\\nA asossiz: matnda Morrowning tashrifiga shubha uyg‘otadigan hech narsa yo‘q. B matnga zid, chunki Morrow minorani 1903-yilda tik turgan holda ko‘rgan. D tosh atrofdagi tepaliklardagi hech qaysi jinsga o‘xshamasligi haqidagi gapga zid.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Chemist Sevara Ortiqova tested a new paint designed to protect metal. She painted one half of each of twenty steel plates, left the other half bare, and placed all the plates outdoors for a year. At the end of the year, the bare half of every plate was heavily rusted, while the painted half showed little or no rust. These results suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the new paint helps protect steel from rusting.\",\"option_b\":\"steel rusts more slowly outdoors than indoors.\",\"option_c\":\"the new paint gradually weakens the steel beneath it.\",\"option_d\":\"rain has little effect on how quickly steel rusts.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Each plate had a painted half and a bare half exposed to the same conditions, and only the bare halves rusted heavily. This suggests that the paint helps prevent rust, as choice A says.\\n\\nChoice B is unsupported because no plates were kept indoors for comparison. Choice C is unsupported: the text reports nothing about the strength of the steel. Choice D is unsupported: the experiment did not test the effect of rain.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir plastinaning bo‘yalgan va bo‘yalmagan yarmi bir xil sharoitda turgan va faqat bo‘yalmagan yarmi qattiq zanglagan. Bu bo‘yoq zanglashning oldini olishga yordam berishini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB asossiz, chunki solishtirish uchun hech qaysi plastina xonada saqlanmagan. C asossiz: matnda po‘latning mustahkamligi haqida hech narsa aytilmagan. D ham asossiz: tajribada yomg‘irning ta’siri sinab ko‘rilmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In 2021, the city of Pellam began charging drivers a fee to enter its downtown area on weekdays but not on weekends. Over the following year, weekday car traffic downtown fell by 18 percent, while weekend traffic stayed about the same as before. Meanwhile, downtown shops reported that their weekday sales were about the same as in the year before the fee. These findings suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the fee caused many shoppers to move their downtown visits from weekdays to weekends.\",\"option_b\":\"the drop in weekday car traffic downtown did not harm downtown shops' weekday business.\",\"option_c\":\"the fee did not reduce the number of cars entering downtown on weekdays.\",\"option_d\":\"downtown shops raised their prices to make up for customers lost because of the fee.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Weekday car traffic fell by 18 percent, yet weekday sales at downtown shops stayed about the same. This suggests that the reduced driving did not hurt shops' weekday business, as choice B says.\\n\\nChoice A is unlikely: weekend traffic did not rise and weekday sales did not fall, so there is no sign that shoppers shifted to weekends. Choice C contradicts the reported 18 percent drop in weekday traffic. Choice D is unsupported: the text never mentions prices, and stable sales give no reason to think customers were lost.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ish kunlaridagi avtomobil harakati 18 foizga kamaygan, lekin markazdagi do‘konlarning ish kunlaridagi savdosi deyarli o‘zgarmagan. Bu harakatning kamayishi do‘konlarning ish kunlaridagi savdosiga zarar yetkazmaganini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA ehtimoldan yiroq: dam olish kunlaridagi harakat oshmagan, ish kunlaridagi savdo ham kamaymagan, demak xaridorlar dam olish kunlariga o‘tgani haqida belgi yo‘q. C ish kunlaridagi harakat 18 foizga kamaygani haqidagi ma’lumotga zid. D asossiz: matnda narxlar tilga olinmagan, barqaror savdo esa xaridorlar yo‘qotilganini o‘ylashga asos bermaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Archaeologists excavating Darsa, an ancient settlement located about 300 kilometers from the sea, found the bones of several fish species that live only in salt water. Cut marks on the bones match those made when fish are split open for drying and salting, a common way of preserving fish for long journeys. The archaeologists also found pottery made in the style of coastal towns but no fishing equipment of any kind. These findings suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"Darsa was once located on the coast before the sea retreated.\",\"option_b\":\"the people of Darsa made their own fishing equipment from materials that do not survive.\",\"option_c\":\"saltwater fish were the main source of food for the people of Darsa.\",\"option_d\":\"the people of Darsa obtained preserved saltwater fish through contact with communities near the coast.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Darsa is far inland, the fish bones show signs of preservation for long journeys, coastal-style pottery was found there, and there is no fishing equipment. Together these clues point to fish being brought from the coast, as choice D says.\\n\\nChoice A is unsupported, and the preservation marks suggest the fish traveled a long way rather than being caught nearby. Choice B is speculation that the text gives no reason for; the evidence points to fish arriving already preserved. Choice C goes too far: the text shows that some saltwater fish were eaten, not that they were the main food.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Darsa dengizdan ancha uzoqda joylashgan, baliq suyaklarida uzoq yo‘lga saqlash uchun ishlov berilganini ko‘rsatuvchi izlar bor, u yerda sohil shaharlari uslubidagi sopol idishlar topilgan, baliq ovlash anjomlari esa yo‘q. Bu dalillar baliq sohildan keltirilganini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA asossiz; bundan tashqari, saqlash izlari baliq yaqin joyda ovlanmay, uzoq yo‘l bosganini bildiradi. B matnda asosi bo‘lmagan taxmin; dalillar baliq allaqachon saqlashga tayyorlangan holda kelganini ko‘rsatadi. C haddan oshib ketadi: matn dengiz baliqlari iste’mol qilinganini ko‘rsatadi, ular asosiy ozuqa bo‘lganini emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Biologist Zarina Ahmedova trained bumblebees to find sugar water in a blue artificial flower placed among yellow flowers that held only plain water. When she moved the blue flower to a different position each day, the bees continued to find it quickly. But when she put the sugar water in a yellow flower and filled the blue flower with plain water, the bees still flew to the blue flower first. This suggests that the bees ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"relied more on the flower's color than on its position to find the sugar water.\",\"option_b\":\"were unable to tell blue flowers from yellow ones.\",\"option_c\":\"preferred plain water to sugar water.\",\"option_d\":\"remembered the position of the sugar water but not the color of its flower.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The bees found the blue flower even when its position changed, and they kept flying to it first after the sugar water was moved to a yellow flower. Both results show that they were tracking the color blue rather than a location, as choice A says.\\n\\nChoice B contradicts the results, since the bees consistently picked out the blue flower among yellow ones. Choice C is unsupported: the bees went to the blue flower because they had learned it held sugar water. Choice D reverses the finding: the bees followed the color, not the position.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Arilar ko‘k gul joyi o‘zgarganda ham uni topgan, shakarli suv sariq gulga o‘tkazilgandan keyin ham birinchi bo‘lib ko‘k gulga uchgan. Ikkala natija ham arilar joyni emas, ko‘k rangni kuzatganini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB natijalarga zid, chunki arilar sariq gullar orasidan ko‘k gulni doim ajratib olgan. C asossiz: arilar ko‘k gulga unda shakarli suv borligini o‘rgangani uchun borgan. D topilmani teskari qiladi: arilar joyga emas, rangga ergashgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The large townhouse that the merchant Pieter Vandell built in 1652 is often cited as evidence of how profitable the spice trade was for merchants in the port of Haldern. Yet Vandell's surviving account books show that his trading profits during the 1640s were smaller than those of most other Haldern merchants, many of whom lived in modest homes. The account books also record that in 1651, his wife, Margriet, received a large inheritance from her father, a wealthy landowner. These records suggest that ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the spice trade was unprofitable for nearly all Haldern merchants during the 1640s.\",\"option_b\":\"Vandell's townhouse may be weak evidence of the spice trade's profitability, since the money to build it may have come largely from Margriet's inheritance.\",\"option_c\":\"Vandell recorded smaller profits in his account books than he actually earned.\",\"option_d\":\"most Haldern merchants who earned large profits from the spice trade built large townhouses.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The townhouse is cited as a sign of spice-trade wealth, but Vandell's trade profits were below average, and his wife received a large inheritance the year before the house was built. This suggests the house may have been paid for mainly with inherited money, so it may say little about the spice trade, as choice B says.\\n\\nChoice A goes too far: the text says other merchants earned more than Vandell, which does not mean the trade was unprofitable. Choice C has no support; nothing suggests that the account books are inaccurate. Choice D conflicts with the text, which says that many of the merchants who earned more than Vandell lived in modest homes.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Uy ziravorlar savdosidan kelgan boylik belgisi sifatida keltiriladi, ammo Vandellning savdo foydasi o‘rtachadan past bo‘lgan, rafiqasi esa uy qurilishidan bir yil oldin katta meros olgan. Bu uy asosan meros puli hisobiga qurilgan bo‘lishi mumkinligini, demak u ziravorlar savdosi haqida kam narsa aytishini ko‘rsatadi — to‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA haddan oshib ketadi: matnda boshqa savdogarlar Vandelldan ko‘proq foyda ko‘rgani aytilgan, bu savdo foydasiz bo‘lganini anglatmaydi. C asossiz: hisob daftarlari noto‘g‘ri ekani haqida hech qanday ishora yo‘q. D matnga zid: Vandelldan ko‘p topgan savdogarlarning ko‘pchiligi oddiy uylarda yashagani aytilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"inferences\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"In 2022, the weekly farmers' market in the town of Brisk moved from a small downtown square to a larger lot at the edge of town. The number of vendors rose from 40 to 65, but total sales for the market as a whole were nearly the same in 2022 as in 2021. Many of the original 40 vendors reported lower sales after the move and blamed the new site's distance from downtown. However, because the market's total sales barely changed, ______\",\"stem\":\"Which choice most logically completes the text?\",\"option_a\":\"the new location must have attracted far more customers than the old one did.\",\"option_b\":\"the new vendors probably sold less, on average, than the original vendors did.\",\"option_c\":\"the original vendors' lower sales may be explained largely by competition from the new vendors rather than by a loss of customers.\",\"option_d\":\"the move to the edge of town must have caused the market's total sales to decline.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"If total spending at the market stayed about the same while 25 new vendors joined, the same money was divided among more sellers. That would lower the original vendors' sales even if no customers were lost, so the move's distance from downtown need not be the cause. Choice C draws this conclusion.\\n\\nChoice A is unsupported: unchanged total sales do not show that more customers came. Choice B is unsupported: the text gives no figures comparing new and original vendors. Choice D contradicts the statement that total sales barely changed.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Agar bozordagi umumiy xarajat deyarli o‘zgarmagan holda 25 ta yangi sotuvchi qo‘shilgan bo‘lsa, o‘sha pul ko‘proq sotuvchi o‘rtasida taqsimlangan. Bu hatto xaridorlar kamaymagan taqdirda ham eski sotuvchilarning savdosini kamaytiradi, ya’ni sabab yangi joyning markazdan uzoqligi bo‘lmasligi mumkin. C javob aynan shu xulosani chiqaradi.\\n\\nA asossiz: umumiy savdo o‘zgarmagani ko‘proq xaridor kelganini isbotlamaydi. B asossiz: matnda yangi va eski sotuvchilarni solishtiruvchi raqamlar yo‘q. D umumiy savdo deyarli o‘zgarmagani haqidagi gapga zid.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What value of $x$ is the solution to the equation $4(x - 3) = 2x + 10$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-1$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{11}{3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{13}{2}$\",\"option_d\":\"$11$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute the $4$: $4x - 12 = 2x + 10$. Subtract $2x$ from both sides: $2x - 12 = 10$. Add $12$ to both sides: $2x = 22$, so $x = 11$.\\n\\nCheck: $4(11 - 3) = 32$ and $2(11) + 10 = 32$.\\n\\nChoice C comes from multiplying only $x$ by $4$, which gives $4x - 3 = 2x + 10$. Choice A comes from subtracting $12$ instead of adding it ($2x = 10 - 12$). Choice B comes from adding $2x$ to the left side instead of subtracting it ($6x = 22$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$4$ ni qavs ichidagi har bir hadga ko‘paytiramiz: $4x - 12 = 2x + 10$. Ikkala tomondan $2x$ ni ayiramiz: $2x - 12 = 10$. Ikkala tomonga $12$ ni qo‘shamiz: $2x = 22$, demak $x = 11$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $4(11 - 3) = 32$ va $2(11) + 10 = 32$.\\n\\nC variant faqat $x$ ni $4$ ga ko‘paytirishdan kelib chiqadi: $4x - 3 = 2x + 10$. A variant $12$ ni qo‘shish o‘rniga ayirishdan chiqadi ($2x = 10 - 12$). B variant $2x$ ni ayirish o‘rniga chap tomonga qo‘shishdan chiqadi ($6x = 22$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A taxi service in Tashkent charges a fixed fee of 5,000 soums plus 2,500 soums for each kilometer driven. A ride cost a total of 32,500 soums. How many kilometers long was the ride?\",\"option_a\":\"$6.5$\",\"option_b\":\"$11$\",\"option_c\":\"$13$\",\"option_d\":\"$15$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $k$ be the length of the ride in kilometers. The total cost is $5{,}000 + 2{,}500k = 32{,}500$.\\n\\nSubtract $5{,}000$ from both sides: $2{,}500k = 27{,}500$. Divide by $2{,}500$: $k = 11$.\\n\\nChoice C ($13$) divides the whole cost by $2{,}500$ and ignores the fixed fee. Choice D ($15$) adds the fee instead of subtracting it ($37{,}500 \\\\div 2{,}500$). Choice A ($6.5$) divides the total by the fixed fee instead of by the price per kilometer.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$k$ — yo‘l uzunligi (kilometrda) bo‘lsin. Umumiy narx: $5{,}000 + 2{,}500k = 32{,}500$.\\n\\nIkkala tomondan $5{,}000$ ni ayiramiz: $2{,}500k = 27{,}500$. $2{,}500$ ga bo‘lamiz: $k = 11$.\\n\\nC variant ($13$) — butun summani $2{,}500$ ga bo‘lish natijasi; bunda qat’iy to‘lov hisobga olinmagan. D variant ($15$) — to‘lovni ayirish o‘rniga qo‘shish natijasi ($37{,}500 \\\\div 2{,}500$). A variant ($6.5$) — umumiy summani kilometr narxiga emas, qat’iy to‘lovga bo‘lishdan chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\frac{x}{4} + 6 = 9$$\\n\\nWhat is the solution to the given equation?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract $6$ from both sides: $\\\\frac{x}{4} = 3$. Multiply both sides by $4$: $x = 12$.\\n\\nCheck: $\\\\frac{12}{4} + 6 = 3 + 6 = 9$.\\n\\nA common mistake is multiplying only $\\\\frac{x}{4}$ by $4$ and not the other terms, which gives $x + 6 = 9$ and the wrong answer $x = 3$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomondan $6$ ni ayiramiz: $\\\\frac{x}{4} = 3$. Ikkala tomonni $4$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $x = 12$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $\\\\frac{12}{4} + 6 = 3 + 6 = 9$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $4$ ga faqat $\\\\frac{x}{4}$ ni ko‘paytirib, qolgan hadlarni ko‘paytirmaslik. Unda $x + 6 = 9$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $x = 3$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the solution to the equation $\\\\dfrac{x}{3} - \\\\dfrac{x}{5} = 4$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-30$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{8}{15}$\",\"option_c\":\"$30$\",\"option_d\":\"$60$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Multiply both sides by $15$, the least common denominator: $5x - 3x = 60$. So $2x = 60$ and $x = 30$.\\n\\nCheck: $\\\\frac{30}{3} - \\\\frac{30}{5} = 10 - 6 = 4$.\\n\\nChoice D treats $5x - 3x$ as $x$. Choice A subtracts the fractions in the wrong order ($\\\\frac{x}{5} - \\\\frac{x}{3}$). Choice B finds $\\\\frac{x}{3} - \\\\frac{x}{5} = \\\\frac{2}{15}x$ correctly but then multiplies $4$ by $\\\\frac{2}{15}$ instead of dividing.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomonni eng kichik umumiy maxraj $15$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $5x - 3x = 60$. Demak $2x = 60$ va $x = 30$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $\\\\frac{30}{3} - \\\\frac{30}{5} = 10 - 6 = 4$.\\n\\nD variantda $5x - 3x$ xato ravishda $x$ deb olingan. A variantda kasrlar teskari tartibda ayirilgan ($\\\\frac{x}{5} - \\\\frac{x}{3}$). B variantda $\\\\frac{x}{3} - \\\\frac{x}{5} = \\\\frac{2}{15}x$ to‘g‘ri topilgan, lekin $4$ ni $\\\\frac{2}{15}$ ga bo‘lish o‘rniga ko‘paytirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Dilnoza has 180,000 soums in savings and adds 25,000 soums each week. Her brother Jasur has 420,000 soums and spends 15,000 soums of it each week. If both continue this pattern, after how many weeks will they have the same amount of money?\",\"option_a\":\"$6$\",\"option_b\":\"$9.6$\",\"option_c\":\"$15$\",\"option_d\":\"$24$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"After $w$ weeks, Dilnoza has $180{,}000 + 25{,}000w$ soums and Jasur has $420{,}000 - 15{,}000w$ soums. Set them equal:\\n\\n$180{,}000 + 25{,}000w = 420{,}000 - 15{,}000w$, so $40{,}000w = 240{,}000$ and $w = 6$. After $6$ weeks each has $330{,}000$ soums.\\n\\nChoice D subtracts the weekly amounts ($10{,}000w = 240{,}000$), but the gap closes from both sides, so the rates add. Choice B ignores Jasur's spending ($240{,}000 \\\\div 25{,}000$). Choice C adds the starting amounts instead of subtracting them ($600{,}000 \\\\div 40{,}000$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$w$ haftadan keyin Dilnozada $180{,}000 + 25{,}000w$ so‘m, Jasurda esa $420{,}000 - 15{,}000w$ so‘m bo‘ladi. Ularni tenglaymiz:\\n\\n$180{,}000 + 25{,}000w = 420{,}000 - 15{,}000w$, bundan $40{,}000w = 240{,}000$ va $w = 6$. $6$ haftadan keyin har birida $330{,}000$ so‘m bo‘ladi.\\n\\nD variantda haftalik miqdorlar ayirilgan ($10{,}000w = 240{,}000$), ammo farq ikki tomondan qisqaradi, shuning uchun sur’atlar qo‘shiladi. B variantda Jasurning sarfi hisobga olinmagan ($240{,}000 \\\\div 25{,}000$). C variantda boshlang‘ich summalar ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan ($600{,}000 \\\\div 40{,}000$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":100,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$0.4(5x - 2) = 1.3x + 2$$\\n\\nWhat is the solution to the given equation?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute $0.4$: $2x - 0.8 = 1.3x + 2$. Subtract $1.3x$ from both sides: $0.7x - 0.8 = 2$. Add $0.8$: $0.7x = 2.8$. Divide by $0.7$: $x = 4$.\\n\\nCheck: $0.4(20 - 2) = 7.2$ and $1.3(4) + 2 = 7.2$.\\n\\nA common mistake is multiplying only $5x$ by $0.4$, which gives $2x - 2 = 1.3x + 2$ and the wrong value $x = \\\\frac{40}{7}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$0.4$ ni qavs ichiga ko‘paytiramiz: $2x - 0.8 = 1.3x + 2$. Ikkala tomondan $1.3x$ ni ayiramiz: $0.7x - 0.8 = 2$. $0.8$ ni qo‘shamiz: $0.7x = 2.8$. $0.7$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x = 4$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $0.4(20 - 2) = 7.2$ va $1.3(4) + 2 = 7.2$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $0.4$ ga faqat $5x$ ni ko‘paytirish. Unda $2x - 2 = 1.3x + 2$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $x = \\\\frac{40}{7}$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$a(x - 2) + 7 = 3x + b$$\\n\\nIn the given equation, $a$ and $b$ are constants and $a \\\\ne 3$. Which of the following is the solution to the given equation?\",\"option_a\":\"$x = \\\\dfrac{b - 7}{a - 3}$\",\"option_b\":\"$x = \\\\dfrac{b + 2a - 7}{a - 3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$x = \\\\dfrac{b - 2a - 7}{a - 3}$\",\"option_d\":\"$x = \\\\dfrac{b + 2a - 7}{a + 3}$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute: $ax - 2a + 7 = 3x + b$. Collect the $x$-terms on the left and the other terms on the right: $ax - 3x = b + 2a - 7$.\\n\\nFactor out $x$: $(a - 3)x = b + 2a - 7$. Because $a \\\\ne 3$, divide by $a - 3$: $x = \\\\dfrac{b + 2a - 7}{a - 3}$.\\n\\nChoice A forgets to distribute $a$ to $-2$. Choice C moves $-2a$ to the right side without changing its sign. Choice D adds $3x$ to the left side instead of subtracting it, which gives $a + 3$ in the denominator.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qavsni ochamiz: $ax - 2a + 7 = 3x + b$. $x$ li hadlarni chapga, qolganlarini o‘ngga o‘tkazamiz: $ax - 3x = b + 2a - 7$.\\n\\n$x$ ni qavsdan tashqariga chiqaramiz: $(a - 3)x = b + 2a - 7$. $a \\\\ne 3$ bo‘lgani uchun $a - 3$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x = \\\\dfrac{b + 2a - 7}{a - 3}$.\\n\\nA variantda $a$ ni $-2$ ga ko‘paytirish unutilgan. C variantda $-2a$ o‘ng tomonga ishorasi o‘zgartirilmasdan o‘tkazilgan. D variantda $3x$ chap tomondan ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan, shuning uchun maxrajda $a + 3$ hosil bo‘lgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_one_variable\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\frac{3}{4}(8x - 12) - 2(x - k) = 5x + 1$$\\n\\nIn the given equation, $k$ is a constant. If $x = 3$ is a solution to the equation, what is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"13/2\",\"6.5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Simplify the left side: $\\\\frac{3}{4}(8x - 12) = 6x - 9$ and $-2(x - k) = -2x + 2k$, so the equation is $4x - 9 + 2k = 5x + 1$.\\n\\nSubstitute $x = 3$: $12 - 9 + 2k = 15 + 1$, so $3 + 2k = 16$, $2k = 13$ and $k = \\\\frac{13}{2}$. Enter 13/2 or 6.5.\\n\\nA common mistake is writing $-2(x - k)$ as $-2x - 2k$, which leads to $3 - 2k = 16$ and the wrong value $k = -\\\\frac{13}{2}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Chap tomonni soddalashtiramiz: $\\\\frac{3}{4}(8x - 12) = 6x - 9$ va $-2(x - k) = -2x + 2k$, demak tenglama $4x - 9 + 2k = 5x + 1$ ko‘rinishini oladi.\\n\\n$x = 3$ ni qo‘yamiz: $12 - 9 + 2k = 15 + 1$, ya’ni $3 + 2k = 16$, $2k = 13$ va $k = \\\\frac{13}{2}$. Javobni 13/2 yoki 6.5 shaklida kiriting.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $-2(x - k)$ ni $-2x - 2k$ deb yozish. Unda $3 - 2k = 16$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $k = -\\\\frac{13}{2}$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In the equation $5x + 2y = 40$, what is the value of $y$ when $x = 6$?\",\"option_a\":\"$2$\",\"option_b\":\"$5$\",\"option_c\":\"$10$\",\"option_d\":\"$17$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $x = 6$: $5(6) + 2y = 40$, so $30 + 2y = 40$. Subtract $30$: $2y = 10$. Divide by $2$: $y = 5$.\\n\\nChoice C stops at $2y = 10$ and forgets to divide by $2$. Choice A divides $10$ by $5$ instead of by $2$. Choice D subtracts $6$ instead of $5(6)$: $(40 - 6) \\\\div 2 = 17$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x = 6$ ni qo‘yamiz: $5(6) + 2y = 40$, ya’ni $30 + 2y = 40$. $30$ ni ayiramiz: $2y = 10$. $2$ ga bo‘lamiz: $y = 5$.\\n\\nC variantda $2y = 10$ da to‘xtab, $2$ ga bo‘lish unutilgan. A variantda $10$ ni $2$ ga emas, $5$ ga bo‘lingan. D variantda $5(6)$ o‘rniga $6$ ayirilgan: $(40 - 6) \\\\div 2 = 17$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A stationery shop in Samarkand sells notebooks for 4,000 soums each and pens for 1,500 soums each. Malika spent exactly 23,000 soums on $n$ notebooks and $p$ pens. Which equation represents this situation?\",\"option_a\":\"$1{,}500n + 4{,}000p = 23{,}000$\",\"option_b\":\"$n + p = 23{,}000$\",\"option_c\":\"$4{,}000n + 1{,}500p = 23{,}000$\",\"option_d\":\"$5{,}500(n + p) = 23{,}000$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The notebooks cost $4{,}000n$ soums in total and the pens cost $1{,}500p$ soums in total. Together they cost $23{,}000$ soums, so $4{,}000n + 1{,}500p = 23{,}000$.\\n\\nChoice A matches each price with the wrong item. Choice B adds the numbers of items, not their costs. Choice D charges every item $5{,}500$ soums, the sum of the two prices.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Daftarlar jami $4{,}000n$ so‘m, ruchkalar jami $1{,}500p$ so‘m turadi. Birgalikda ular $23{,}000$ so‘m, demak $4{,}000n + 1{,}500p = 23{,}000$.\\n\\nA variantda narxlar buyumlarga noto‘g‘ri mos qo‘yilgan. B variantda narxlar emas, buyumlar soni qo‘shilgan. D variantda har bir buyum ikki narx yig‘indisi — $5{,}500$ so‘mdan hisoblangan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of $3x - 4y = 24$ crosses the $y$-axis at the point $(0, b)$. What is the value of $b$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-6\"],\"explanation_en\":\"On the $y$-axis, $x = 0$. Substitute: $3(0) - 4y = 24$, so $-4y = 24$ and $y = -6$. Thus $b = -6$.\\n\\nCommon mistakes: answering $6$ (dropping the negative sign) or $8$, which is the $x$-intercept (found by setting $y = 0$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y$ o‘qida $x = 0$ bo‘ladi. Qo‘yamiz: $3(0) - 4y = 24$, ya’ni $-4y = 24$ va $y = -6$. Demak $b = -6$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xatolar: manfiy ishorani tushirib qoldirib $6$ deb javob berish yoki $y = 0$ deb topiladigan $x$ o‘qi bilan kesishish nuqtasi — $8$ ni yozish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A line in the $xy$-plane passes through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(6, 11)$. Which equation defines the line?\",\"option_a\":\"$y = \\\\frac{1}{3}x - \\\\frac{5}{3}$\",\"option_b\":\"$y = 3x - 1$\",\"option_c\":\"$y = 3x + 5$\",\"option_d\":\"$y = 3x - 7$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The slope is $\\\\dfrac{11 - (-1)}{6 - 2} = \\\\dfrac{12}{4} = 3$. In $y = 3x + c$, substitute $(6, 11)$: $11 = 18 + c$, so $c = -7$. The line is $y = 3x - 7$. Check with $(2, -1)$: $3(2) - 7 = -1$.\\n\\nChoice A uses the run over the rise, $\\\\frac{4}{12} = \\\\frac{1}{3}$, as the slope. Choice B uses the $y$-coordinate $-1$ of a point as the $y$-intercept. Choice C mixes the two points, using $x = 2$ with $y = 11$: $11 = 6 + c$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Burchak koeffitsiyenti: $\\\\dfrac{11 - (-1)}{6 - 2} = \\\\dfrac{12}{4} = 3$. $y = 3x + c$ ga $(6, 11)$ ni qo‘yamiz: $11 = 18 + c$, demak $c = -7$. To‘g‘ri chiziq: $y = 3x - 7$. $(2, -1)$ bilan tekshiramiz: $3(2) - 7 = -1$.\\n\\nA variantda burchak koeffitsiyenti teskari olingan: $\\\\frac{4}{12} = \\\\frac{1}{3}$. B variantda nuqtaning $y$-koordinatasi $-1$ kesishish nuqtasi deb olingan. C variantda ikki nuqta aralashtirilgan: $x = 2$ va $y = 11$ olinib, $11 = 6 + c$ yozilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of $ax + 3y = 12$, where $a$ is a constant, passes through the point $(2, 6)$. What is the slope of the graph?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"1\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $(2, 6)$: $2a + 18 = 12$, so $2a = -6$ and $a = -3$. The equation is $-3x + 3y = 12$, or $y = x + 4$. The slope is $1$.\\n\\nA common mistake is giving the value of $a$ ($-3$) as the slope. The slope of $ax + 3y = 12$ is $-\\\\frac{a}{3}$, not $a$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$(2, 6)$ ni qo‘yamiz: $2a + 18 = 12$, ya’ni $2a = -6$ va $a = -3$. Tenglama: $-3x + 3y = 12$ yoki $y = x + 4$. Burchak koeffitsiyenti $1$ ga teng.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $a$ ning qiymati ($-3$) ni burchak koeffitsiyenti deb yozish. $ax + 3y = 12$ ning burchak koeffitsiyenti $a$ emas, $-\\\\frac{a}{3}$ ga teng.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A school has 1,200,000 soums to spend on chairs and desks. Each chair costs 150,000 soums and each desk costs 300,000 soums. The equation $150{,}000c + 300{,}000d = 1{,}200{,}000$ represents spending the entire amount on $c$ chairs and $d$ desks. If the school buys $2$ more desks, how many fewer chairs can it buy?\",\"option_a\":\"$1$\",\"option_b\":\"$2$\",\"option_c\":\"$4$\",\"option_d\":\"$8$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Two more desks cost $2 \\\\times 300{,}000 = 600{,}000$ soums more. To keep the total at $1{,}200{,}000$ soums, chair spending must drop by $600{,}000$ soums, which is $600{,}000 \\\\div 150{,}000 = 4$ chairs.\\n\\nEquivalently, solving for $c$ gives $c = 8 - 2d$, so each extra desk means $2$ fewer chairs, and $2$ extra desks mean $4$ fewer chairs.\\n\\nChoice B assumes one chair is given up for each desk. Choice A uses the inverted ratio $\\\\frac{150{,}000}{300{,}000}$. Choice D is the number of chairs the school could buy with no desks at all.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkita qo‘shimcha parta $2 \\\\times 300{,}000 = 600{,}000$ so‘m ko‘p turadi. Umumiy summa $1{,}200{,}000$ so‘m bo‘lib qolishi uchun stullarga sarf $600{,}000$ so‘mga kamayishi kerak, bu $600{,}000 \\\\div 150{,}000 = 4$ ta stul.\\n\\nBoshqacha: $c$ ni ifodalasak, $c = 8 - 2d$; har bir qo‘shimcha parta $2$ ta stulni kamaytiradi, $2$ ta parta esa $4$ ta stulni.\\n\\nB variantda har bir parta uchun bitta stul kamayadi deb olingan. A variantda nisbat teskari olingan: $\\\\frac{150{,}000}{300{,}000}$. D variant — parta umuman olinmaganda sotib olish mumkin bo‘lgan stullar soni.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Line $m$ in the $xy$-plane is parallel to the line $4x - 6y = 9$ and passes through the point $(3, -2)$. What is the $y$-coordinate of the $y$-intercept of line $m$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-4$\",\"option_b\":\"$-\\\\frac{3}{2}$\",\"option_c\":\"$0$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{5}{2}$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Rewrite $4x - 6y = 9$ as $y = \\\\frac{2}{3}x - \\\\frac{3}{2}$, so its slope is $\\\\frac{2}{3}$. Parallel lines have equal slopes, so line $m$ is $y = \\\\frac{2}{3}x + c$.\\n\\nSubstitute $(3, -2)$: $-2 = \\\\frac{2}{3}(3) + c = 2 + c$, so $c = -4$.\\n\\nChoice B is the $y$-intercept of the given line, not of line $m$. Choice C uses the slope $-\\\\frac{2}{3}$ (a sign error when solving for $y$). Choice D uses the perpendicular slope $-\\\\frac{3}{2}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$4x - 6y = 9$ ni $y = \\\\frac{2}{3}x - \\\\frac{3}{2}$ ko‘rinishiga keltiramiz, burchak koeffitsiyenti $\\\\frac{2}{3}$. Parallel to‘g‘ri chiziqlarning burchak koeffitsiyentlari teng, demak $m$: $y = \\\\frac{2}{3}x + c$.\\n\\n$(3, -2)$ ni qo‘yamiz: $-2 = \\\\frac{2}{3}(3) + c = 2 + c$, bundan $c = -4$.\\n\\nB variant — berilgan to‘g‘ri chiziqning $y$ o‘qi bilan kesishishi, $m$ niki emas. C variantda burchak koeffitsiyenti $-\\\\frac{2}{3}$ olingan ($y$ ni ifodalashda ishora xatosi). D variantda perpendikulyar to‘g‘ri chiziqning koeffitsiyenti $-\\\\frac{3}{2}$ ishlatilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":110,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_equations_two_variables\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of $px + 5y = q$, where $p$ and $q$ are constants, is parallel to the graph of $y = -0.8x + 3$ and has an $x$-intercept of $(10, 0)$. What is the value of $p + q$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"44\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Solving $px + 5y = q$ for $y$ gives $y = -\\\\frac{p}{5}x + \\\\frac{q}{5}$, so the slope is $-\\\\frac{p}{5}$. Parallel lines have equal slopes: $-\\\\frac{p}{5} = -0.8$, so $p = 4$.\\n\\nThe point $(10, 0)$ is on the graph: $4(10) + 5(0) = q$, so $q = 40$. Therefore $p + q = 44$.\\n\\nA common mistake is taking the slope of $px + 5y = q$ as $\\\\frac{p}{5}$, which gives $p = -4$, $q = -40$ and $p + q = -44$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$px + 5y = q$ dan $y$ ni ifodalaymiz: $y = -\\\\frac{p}{5}x + \\\\frac{q}{5}$, burchak koeffitsiyenti $-\\\\frac{p}{5}$. Parallel to‘g‘ri chiziqlarda ular teng: $-\\\\frac{p}{5} = -0.8$, demak $p = 4$.\\n\\n$(10, 0)$ nuqta grafikda yotadi: $4(10) + 5(0) = q$, demak $q = 40$. Shunday qilib, $p + q = 44$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $px + 5y = q$ ning burchak koeffitsiyentini $\\\\frac{p}{5}$ deb olish. Unda $p = -4$, $q = -40$ va $p + q = -44$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = 7 - 3x$. What is the value of $g(4)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-5$\",\"option_b\":\"$5$\",\"option_c\":\"$16$\",\"option_d\":\"$19$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $x = 4$: $g(4) = 7 - 3(4) = 7 - 12 = -5$.\\n\\nChoice B reverses the subtraction ($12 - 7$). Choice C computes $(7 - 3) \\\\cdot 4$, ignoring the order of operations. Choice D adds $12$ instead of subtracting it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x = 4$ ni qo‘yamiz: $g(4) = 7 - 3(4) = 7 - 12 = -5$.\\n\\nB variantda ayirish teskari bajarilgan ($12 - 7$). C variantda amallar tartibi buzilib, $(7 - 3) \\\\cdot 4$ hisoblangan. D variantda $12$ ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":45,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The amount of mobile data, in gigabytes, remaining on Bekzod's monthly plan $t$ days after the start of the month is given by the function $D(t) = 20 - 0.6t$. What is the best interpretation of $0.6$ in this context?\",\"option_a\":\"The total amount of data, in gigabytes, on the plan at the start of the month\",\"option_b\":\"The amount of data, in gigabytes, that Bekzod uses each day\",\"option_c\":\"The number of days it takes Bekzod to use all of the data\",\"option_d\":\"The amount of data, in gigabytes, remaining after one day\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The function is linear, and $0.6$ is the coefficient of $t$. Each time $t$ increases by $1$ day, $D(t)$ decreases by $0.6$ gigabyte, so $0.6$ is the amount of data Bekzod uses each day.\\n\\nChoice A describes $20$, the value of $D(0)$. Choice C describes $\\\\frac{20}{0.6} \\\\approx 33.3$, the value of $t$ when $D(t) = 0$. Choice D describes $D(1) = 19.4$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Funksiya chiziqli, $0.6$ esa $t$ oldidagi koeffitsiyent. $t$ har $1$ kunga oshganda $D(t)$ $0.6$ gigabaytga kamayadi, demak $0.6$ — Bekzod har kuni sarflaydigan internet hajmi.\\n\\nA variant $20$ ni, ya’ni $D(0)$ ni tasvirlaydi. C variant $D(t) = 0$ bo‘ladigan $t = \\\\frac{20}{0.6} \\\\approx 33.3$ ni tasvirlaydi. D variant $D(1) = 19.4$ ni tasvirlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 5x + b$, where $b$ is a constant. If $f(2) = 13$, what is the value of $b$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $x = 2$: $f(2) = 5(2) + b = 10 + b$. Since $f(2) = 13$, $10 + b = 13$ and $b = 3$.\\n\\nA common mistake is substituting $13$ for $x$ instead of for $f(x)$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x = 2$ ni qo‘yamiz: $f(2) = 5(2) + b = 10 + b$. $f(2) = 13$ bo‘lgani uchun $10 + b = 13$ va $b = 3$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $13$ ni $f(x)$ o‘rniga emas, $x$ o‘rniga qo‘yish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $h(x)$ for the linear function $h$.\\n\\n| x | h(x) |\\n| ---: | ---: |\\n| 1 | 11 |\\n| 4 | 2 |\\n| 7 | −7 |\\n\\nWhich equation defines $h$?\",\"option_a\":\"$h(x) = 3x + 8$\",\"option_b\":\"$h(x) = -3x + 11$\",\"option_c\":\"$h(x) = -3x + 14$\",\"option_d\":\"$h(x) = -\\\\frac{1}{3}x + \\\\frac{34}{3}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The slope is $\\\\dfrac{2 - 11}{4 - 1} = \\\\dfrac{-9}{3} = -3$. Write $h(x) = -3x + c$ and use $h(1) = 11$: $-3 + c = 11$, so $c = 14$. Check: $h(4) = 2$ and $h(7) = -7$.\\n\\nChoice B uses $h(1) = 11$ as the $y$-intercept, but the $y$-intercept is $h(0)$. Choice A has the wrong sign for the slope. Choice D uses $\\\\frac{\\\\text{change in } x}{\\\\text{change in } h(x)}$ as the slope; it fits $(1, 11)$ but gives $h(4) = 10$, not $2$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Burchak koeffitsiyenti: $\\\\dfrac{2 - 11}{4 - 1} = \\\\dfrac{-9}{3} = -3$. $h(x) = -3x + c$ deb yozamiz va $h(1) = 11$ dan foydalanamiz: $-3 + c = 11$, demak $c = 14$. Tekshiruv: $h(4) = 2$ va $h(7) = -7$.\\n\\nB variantda $h(1) = 11$ ozod had deb olingan, lekin ozod had $h(0)$ ga teng. A variantda koeffitsiyent ishorasi noto‘g‘ri. D variantda koeffitsiyent teskari olingan; u $(1, 11)$ ga mos keladi, ammo $h(4) = 10$ beradi, $2$ emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The amount of fuel in a car's tank decreases at a constant rate as the car is driven. After the car has been driven 150 kilometers, the tank contains 36 liters of fuel. After the car has been driven 400 kilometers, the tank contains 16 liters of fuel. Which function $F$ gives the number of liters of fuel in the tank after the car has been driven $d$ kilometers?\",\"option_a\":\"$F(d) = 36 - 0.08d$\",\"option_b\":\"$F(d) = 48 + 0.08d$\",\"option_c\":\"$F(d) = 48 - 12.5d$\",\"option_d\":\"$F(d) = 48 - 0.08d$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The rate of change is $\\\\dfrac{16 - 36}{400 - 150} = \\\\dfrac{-20}{250} = -0.08$ liter per kilometer. So $F(d) = -0.08d + c$. Using $F(150) = 36$: $-12 + c = 36$, so $c = 48$. Thus $F(d) = 48 - 0.08d$.\\n\\nChoice A uses $36$, the fuel after $150$ km, as the starting amount. Choice B makes the fuel increase. Choice C uses $\\\\frac{250}{20} = 12.5$ kilometers per liter as the rate.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"O‘zgarish tezligi: $\\\\dfrac{16 - 36}{400 - 150} = \\\\dfrac{-20}{250} = -0.08$ litr/km. Demak $F(d) = -0.08d + c$. $F(150) = 36$ dan: $-12 + c = 36$, ya’ni $c = 48$. Shunday qilib, $F(d) = 48 - 0.08d$.\\n\\nA variantda $150$ km dan keyingi yoqilg‘i — $36$ boshlang‘ich miqdor deb olingan. B variantda yoqilg‘i ortib boradi. C variantda tezlik sifatida $\\\\frac{250}{20} = 12.5$ km/litr ishlatilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":100,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 4x - 5$. For any value of $k$, what is the value of $f(k + 3) - f(k)$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12\"],\"explanation_en\":\"$f(k + 3) = 4(k + 3) - 5 = 4k + 7$ and $f(k) = 4k - 5$. The difference is $(4k + 7) - (4k - 5) = 12$.\\n\\nAnother way: the slope is $4$, so when the input increases by $3$, the output increases by $4 \\\\times 3 = 12$.\\n\\nCommon mistakes: answering $3$ (the change in input, not output) or writing $f(k + 3)$ as $4k + 3 - 5$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$f(k + 3) = 4(k + 3) - 5 = 4k + 7$ va $f(k) = 4k - 5$. Ayirma: $(4k + 7) - (4k - 5) = 12$.\\n\\nBoshqa usul: burchak koeffitsiyenti $4$, demak argument $3$ ga oshganda qiymat $4 \\\\times 3 = 12$ ga oshadi.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xatolar: $3$ deb javob berish (bu qiymatning emas, argumentning o‘zgarishi) yoki $f(k + 3)$ ni $4k + 3 - 5$ deb yozish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"For the linear function $f$, $f(0) = 3$, $f(a) = 9$, and $f(a + 5) = -1$, where $a$ is a constant. What is the value of $a$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-12$\",\"option_b\":\"$-6$\",\"option_c\":\"$-3$\",\"option_d\":\"$3$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"When the input increases by $5$ (from $a$ to $a + 5$), the output changes by $-1 - 9 = -10$. So the slope is $\\\\frac{-10}{5} = -2$, and with $f(0) = 3$, $f(x) = -2x + 3$.\\n\\nThen $f(a) = -2a + 3 = 9$, so $-2a = 6$ and $a = -3$. Check: $f(2) = -1$.\\n\\nChoice A uses $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ (run over rise) as the slope. Choice B treats the slope as $-1$, using only the change in output. Choice D uses a slope of $+2$, losing the negative sign.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Argument $5$ ga oshganda ($a$ dan $a + 5$ gacha) qiymat $-1 - 9 = -10$ ga o‘zgaradi. Demak burchak koeffitsiyenti $\\\\frac{-10}{5} = -2$, $f(0) = 3$ bo‘lgani uchun $f(x) = -2x + 3$.\\n\\nU holda $f(a) = -2a + 3 = 9$, ya’ni $-2a = 6$ va $a = -3$. Tekshiruv: $f(2) = -1$.\\n\\nA variantda koeffitsiyent teskari olingan: $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$. B variantda faqat qiymat o‘zgarishiga qarab koeffitsiyent $-1$ deb olingan. D variantda manfiy ishora yo‘qotilib, koeffitsiyent $+2$ deb olingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The total amount a gym member has paid, in thousands of soums, is a linear function of the number of months since joining and includes a one-time sign-up fee. After 4 months, the member had paid a total of 1,140 thousand soums. After 10 months, the member had paid a total of 2,250 thousand soums. What is the total amount, in thousands of soums, the member will have paid after 15 months?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3175\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The monthly rate is $\\\\dfrac{2{,}250 - 1{,}140}{10 - 4} = \\\\dfrac{1{,}110}{6} = 185$ thousand soums per month.\\n\\nFrom month $10$ to month $15$ the total grows by $5 \\\\times 185 = 925$, so the total after $15$ months is $2{,}250 + 925 = 3{,}175$ thousand soums. (The sign-up fee is $1{,}140 - 4 \\\\times 185 = 400$ thousand soums, and $400 + 15 \\\\times 185 = 3{,}175$ as well.)\\n\\nA common mistake is treating the total as proportional to the number of months, for example $\\\\frac{1{,}140}{4} \\\\times 15 = 4{,}275$, which ignores the one-time fee.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Oylik to‘lov: $\\\\dfrac{2{,}250 - 1{,}140}{10 - 4} = \\\\dfrac{1{,}110}{6} = 185$ ming so‘m.\\n\\n$10$-oydan $15$-oygacha jami summa $5 \\\\times 185 = 925$ ga oshadi, demak $15$ oydan keyin jami $2{,}250 + 925 = 3{,}175$ ming so‘m. (Ro‘yxatdan o‘tish to‘lovi $1{,}140 - 4 \\\\times 185 = 400$ ming so‘m va $400 + 15 \\\\times 185 = 3{,}175$ ham shuni beradi.)\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: jami summani oylar soniga proporsional deb hisoblash, masalan $\\\\frac{1{,}140}{4} \\\\times 15 = 4{,}275$; bunda bir martalik to‘lov hisobga olinmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which inequality describes all solutions to $5 - 2x > 13$?\",\"option_a\":\"$x < 4$\",\"option_b\":\"$x > 4$\",\"option_c\":\"$x > -4$\",\"option_d\":\"$x < -4$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract $5$ from both sides: $-2x > 8$. Divide both sides by $-2$; dividing by a negative number reverses the inequality: $x < -4$.\\n\\nCheck: $x = -5$ gives $5 + 10 = 15 > 13$, which is true.\\n\\nChoice C forgets to reverse the inequality sign. Choice B drops the negative sign of $-2$ and solves $2x > 8$. Choice A drops the negative sign and also reverses the inequality, which is only needed when dividing by a negative number.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomondan $5$ ni ayiramiz: $-2x > 8$. Ikkala tomonni $-2$ ga bo‘lamiz; manfiy songa bo‘lganda tengsizlik belgisi teskarisiga o‘zgaradi: $x < -4$.\\n\\nTekshiruv: $x = -5$ da $5 + 10 = 15 > 13$ — to‘g‘ri.\\n\\nC variantda tengsizlik belgisini o‘zgartirish unutilgan. B variantda $-2$ ning manfiy ishorasi tushirib qoldirilib, $2x > 8$ yechilgan. A variantda manfiy ishora tushirib qoldirilgan va belgi ham o‘zgartirilgan, holbuki belgi faqat manfiy songa bo‘lganda o‘zgaradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"An elevator can safely carry at most 650 kilograms. An operator who weighs 80 kilograms rides in the elevator with boxes of supplies that weigh 25 kilograms each. What is the greatest number of boxes the operator can take in one trip?\",\"option_a\":\"$22$\",\"option_b\":\"$23$\",\"option_c\":\"$26$\",\"option_d\":\"$29$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $b$ be the number of boxes. The total weight must satisfy $80 + 25b \\\\le 650$. Subtract $80$: $25b \\\\le 570$. Divide by $25$: $b \\\\le 22.8$. The number of boxes must be a whole number, so the greatest possible value is $22$.\\n\\nChoice B rounds $22.8$ up, but $23$ boxes and the operator weigh $655$ kilograms, which is too much. Choice C ignores the operator's weight ($650 \\\\div 25$). Choice D adds the operator's weight instead of subtracting it ($730 \\\\div 25 \\\\approx 29.2$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$b$ — qutilar soni bo‘lsin. Umumiy og‘irlik: $80 + 25b \\\\le 650$. $80$ ni ayiramiz: $25b \\\\le 570$. $25$ ga bo‘lamiz: $b \\\\le 22.8$. Qutilar soni butun son bo‘lishi kerak, demak eng katta qiymat $22$.\\n\\nB variantda $22.8$ yuqoriga yaxlitlangan, ammo $23$ ta quti va operator $655$ kilogramm bo‘ladi — bu ruxsat etilganidan ko‘p. C variantda operatorning og‘irligi hisobga olinmagan ($650 \\\\div 25$). D variantda operator og‘irligi ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan ($730 \\\\div 25 \\\\approx 29.2$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"What is the least integer $n$ that satisfies the inequality $3n + 4 > 19$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"6\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Subtract $4$ from both sides: $3n > 15$. Divide by $3$: $n > 5$. The least integer greater than $5$ is $6$.\\n\\nA common mistake is answering $5$, but $3(5) + 4 = 19$, and $19 > 19$ is false.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomondan $4$ ni ayiramiz: $3n > 15$. $3$ ga bo‘lamiz: $n > 5$. $5$ dan katta eng kichik butun son — $6$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $5$ deb javob berish. Lekin $3(5) + 4 = 19$ va $19 > 19$ noto‘g‘ri.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Sardor has 300,000 soums. He buys a book for 85,000 soums and plans to visit a café, where each visit costs 18,000 soums. He wants to have at least 50,000 soums left after buying the book and paying for the café visits. Which inequality represents this situation, where $v$ is the number of café visits?\",\"option_a\":\"$300{,}000 - 18{,}000v \\\\ge 50{,}000$\",\"option_b\":\"$215{,}000 - 18{,}000v \\\\le 50{,}000$\",\"option_c\":\"$215{,}000 - 18{,}000v \\\\ge 50{,}000$\",\"option_d\":\"$18{,}000v - 215{,}000 \\\\ge 50{,}000$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"After the book, Sardor has $300{,}000 - 85{,}000 = 215{,}000$ soums. After $v$ visits he has $215{,}000 - 18{,}000v$ soums. \\\\\\\"At least $50{,}000$ left\\\\\\\" means this amount is greater than or equal to $50{,}000$: $215{,}000 - 18{,}000v \\\\ge 50{,}000$.\\n\\nChoice A forgets the cost of the book. Choice B uses $\\\\le$, which means \\\\\\\"at most $50{,}000$ left.\\\\\\\" Choice D subtracts in the wrong order.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kitobdan keyin Sardorda $300{,}000 - 85{,}000 = 215{,}000$ so‘m qoladi. $v$ marta borgandan keyin unda $215{,}000 - 18{,}000v$ so‘m qoladi. \\\\\\\"Kamida $50{,}000$ qolishi\\\\\\\" bu miqdor $50{,}000$ dan katta yoki teng degani: $215{,}000 - 18{,}000v \\\\ge 50{,}000$.\\n\\nA variantda kitob narxi unutilgan. B variantda $\\\\le$ ishlatilgan, bu \\\\\\\"ko‘pi bilan $50{,}000$ qoladi\\\\\\\" degani. D variantda ayirish teskari tartibda bajarilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following describes all values of $x$ that satisfy both $2x - 3 \\\\ge 5$ and $x + 7 < 20$?\",\"option_a\":\"$1 \\\\le x < 13$\",\"option_b\":\"$4 \\\\le x < 13$\",\"option_c\":\"$4 < x \\\\le 13$\",\"option_d\":\"$4 \\\\le x < 27$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"First inequality: $2x \\\\ge 8$, so $x \\\\ge 4$. Second inequality: $x < 13$. Values that satisfy both are $4 \\\\le x < 13$.\\n\\nChoice A subtracts $3$ instead of adding it in the first inequality ($2x \\\\ge 2$). Choice C puts the strict and non-strict signs on the wrong ends. Choice D adds $7$ instead of subtracting it in the second inequality.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi tengsizlik: $2x \\\\ge 8$, demak $x \\\\ge 4$. Ikkinchi tengsizlik: $x < 13$. Ikkalasini qanoatlantiradigan qiymatlar: $4 \\\\le x < 13$.\\n\\nA variantda birinchi tengsizlikda $3$ qo‘shilish o‘rniga ayirilgan ($2x \\\\ge 2$). C variantda qat’iy va noqat’iy belgilar o‘rni almashtirilgan. D variantda ikkinchi tengsizlikda $7$ ayirilish o‘rniga qo‘shilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$-3(x - 4) \\\\ge 7x - 23$$\\n\\nWhat is the greatest value of $x$ that satisfies the given inequality?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"7/2\",\"3.5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Distribute: $-3x + 12 \\\\ge 7x - 23$. Add $3x$ and $23$ to both sides: $35 \\\\ge 10x$. Divide by $10$: $x \\\\le 3.5$. The greatest value is $3.5$. Enter 7/2 or 3.5.\\n\\nA common mistake is writing $-3(x - 4)$ as $-3x - 12$, which gives $11 \\\\ge 10x$ and the wrong value $1.1$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qavsni ochamiz: $-3x + 12 \\\\ge 7x - 23$. Ikkala tomonga $3x$ va $23$ ni qo‘shamiz: $35 \\\\ge 10x$. $10$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x \\\\le 3.5$. Eng katta qiymat — $3.5$. Javobni 7/2 yoki 3.5 shaklida kiriting.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $-3(x - 4)$ ni $-3x - 12$ deb yozish. Unda $11 \\\\ge 10x$ va noto‘g‘ri javob $1.1$ chiqadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A delivery van can carry at most 1,500 kilograms of cargo. Each box weighs 40 kilograms and each sack weighs 25 kilograms. For a certain delivery, the number of boxes must be at least twice the number of sacks. What is the greatest number of sacks the van can carry on this delivery?\",\"option_a\":\"$14$\",\"option_b\":\"$15$\",\"option_c\":\"$23$\",\"option_d\":\"$60$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $x$ be the number of boxes and $y$ the number of sacks. The conditions are $40x + 25y \\\\le 1{,}500$ and $x \\\\ge 2y$.\\n\\nTo carry as many sacks as possible, use the fewest boxes allowed, $x = 2y$. Then $40(2y) + 25y = 105y \\\\le 1{,}500$, so $y \\\\le 14.28\\\\ldots$ and the greatest whole number is $14$. Check: $28$ boxes and $14$ sacks weigh $1{,}120 + 350 = 1{,}470$ kg. With $15$ sacks, at least $30$ boxes are needed, and $1{,}200 + 375 = 1{,}575$ kg is too heavy.\\n\\nChoice B rounds $14.28\\\\ldots$ up. Choice C uses one box per sack ($1{,}500 \\\\div 65 \\\\approx 23.1$). Choice D ignores the condition on boxes and fills the van with sacks only ($1{,}500 \\\\div 25$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x$ — qutilar soni, $y$ — qoplar soni bo‘lsin. Shartlar: $40x + 25y \\\\le 1{,}500$ va $x \\\\ge 2y$.\\n\\nQoplar iloji boricha ko‘p bo‘lishi uchun qutilarni ruxsat etilgan eng kam miqdorda olamiz: $x = 2y$. U holda $40(2y) + 25y = 105y \\\\le 1{,}500$, ya’ni $y \\\\le 14.28\\\\ldots$, eng katta butun son $14$. Tekshiruv: $28$ ta quti va $14$ ta qop $1{,}120 + 350 = 1{,}470$ kg. $15$ ta qop uchun kamida $30$ ta quti kerak va $1{,}200 + 375 = 1{,}575$ kg — juda og‘ir.\\n\\nB variantda $14.28\\\\ldots$ yuqoriga yaxlitlangan. C variantda har bir qopga bitta quti olingan ($1{,}500 \\\\div 65 \\\\approx 23.1$). D variantda qutilar sharti e’tiborga olinmay, furgon faqat qoplar bilan to‘ldirilgan ($1{,}500 \\\\div 25$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":140,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"linear_inequalities\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$kx - 6 \\\\le 2x + 9$$\\n\\nIn the given inequality, $k$ is a constant. If the solution set of the inequality is $x \\\\ge -5$, what is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-1\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Rearrange: $(k - 2)x \\\\le 15$. The solution set is $x \\\\ge -5$, so the inequality sign must reverse when dividing by $k - 2$. That means $k - 2 < 0$ and $x \\\\ge \\\\frac{15}{k - 2}$.\\n\\nSet $\\\\frac{15}{k - 2} = -5$: $k - 2 = -3$, so $k = -1$. Check: $-x - 6 \\\\le 2x + 9$ gives $-15 \\\\le 3x$, or $x \\\\ge -5$.\\n\\nA common mistake is not reversing the sign; that leads to $x \\\\le \\\\frac{15}{k - 2}$, which can never be the set $x \\\\ge -5$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tengsizlikni qayta yozamiz: $(k - 2)x \\\\le 15$. Yechimlar to‘plami $x \\\\ge -5$, demak $k - 2$ ga bo‘lganda belgi teskarisiga o‘zgarishi kerak. Bu $k - 2 < 0$ va $x \\\\ge \\\\frac{15}{k - 2}$ degani.\\n\\n$\\\\frac{15}{k - 2} = -5$ deb olamiz: $k - 2 = -3$, demak $k = -1$. Tekshiruv: $-x - 6 \\\\le 2x + 9$ dan $-15 \\\\le 3x$, ya’ni $x \\\\ge -5$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: belgini o‘zgartirmaslik; unda $x \\\\le \\\\frac{15}{k - 2}$ hosil bo‘ladi, bu hech qachon $x \\\\ge -5$ to‘plami bo‘la olmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Two adjacent angles together form a straight line. One angle measures $(2x + 10)^\\\\circ$ and the other measures $(3x - 20)^\\\\circ$. What is the measure, in degrees, of the smaller angle?\",\"option_a\":\"$38$\",\"option_b\":\"$76$\",\"option_c\":\"$86$\",\"option_d\":\"$94$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Angles that form a straight line are supplementary, so $(2x + 10) + (3x - 20) = 180$. This gives $5x - 10 = 180$, so $5x = 190$ and $x = 38$. The angles measure $2(38) + 10 = 86^\\\\circ$ and $3(38) - 20 = 94^\\\\circ$. The smaller angle is $86^\\\\circ$. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($38$) is the value of $x$, not an angle measure. Choice B ($76$) is $2x$, leaving out the $+10$. Choice D ($94$) is the larger angle.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"To‘g‘ri chiziq hosil qiluvchi burchaklar yig‘indisi $180^\\\\circ$, demak $(2x + 10) + (3x - 20) = 180$. Bundan $5x - 10 = 180$, $5x = 190$ va $x = 38$. Burchaklar $2(38) + 10 = 86^\\\\circ$ va $3(38) - 20 = 94^\\\\circ$. Kichigi $86^\\\\circ$. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($38$) — bu $x$ ning qiymati, burchak emas. B ($76$) — bu $2x$, $+10$ tushirib qoldirilgan. D ($94$) — katta burchak.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In isosceles triangle $PQR$, $PQ = PR$, and the measure of angle $P$ is $46^\\\\circ$. What is the measure, in degrees, of angle $Q$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"67\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Since $PQ = PR$, the angles opposite those sides, angles $R$ and $Q$, are equal. The three angles sum to $180^\\\\circ$, so $46 + 2\\\\angle Q = 180$, which gives $2\\\\angle Q = 134$ and $\\\\angle Q = 67^\\\\circ$.\\n\\nIf you got 134, you forgot to divide by 2. If you got 46, you assumed angle $Q$ equals angle $P$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$PQ = PR$ bo‘lgani uchun bu tomonlar qarshisidagi $R$ va $Q$ burchaklar teng. Uchburchak burchaklari yig‘indisi $180^\\\\circ$, demak $46 + 2\\\\angle Q = 180$, bundan $2\\\\angle Q = 134$ va $\\\\angle Q = 67^\\\\circ$.\\n\\nAgar 134 chiqqan bo‘lsa, 2 ga bo‘lish unutilgan. Agar 46 chiqqan bo‘lsa, $Q$ burchak $P$ burchakka teng deb olingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Two sides of a triangle have lengths 7 and 12. Which of the following could be the length of the third side?\",\"option_a\":\"$3$\",\"option_b\":\"$11$\",\"option_c\":\"$19$\",\"option_d\":\"$20$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"By the triangle inequality, the third side must be greater than $12 - 7 = 5$ and less than $12 + 7 = 19$. Only 11 lies strictly between 5 and 19. Choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($3$) is too short: $3 + 7 = 10$, which is not greater than 12. Choice C ($19$) equals $7 + 12$, so the three segments would lie flat on a line instead of forming a triangle. Choice D ($20$) is longer than $7 + 12$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Uchburchak tengsizligiga ko‘ra uchinchi tomon $12 - 7 = 5$ dan katta va $12 + 7 = 19$ dan kichik bo‘lishi kerak. Faqat 11 soni 5 va 19 orasida yotadi. To‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA ($3$) — juda qisqa: $3 + 7 = 10$, bu 12 dan katta emas. C ($19$) — $7 + 12$ ga teng, kesmalar uchburchak hosil qilmay, bitta to‘g‘ri chiziqda yotadi. D ($20$) — $7 + 12$ dan uzun.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Parallel lines $p$ and $q$ are intersected by transversal $t$. Two alternate interior angles formed by these lines measure $(5x + 12)^\\\\circ$ and $(7x - 24)^\\\\circ$. What is the measure, in degrees, of the angle that measures $(5x + 12)^\\\\circ$?\",\"option_a\":\"$16$\",\"option_b\":\"$18$\",\"option_c\":\"$78$\",\"option_d\":\"$102$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"When parallel lines are cut by a transversal, alternate interior angles are congruent. So $5x + 12 = 7x - 24$, which gives $36 = 2x$ and $x = 18$. The angle measures $5(18) + 12 = 102^\\\\circ$ (and $7(18) - 24 = 102^\\\\circ$ checks). Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($16$) comes from treating the angles as supplementary: $12x - 12 = 180$ gives $x = 16$. Choice B ($18$) is the value of $x$. Choice C ($78$) is the supplement of the correct angle.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Parallel to‘g‘ri chiziqlar kesuvchi bilan kesilganda ichki almashinuvchi burchaklar teng bo‘ladi. Demak $5x + 12 = 7x - 24$, bundan $36 = 2x$ va $x = 18$. Burchak $5(18) + 12 = 102^\\\\circ$ ga teng (tekshiruv: $7(18) - 24 = 102^\\\\circ$). To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA ($16$) — burchaklar yig‘indisi $180^\\\\circ$ deb olingan: $12x - 12 = 180$ dan $x = 16$. B ($18$) — bu $x$ ning qiymati. C ($78$) — to‘g‘ri burchakni $180^\\\\circ$ gacha to‘ldiruvchi burchak.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Each exterior angle of a regular polygon measures $24^\\\\circ$. How many sides does the polygon have?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"15\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The exterior angles of any convex polygon, one at each vertex, add up to $360^\\\\circ$. In a regular polygon all of them are equal, so the number of sides is $\\\\frac{360}{24} = 15$.\\n\\nIf you got 7.5, you used $180^\\\\circ$ instead of $360^\\\\circ$. Using the interior angle instead: each interior angle is $180 - 24 = 156^\\\\circ$, and $\\\\frac{(15 - 2) \\\\cdot 180}{15} = 156$ confirms the answer.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har qanday qavariq ko‘pburchakning tashqi burchaklari (har bir uchda bittadan) yig‘indisi $360^\\\\circ$. Muntazam ko‘pburchakda ularning barchasi teng, demak tomonlar soni $\\\\frac{360}{24} = 15$.\\n\\nAgar 7.5 chiqqan bo‘lsa, $360^\\\\circ$ o‘rniga $180^\\\\circ$ olingan. Ichki burchak orqali tekshirish: har bir ichki burchak $180 - 24 = 156^\\\\circ$, va $\\\\frac{(15 - 2) \\\\cdot 180}{15} = 156$ javobni tasdiqlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A triangle has side lengths 6, 8, and 10 inches. A second triangle is similar to the first and has a perimeter of 60 inches. What is the length, in inches, of the shortest side of the second triangle?\",\"option_a\":\"$15$\",\"option_b\":\"$20$\",\"option_c\":\"$25$\",\"option_d\":\"$42$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first triangle has perimeter $6 + 8 + 10 = 24$ inches. Perimeters of similar triangles are in the same ratio as corresponding sides, so the scale factor is $\\\\frac{60}{24} = 2.5$. The shortest side of the second triangle is $6 \\\\cdot 2.5 = 15$ inches. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B ($20$) is the middle side, $8 \\\\cdot 2.5$ (it is also $\\\\frac{60}{3}$, as if the triangle were equilateral). Choice C ($25$) is the longest side, $10 \\\\cdot 2.5$. Choice D ($42$) adds the perimeter difference, $6 + 36$, instead of multiplying by a scale factor.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi uchburchak perimetri $6 + 8 + 10 = 24$ dyuym. O‘xshash uchburchaklar perimetrlari mos tomonlar kabi nisbatda bo‘ladi, demak o‘xshashlik koeffitsiyenti $\\\\frac{60}{24} = 2.5$. Ikkinchi uchburchakning eng qisqa tomoni $6 \\\\cdot 2.5 = 15$ dyuym. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB ($20$) — o‘rtacha tomon, $8 \\\\cdot 2.5$ (bu $\\\\frac{60}{3}$ ga ham teng, go‘yo uchburchak teng tomonli). C ($25$) — eng uzun tomon, $10 \\\\cdot 2.5$. D ($42$) — koeffitsiyentga ko‘paytirish o‘rniga perimetrlar farqi qo‘shilgan, $6 + 36$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In triangle $ABC$, $AB = AC$ and the measure of angle $BAC$ is $36^\\\\circ$. Point $D$ lies on side $\\\\overline{AC}$ so that $\\\\overline{BD}$ bisects angle $ABC$. What is the measure, in degrees, of angle $BDC$?\",\"option_a\":\"$36$\",\"option_b\":\"$72$\",\"option_c\":\"$90$\",\"option_d\":\"$108$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Because $AB = AC$, the base angles are equal: $\\\\angle ABC = \\\\angle ACB = \\\\frac{180 - 36}{2} = 72^\\\\circ$. The bisector splits angle $ABC$ into two $36^\\\\circ$ angles, so $\\\\angle ABD = 36^\\\\circ$. Angle $BDC$ is an exterior angle of triangle $ABD$, so it equals the sum of the two remote interior angles: $\\\\angle BAD + \\\\angle ABD = 36 + 36 = 72^\\\\circ$. (Check in triangle $BDC$: $36 + 72 + 72 = 180$.) Choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($36$) is the measure of angle $DBC$. Choice C ($90$) assumes the bisector is perpendicular to the opposite side, which is true only for the bisector of the vertex angle $A$. Choice D ($108$) is angle $ADB$, the supplement of angle $BDC$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$AB = AC$ bo‘lgani uchun asosdagi burchaklar teng: $\\\\angle ABC = \\\\angle ACB = \\\\frac{180 - 36}{2} = 72^\\\\circ$. Bissektrisa $ABC$ burchakni ikkita $36^\\\\circ$ li burchakka bo‘ladi, demak $\\\\angle ABD = 36^\\\\circ$. $BDC$ burchak $ABD$ uchburchakning tashqi burchagi, shuning uchun u o‘ziga qo‘shni bo‘lmagan ikki ichki burchak yig‘indisiga teng: $\\\\angle BAD + \\\\angle ABD = 36 + 36 = 72^\\\\circ$. (Tekshiruv, $BDC$ uchburchakda: $36 + 72 + 72 = 180$.) To‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA ($36$) — bu $DBC$ burchak. C ($90$) — bissektrisa qarama-qarshi tomonga perpendikulyar deb olingan, bu faqat uchidagi $A$ burchak bissektrisasi uchun to‘g‘ri. D ($108$) — bu $ADB$ burchak, $BDC$ burchakka qo‘shni burchak.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"lines_angles_triangles\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In triangle $ABC$, $AB = 12$ and $BC = 18$. Point $D$ lies on side $\\\\overline{BC}$ so that angle $BAD$ is congruent to angle $BCA$. What is the length of $\\\\overline{BD}$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"8\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Triangles $BAD$ and $BCA$ share angle $B$, and angle $BAD$ is congruent to angle $BCA$. By angle-angle similarity, triangle $BAD$ is similar to triangle $BCA$, with $B \\\\leftrightarrow B$, $A \\\\leftrightarrow C$, and $D \\\\leftrightarrow A$. Corresponding sides are proportional: $\\\\frac{BD}{BA} = \\\\frac{BA}{BC}$. So $\\\\frac{BD}{12} = \\\\frac{12}{18}$, and $BD = \\\\frac{144}{18} = 8$.\\n\\nIf you got 18 or 27, you matched the vertices in the wrong order (for example, writing $\\\\frac{BD}{BC} = \\\\frac{BA}{BA}$ or $\\\\frac{BD}{18} = \\\\frac{18}{12}$). Always match the congruent angles first: the angle at $A$ in the small triangle corresponds to the angle at $C$ in the large one.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$BAD$ va $BCA$ uchburchaklarda $B$ burchak umumiy, $BAD$ burchak esa $BCA$ burchakka teng. Ikki burchak bo‘yicha $BAD$ uchburchak $BCA$ uchburchakka o‘xshash, bunda $B \\\\leftrightarrow B$, $A \\\\leftrightarrow C$ va $D \\\\leftrightarrow A$. Mos tomonlar proporsional: $\\\\frac{BD}{BA} = \\\\frac{BA}{BC}$. Demak $\\\\frac{BD}{12} = \\\\frac{12}{18}$ va $BD = \\\\frac{144}{18} = 8$.\\n\\nAgar 18 yoki 27 chiqqan bo‘lsa, uchlar noto‘g‘ri moslashtirilgan (masalan, $\\\\frac{BD}{18} = \\\\frac{18}{12}$ deb yozilgan). Avval teng burchaklarni moslang: kichik uchburchakdagi $A$ burchak katta uchburchakdagi $C$ burchakka mos keladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What are all the solutions to the equation $x^2 = 7x$?\",\"option_a\":\"$7$ only\",\"option_b\":\"$-7$ and $0$\",\"option_c\":\"$-\\\\sqrt{7}$ and $\\\\sqrt{7}$\",\"option_d\":\"$0$ and $7$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Move all terms to one side and factor: $x^2 - 7x = 0$, so $x(x - 7) = 0$. By the zero product property, $x = 0$ or $x = 7$. Both check: $0^2 = 7(0)$ and $7^2 = 49 = 7(7)$.\\n\\nChoice A divides both sides by $x$, which loses the solution $x = 0$. Choice B uses the wrong sign when solving $x - 7 = 0$. Choice C treats the equation as $x^2 = 7$, ignoring the $x$ on the right side.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Barcha hadlarni bir tomonga o‘tkazib, ko‘paytuvchilarga ajratamiz: $x^2 - 7x = 0$, ya’ni $x(x - 7) = 0$. Ko‘paytma nolga teng bo‘lishi uchun $x = 0$ yoki $x = 7$. Ikkalasi ham tekshiruvdan o‘tadi: $0^2 = 7(0)$ va $7^2 = 49 = 7(7)$.\\n\\nA variantda ikkala tomon $x$ ga bo‘lingan, natijada $x = 0$ yechim yo‘qolgan. B variantda $x - 7 = 0$ yechilganda ishora xato olingan. C variantda tenglama $x^2 = 7$ deb qaralgan, o‘ng tomondagi $x$ e’tiborsiz qolgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$3(x + 2)^2 = 75$$\\n\\nWhat is the positive solution to the given equation?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Divide both sides by $3$: $(x + 2)^2 = 25$. Take the square root of both sides: $x + 2 = 5$ or $x + 2 = -5$. So $x = 3$ or $x = -7$. The positive solution is $3$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $23$, which comes from taking the square root of $25$ as if it were the equation $x + 2 = 25$. Another is entering $-7$, the negative solution.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomonni $3$ ga bo‘lamiz: $(x + 2)^2 = 25$. Ikkala tomondan kvadrat ildiz olamiz: $x + 2 = 5$ yoki $x + 2 = -5$. Demak, $x = 3$ yoki $x = -7$. Musbat yechim — $3$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — ildiz chiqarishni unutib, $x + 2 = 25$ deb $23$ ni kiritish. Yana bir xato — manfiy yechim $-7$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} y &= x^2 + 1 \\\\\\\\ y &= 10 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nWhich of the following points $(x, y)$ is a solution to the given system of equations?\",\"option_a\":\"$(10, 3)$\",\"option_b\":\"$(9, 10)$\",\"option_c\":\"$(3, 10)$\",\"option_d\":\"$(10, 101)$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $y = 10$ into the first equation: $10 = x^2 + 1$, so $x^2 = 9$ and $x = 3$ or $x = -3$. The solutions are $(3, 10)$ and $(-3, 10)$; only $(3, 10)$ is listed.\\n\\nChoice A reverses the coordinates. Choice B stops at $x^2 = 9$ and uses $9$ for $x$ without taking the square root. Choice D substitutes $x = 10$ into the first equation, but then $y = 101$ does not satisfy $y = 10$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi tenglamaga $y = 10$ ni qo‘yamiz: $10 = x^2 + 1$, demak $x^2 = 9$ va $x = 3$ yoki $x = -3$. Yechimlar $(3, 10)$ va $(-3, 10)$; ulardan faqat $(3, 10)$ variantlarda bor.\\n\\nA variantda koordinatalar o‘rni almashtirilgan. B variantda $x^2 = 9$ da to‘xtab, ildiz chiqarilmasdan $x$ uchun $9$ olingan. D variantda birinchi tenglamaga $x = 10$ qo‘yilgan, lekin $y = 101$ ikkinchi tenglama $y = 10$ ni qanoatlantirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What are all the solutions to the equation $\\\\sqrt{2x + 7} = x + 2$?\",\"option_a\":\"$1$ only\",\"option_b\":\"$-3$ only\",\"option_c\":\"$1$ and $-3$\",\"option_d\":\"There are no solutions.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Square both sides: $2x + 7 = (x + 2)^2 = x^2 + 4x + 4$. Rearrange: $x^2 + 2x - 3 = 0$, which factors as $(x + 3)(x - 1) = 0$, so $x = -3$ or $x = 1$.\\n\\nSquaring can create extraneous solutions, so check both in the original equation:\\n- $x = 1$: $\\\\sqrt{9} = 3$ and $1 + 2 = 3$. ✓\\n- $x = -3$: $\\\\sqrt{1} = 1$ but $-3 + 2 = -1$. ✗\\n\\nThe only solution is $1$.\\n\\nChoice C skips the check and keeps the extraneous value $-3$. Choice B keeps the wrong value. Choice D assumes that because one value fails, the equation has no solution.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomonni kvadratga oshiramiz: $2x + 7 = (x + 2)^2 = x^2 + 4x + 4$. Soddalashtiramiz: $x^2 + 2x - 3 = 0$, ya’ni $(x + 3)(x - 1) = 0$, demak $x = -3$ yoki $x = 1$.\\n\\nKvadratga oshirish chet yechim keltirib chiqarishi mumkin, shuning uchun ikkalasini dastlabki tenglamada tekshiramiz:\\n- $x = 1$: $\\\\sqrt{9} = 3$ va $1 + 2 = 3$. ✓\\n- $x = -3$: $\\\\sqrt{1} = 1$, lekin $-3 + 2 = -1$. ✗\\n\\nYagona yechim — $1$.\\n\\nC variantda tekshiruv o‘tkazilmay, chet yechim $-3$ ham qoldirilgan. B variantda noto‘g‘ri qiymat tanlangan. D variantda bitta qiymat tekshiruvdan o‘tmagani uchun tenglamaning yechimi yo‘q deb xulosa qilingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":100,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} y &= x^2 - 4x + 7 \\\\\\\\ y &= 2x - 2 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nThe given system of equations has exactly one solution, $(x, y)$. What is the value of $y$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Set the right sides equal: $x^2 - 4x + 7 = 2x - 2$. Rearrange: $x^2 - 6x + 9 = 0$, which is $(x - 3)^2 = 0$, so $x = 3$. Substitute into the linear equation: $y = 2(3) - 2 = 4$. Check in the first equation: $3^2 - 4(3) + 7 = 9 - 12 + 7 = 4$. ✓\\n\\nA common error is entering $3$, the $x$-coordinate, instead of $y$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"O‘ng tomonlarni tenglashtiramiz: $x^2 - 4x + 7 = 2x - 2$. Soddalashtiramiz: $x^2 - 6x + 9 = 0$, ya’ni $(x - 3)^2 = 0$, demak $x = 3$. Chiziqli tenglamaga qo‘yamiz: $y = 2(3) - 2 = 4$. Birinchi tenglamada tekshiramiz: $3^2 - 4(3) + 7 = 9 - 12 + 7 = 4$. ✓\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $y$ o‘rniga $x$ koordinatasi $3$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":95,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the solution to the equation $2^{x + 3} = 4^{x - 1}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$4$\",\"option_b\":\"$5$\",\"option_c\":\"$-7$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\dfrac{7}{3}$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Write both sides with base $2$: $4^{x - 1} = (2^2)^{x - 1} = 2^{2(x - 1)} = 2^{2x - 2}$. Now $2^{x + 3} = 2^{2x - 2}$, so the exponents are equal: $x + 3 = 2x - 2$, which gives $x = 5$. Check: $2^8 = 256$ and $4^4 = 256$. ✓\\n\\nChoice A distributes incorrectly, writing $2(x - 1)$ as $2x - 1$. Choice C doubles the left exponent instead of the right one: $2(x + 3) = x - 1$. Choice D multiplies the exponent by $4$ instead of $2$: $x + 3 = 4(x - 1)$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala tomonni $2$ asosda yozamiz: $4^{x - 1} = (2^2)^{x - 1} = 2^{2(x - 1)} = 2^{2x - 2}$. Endi $2^{x + 3} = 2^{2x - 2}$, demak ko‘rsatkichlar teng: $x + 3 = 2x - 2$, bundan $x = 5$. Tekshiruv: $2^8 = 256$ va $4^4 = 256$. ✓\\n\\nA variantda qavs noto‘g‘ri ochilgan: $2(x - 1)$ o‘rniga $2x - 1$ yozilgan. C variantda o‘ng emas, chap ko‘rsatkich ikkiga ko‘paytirilgan: $2(x + 3) = x - 1$. D variantda ko‘rsatkich $2$ ga emas, $4$ ga ko‘paytirilgan: $x + 3 = 4(x - 1)$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":95,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} x^2 + y^2 &= 25 \\\\\\\\ y &= x + 1 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIf $(a, b)$ is a solution to the given system of equations and $a > 0$, what is the value of $b$?\",\"option_a\":\"$3$\",\"option_b\":\"$-3$\",\"option_c\":\"$4$\",\"option_d\":\"$-4$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $y = x + 1$ into the first equation: $x^2 + (x + 1)^2 = 25$, so $x^2 + x^2 + 2x + 1 = 25$, or $2x^2 + 2x - 24 = 0$. Divide by $2$: $x^2 + x - 12 = 0$, which factors as $(x + 4)(x - 3) = 0$. So $x = 3$ or $x = -4$.\\n\\nSince $a > 0$, $a = 3$ and $b = 3 + 1 = 4$. Check: $3^2 + 4^2 = 9 + 16 = 25$. ✓\\n\\nChoice A gives the value of $a$, not $b$. Choice B is the $y$-value of the other solution, $(-4, -3)$. Choice D is the $x$-value of that other solution.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi tenglamaga $y = x + 1$ ni qo‘yamiz: $x^2 + (x + 1)^2 = 25$, ya’ni $x^2 + x^2 + 2x + 1 = 25$ yoki $2x^2 + 2x - 24 = 0$. $2$ ga bo‘lamiz: $x^2 + x - 12 = 0$, ya’ni $(x + 4)(x - 3) = 0$. Demak, $x = 3$ yoki $x = -4$.\\n\\n$a > 0$ bo‘lgani uchun $a = 3$ va $b = 3 + 1 = 4$. Tekshiruv: $3^2 + 4^2 = 9 + 16 = 25$. ✓\\n\\nA variant — $b$ emas, $a$ ning qiymati. B variant — ikkinchi yechim $(-4, -3)$ ning $y$ qiymati. D variant — o‘sha ikkinchi yechimning $x$ qiymati.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_equations_systems\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\dfrac{x}{x - 2} - \\\\dfrac{8}{x^2 - 4} = \\\\dfrac{3}{x + 2}$$\\n\\nWhat is the solution to the given equation?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-1\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Note that $x^2 - 4 = (x - 2)(x + 2)$, so $x \\\\ne 2$ and $x \\\\ne -2$. Multiply both sides by $(x - 2)(x + 2)$: $x(x + 2) - 8 = 3(x - 2)$. Expand: $x^2 + 2x - 8 = 3x - 6$. Rearrange: $x^2 - x - 2 = 0$, which factors as $(x - 2)(x + 1) = 0$. So $x = 2$ or $x = -1$.\\n\\nThe value $x = 2$ makes the denominators $x - 2$ and $x^2 - 4$ equal to zero, so it is extraneous. Check $x = -1$: $\\\\dfrac{-1}{-3} - \\\\dfrac{8}{-3} = \\\\dfrac{9}{3} = 3$ and $\\\\dfrac{3}{1} = 3$. ✓ The solution is $-1$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $2$, which comes from not checking the solutions against the restrictions on $x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"E’tibor bering: $x^2 - 4 = (x - 2)(x + 2)$, demak $x \\\\ne 2$ va $x \\\\ne -2$. Ikkala tomonni $(x - 2)(x + 2)$ ga ko‘paytiramiz: $x(x + 2) - 8 = 3(x - 2)$. Qavslarni ochamiz: $x^2 + 2x - 8 = 3x - 6$. Soddalashtiramiz: $x^2 - x - 2 = 0$, ya’ni $(x - 2)(x + 1) = 0$. Demak, $x = 2$ yoki $x = -1$.\\n\\n$x = 2$ da $x - 2$ va $x^2 - 4$ maxrajlar nolga aylanadi, shuning uchun bu chet yechim. $x = -1$ ni tekshiramiz: $\\\\dfrac{-1}{-3} - \\\\dfrac{8}{-3} = \\\\dfrac{9}{3} = 3$ va $\\\\dfrac{3}{1} = 3$. ✓ Yechim — $-1$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — yechimlarni $x$ ga qo‘yilgan cheklovlar bilan tekshirmay, $2$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":140,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = x^3 - 4x$. What is the value of $g(-3)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$-15$\",\"option_b\":\"$15$\",\"option_c\":\"$-39$\",\"option_d\":\"$39$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $-3$ for $x$, keeping it in parentheses: $g(-3) = (-3)^3 - 4(-3) = -27 + 12 = -15$.\\n\\nChoice B evaluates $(-3)^3$ as $+27$ and then subtracts $12$; an odd power of a negative number is negative. Choice C treats $-4(-3)$ as $-12$ instead of $+12$. Choice D makes both sign errors: $27 + 12$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x$ o‘rniga $-3$ ni qavs ichida qo‘yamiz: $g(-3) = (-3)^3 - 4(-3) = -27 + 12 = -15$.\\n\\nB variantda $(-3)^3$ musbat $27$ deb olinib, undan $12$ ayirilgan; manfiy sonning toq darajasi manfiy bo‘ladi. C variantda $-4(-3)$ ning qiymati $+12$ o‘rniga $-12$ deb olingan. D variantda ikkala ishora xatosi birga qilingan: $27 + 12$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The value $V$, in dollars, of a used car $t$ years after it was purchased is modeled by the function $V(t) = 18{,}000(0.88)^t$. What is the best interpretation of $18{,}000$ in this context?\",\"option_a\":\"The car loses $18{,}000$ dollars of its value each year.\",\"option_b\":\"The value of the car, in dollars, when it was purchased\",\"option_c\":\"The value of the car, in dollars, $1$ year after it was purchased\",\"option_d\":\"The number of years it takes for the car to lose all of its value\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"When $t = 0$, $V(0) = 18{,}000(0.88)^0 = 18{,}000(1) = 18{,}000$. So $18{,}000$ is the value of the car, in dollars, at the moment it was purchased.\\n\\nChoice A describes a linear model; in this exponential model the car loses $12\\\\%$ of its value each year, not a fixed amount. Choice C would be $V(1) = 18{,}000(0.88) = 15{,}840$ dollars. Choice D is wrong because an exponential decay model never reaches $0$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$t = 0$ da $V(0) = 18{,}000(0.88)^0 = 18{,}000(1) = 18{,}000$. Demak, $18{,}000$ — avtomobil sotib olingan paytdagi qiymati (dollarda).\\n\\nA variant chiziqli modelni tasvirlaydi; bu ko‘rsatkichli modelda avtomobil har yili belgilangan miqdorni emas, qiymatining $12\\\\%$ ini yo‘qotadi. C variant — bu $V(1) = 18{,}000(0.88) = 15{,}840$ dollar bo‘lardi. D variant noto‘g‘ri, chunki ko‘rsatkichli kamayish modeli hech qachon $0$ ga yetmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 4x^2 - 1$. If $f(a) = 35$ and $a > 0$, what is the value of $a$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Set $f(a) = 35$: $4a^2 - 1 = 35$. Add $1$: $4a^2 = 36$. Divide by $4$: $a^2 = 9$. So $a = 3$ or $a = -3$, and since $a > 0$, $a = 3$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $9$, the value of $a^2$, without taking the square root. Another is entering $\\\\pm 3$ or $-3$; the condition $a > 0$ rules out the negative value.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$f(a) = 35$ deb olamiz: $4a^2 - 1 = 35$. $1$ ni qo‘shamiz: $4a^2 = 36$. $4$ ga bo‘lamiz: $a^2 = 9$. Demak, $a = 3$ yoki $a = -3$, va $a > 0$ bo‘lgani uchun $a = 3$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — ildiz chiqarmasdan $a^2$ ning qiymati $9$ ni kiritish. Yana bir xato — $-3$ ni kiritish; $a > 0$ sharti manfiy qiymatni chiqarib tashlaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = -2(x - 5)^2 + 8$. What is the $y$-coordinate of the $y$-intercept of the graph of $y = f(x)$ in the $xy$-plane?\",\"option_a\":\"$8$\",\"option_b\":\"$58$\",\"option_c\":\"$-42$\",\"option_d\":\"$-92$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The $y$-intercept occurs where $x = 0$: $f(0) = -2(0 - 5)^2 + 8 = -2(25) + 8 = -50 + 8 = -42$.\\n\\nChoice A is the $y$-coordinate of the vertex, $(5, 8)$, not the $y$-intercept. Choice B drops the negative sign of the coefficient: $2(25) + 8$. Choice D multiplies $-2$ by $-5$ before squaring: $-(10)^2 + 8$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y$ o‘qini kesish nuqtasida $x = 0$: $f(0) = -2(0 - 5)^2 + 8 = -2(25) + 8 = -50 + 8 = -42$.\\n\\nA variant — $y$ o‘qini kesish nuqtasi emas, parabola uchi $(5, 8)$ ning $y$ koordinatasi. B variantda koeffitsiyentning minus ishorasi tashlab yuborilgan: $2(25) + 8$. D variantda kvadratga oshirishdan oldin $-2$ ni $-5$ ga ko‘paytirilgan: $-(10)^2 + 8$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = a(b)^x$, where $a$ and $b$ are positive constants. If $f(0) = 6$ and $f(2) = 54$, which of the following defines $f$?\",\"option_a\":\"$f(x) = 6(9)^x$\",\"option_b\":\"$f(x) = 3(6)^x$\",\"option_c\":\"$f(x) = 6(24)^x$\",\"option_d\":\"$f(x) = 6(3)^x$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Since $b^0 = 1$, $f(0) = a = 6$. Then $f(2) = 6b^2 = 54$, so $b^2 = 9$ and, because $b > 0$, $b = 3$. Therefore $f(x) = 6(3)^x$. Check: $f(2) = 6 \\\\cdot 9 = 54$. ✓\\n\\nChoice A uses $b^2 = 9$ as the base without taking the square root; then $f(2) = 6 \\\\cdot 81 = 486$. Choice B swaps the roles of $a$ and $b$. Choice C uses the difference $54 - 6 = 48$ divided by $2$ as the base, mixing up a linear rate of change with a growth factor.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$b^0 = 1$ bo‘lgani uchun $f(0) = a = 6$. So‘ng $f(2) = 6b^2 = 54$, demak $b^2 = 9$ va $b > 0$ bo‘lgani uchun $b = 3$. Shunday qilib, $f(x) = 6(3)^x$. Tekshiruv: $f(2) = 6 \\\\cdot 9 = 54$. ✓\\n\\nA variantda ildiz chiqarilmasdan $b^2 = 9$ asos sifatida olingan; u holda $f(2) = 6 \\\\cdot 81 = 486$ bo‘lardi. B variantda $a$ va $b$ ning o‘rni almashtirilgan. C variantda asos sifatida $54 - 6 = 48$ ayirmaning yarmi olingan, ya’ni chiziqli o‘zgarish tezligi o‘sish ko‘paytuvchisi bilan adashtirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":95,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of $y = x^2 - 8x + k$, where $k$ is a constant, has exactly one $x$-intercept. What is the value of $k$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"16\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The graph has exactly one $x$-intercept when the equation $x^2 - 8x + k = 0$ has exactly one real solution, that is, when its discriminant is $0$: $(-8)^2 - 4(1)(k) = 0$, so $64 - 4k = 0$ and $k = 16$.\\n\\nAlternatively, $x^2 - 8x + 16 = (x - 4)^2$, a perfect square whose graph touches the $x$-axis only at $(4, 0)$.\\n\\nA common error is entering $64$, which sets $b^2 = k$ and forgets the factor $4a$. Another is entering $4$, the $x$-coordinate of the vertex.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Grafik $x$ o‘qini faqat bitta nuqtada kesishi uchun $x^2 - 8x + k = 0$ tenglama yagona haqiqiy yechimga ega bo‘lishi, ya’ni diskriminant $0$ bo‘lishi kerak: $(-8)^2 - 4(1)(k) = 0$, demak $64 - 4k = 0$ va $k = 16$.\\n\\nBoshqa usul: $x^2 - 8x + 16 = (x - 4)^2$ — to‘liq kvadrat, uning grafigi $x$ o‘qiga faqat $(4, 0)$ nuqtada tegadi.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $4a$ ko‘paytuvchini unutib, $b^2 = k$ deb $64$ ni kiritish. Yana bir xato — parabola uchining $x$ koordinatasi $4$ ni kiritish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":95,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 2^x$. The function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = f(x + 3) - 5$. Which of the following is an equivalent form of $g(x)$?\",\"option_a\":\"$g(x) = 2^x - 2$\",\"option_b\":\"$g(x) = 8(2)^x - 5$\",\"option_c\":\"$g(x) = 6(2)^x - 5$\",\"option_d\":\"$g(x) = \\\\dfrac{1}{8}(2)^x - 5$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Replace $x$ with $x + 3$ in $f$: $f(x + 3) = 2^{x + 3}$. By the product rule for exponents, $2^{x + 3} = 2^x \\\\cdot 2^3 = 8(2)^x$. So $g(x) = 8(2)^x - 5$.\\n\\nChoice A adds $3$ to the output instead of the input, giving $2^x + 3 - 5$. Choice C multiplies $2 \\\\cdot 3$ instead of computing $2^3$. Choice D uses $f(x - 3) = 2^{x - 3} = \\\\frac{1}{8}(2)^x$, shifting in the wrong direction.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$f$ dagi $x$ ni $x + 3$ bilan almashtiramiz: $f(x + 3) = 2^{x + 3}$. Darajalar ko‘paytmasi qoidasiga ko‘ra $2^{x + 3} = 2^x \\\\cdot 2^3 = 8(2)^x$. Demak, $g(x) = 8(2)^x - 5$.\\n\\nA variantda $3$ argumentga emas, funksiya qiymatiga qo‘shilgan: $2^x + 3 - 5$. C variantda $2^3$ o‘rniga $2 \\\\cdot 3$ hisoblangan. D variantda $f(x - 3) = 2^{x - 3} = \\\\frac{1}{8}(2)^x$ olingan, ya’ni siljish noto‘g‘ri yo‘nalishda bajarilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"nonlinear_functions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = a(b)^x$, where $a$ and $b$ are positive constants. If $f(1) = 12$ and $f(3) = 108$, what is the value of $f(-1)$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"4/3\",\"1.333\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Divide the two given values: $\\\\dfrac{f(3)}{f(1)} = \\\\dfrac{ab^3}{ab} = b^2 = \\\\dfrac{108}{12} = 9$. Since $b > 0$, $b = 3$. Then $f(1) = 3a = 12$, so $a = 4$ and $f(x) = 4(3)^x$.\\n\\nTherefore $f(-1) = 4(3)^{-1} = \\\\dfrac{4}{3}$, which can be entered as 4/3 or 1.333.\\n\\nA common error is entering $4$, which is $f(0) = a$ rather than $f(-1)$. Another is entering $-12$, which assumes $f(-1) = -f(1)$; exponential functions do not behave this way.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Berilgan ikki qiymatni bo‘lamiz: $\\\\dfrac{f(3)}{f(1)} = \\\\dfrac{ab^3}{ab} = b^2 = \\\\dfrac{108}{12} = 9$. $b > 0$ bo‘lgani uchun $b = 3$. So‘ng $f(1) = 3a = 12$, demak $a = 4$ va $f(x) = 4(3)^x$.\\n\\nShunday qilib, $f(-1) = 4(3)^{-1} = \\\\dfrac{4}{3}$; javobni 4/3 yoki 1.333 ko‘rinishida kiritish mumkin.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato — $f(-1)$ o‘rniga $f(0) = a$ qiymati $4$ ni kiritish. Yana bir xato — $f(-1) = -f(1)$ deb $-12$ ni kiritish; ko‘rsatkichli funksiyalar bunday xossaga ega emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":140,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The list shows the high temperature, in degrees Celsius, in a town on each of 7 days.\\n\\n18, 22, 19, 25, 21, 17, 23\\n\\nWhat is the median high temperature, in degrees Celsius, for these 7 days?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"21\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Order the values from least to greatest: 17, 18, 19, 21, 22, 23, 25. With 7 values, the median is the 4th value, which is 21. Choosing the middle value of the list **as written** gives 25, which is wrong because the values must be ordered first. The mean, $\\\\frac{145}{7} \\\\approx 20.7$, is a different measure of center. Enter 21.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qiymatlarni o‘sish tartibida yozamiz: 17, 18, 19, 21, 22, 23, 25. 7 ta qiymat bo‘lgani uchun mediana 4-qiymat, ya’ni 21. Ro‘yxatning **berilgan holatdagi** o‘rtasidagi qiymatni olish 25 ni beradi — bu xato, chunki avval qiymatlarni tartiblash kerak. O‘rta arifmetik $\\\\frac{145}{7} \\\\approx 20.7$ esa boshqa markaziy ko‘rsatkich. Javob maydoniga 21 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The masses, in kilograms, of 6 melons are 3.2, 4.8, 2.9, 5.1, 3.7, and 4.4. What is the range of these masses, in kilograms?\",\"option_a\":\"$2.2$\",\"option_b\":\"$1.2$\",\"option_c\":\"$1.9$\",\"option_d\":\"$8.0$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The range is the greatest value minus the least value: $5.1 - 2.9 = 2.2$ kilograms. Choice B subtracts the first listed value from the last listed value, $4.4 - 3.2$, instead of using the greatest and least values. Choice C uses the greatest value but the first listed value, $5.1 - 3.2$. Choice D adds the greatest and least values instead of subtracting.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Qamrov — eng katta va eng kichik qiymatlar ayirmasi: $5.1 - 2.9 = 2.2$ kilogramm. B javob eng katta va eng kichik qiymat o‘rniga ro‘yxatdagi oxirgi va birinchi qiymatlarni ayirgan: $4.4 - 3.2$. C javob eng katta qiymatni, lekin ro‘yxatdagi birinchi qiymatni olgan: $5.1 - 3.2$. D javob eng katta va eng kichik qiymatlarni ayirish o‘rniga qo‘shgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"What is the mode of the shoe sizes of these students?\",\"passage\":\"The table shows the shoe sizes of the 25 students in a class.\\n\\n| Shoe size | Number of students |\\n| ---: | ---: |\\n| 36 | 3 |\\n| 37 | 5 |\\n| 38 | 9 |\\n| 39 | 6 |\\n| 40 | 2 |\",\"option_a\":\"$5$\",\"option_b\":\"$9$\",\"option_c\":\"$40$\",\"option_d\":\"$38$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The mode is the value that occurs most often. The greatest number of students, 9, wear size 38, so the mode is 38. Choice B, 9, is how many students wear the most common size, not the size itself. Choice A is the number of different sizes in the table, and choice C is the largest size.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Moda — eng ko‘p uchraydigan qiymat. Eng ko‘p o‘quvchi (9 nafar) 38-o‘lchamdagi poyabzal kiyadi, demak moda 38. B javob (9) — o‘lchamning o‘zi emas, eng ko‘p uchraydigan o‘lchamni kiyadigan o‘quvchilar soni. A javob — jadvaldagi turli o‘lchamlar soni, C javob esa eng katta o‘lcham.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following statements about the means and standard deviations of the scores of the two archers is true?\",\"passage\":\"Two archers each shot 5 arrows at a target. Their scores are shown.\\n\\n- Dilnoza: 7, 8, 8, 8, 9\\n- Sardor: 4, 6, 8, 10, 12\",\"option_a\":\"The means are equal, and the standard deviation of Dilnoza's scores is greater.\",\"option_b\":\"The means are equal, and the standard deviation of Sardor's scores is greater.\",\"option_c\":\"The mean of Dilnoza's scores is greater, and the standard deviations are equal.\",\"option_d\":\"The mean of Sardor's scores is greater, and the standard deviation of Sardor's scores is greater.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Both means equal 8: $\\\\frac{7 + 8 + 8 + 8 + 9}{5} = \\\\frac{40}{5} = 8$ and $\\\\frac{4 + 6 + 8 + 10 + 12}{5} = \\\\frac{40}{5} = 8$. Standard deviation measures how spread out the values are from the mean. Dilnoza's scores are all within 1 point of 8, while Sardor's scores are as far as 4 points from 8, so Sardor's scores have the greater standard deviation. Choice A reverses the spreads. Choices C and D claim different means, but both means are 8; Sardor's larger values (10 and 12) are balanced by his smaller values (4 and 6).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala o‘rta qiymat ham 8 ga teng: $\\\\frac{7 + 8 + 8 + 8 + 9}{5} = \\\\frac{40}{5} = 8$ va $\\\\frac{4 + 6 + 8 + 10 + 12}{5} = \\\\frac{40}{5} = 8$. Standart chetlanish qiymatlar o‘rta qiymat atrofida qanchalik tarqalganini o‘lchaydi. Dilnozaning barcha ballari 8 dan ko‘pi bilan 1 ballga farq qiladi, Sardorning ballari esa 8 dan 4 ballgacha uzoqlashadi, demak Sardorning ballari standart chetlanishi kattaroq. A javobda tarqoqliklar teskari olingan. C va D javoblar o‘rta qiymatlar har xil deydi, lekin ikkalasi ham 8: Sardorning katta qiymatlari (10 va 12) kichik qiymatlari (4 va 6) bilan muvozanatlashadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Aziz took 5 tests. His scores on the first 4 tests were 82, 75, 90, and 68. The mean of his scores on all 5 tests was 80. What was his score on the fifth test?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"85\"],\"explanation_en\":\"If the mean of 5 scores is 80, the sum of the 5 scores is $5 \\\\times 80 = 400$. The first 4 scores add up to $82 + 75 + 90 + 68 = 315$, so the fifth score is $400 - 315 = 85$. Check: $\\\\frac{315 + 85}{5} = 80$. Entering 78.75, the mean of the first 4 scores, does not answer the question. Enter 85.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Agar 5 ta ballning o‘rta qiymati 80 bo‘lsa, ularning yig‘indisi $5 \\\\times 80 = 400$. Dastlabki 4 ta ball yig‘indisi $82 + 75 + 90 + 68 = 315$, demak beshinchi ball $400 - 315 = 85$. Tekshiruv: $\\\\frac{315 + 85}{5} = 80$. 78.75 (dastlabki 4 ta ballning o‘rtachasi) savolga javob emas. Javob maydoniga 85 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"The prices, in thousands of soums, of 7 notebooks in a shop are 8, 9, 9, 10, 11, 12, and 45. If the notebook that costs 45 thousand soums is removed from the data, which of the following best describes how the mean and the median of the prices change?\",\"option_a\":\"Only the mean decreases; the median does not change.\",\"option_b\":\"Both the mean and the median decrease, and the mean decreases by more.\",\"option_c\":\"Both the mean and the median decrease by the same amount.\",\"option_d\":\"Both the mean and the median decrease, and the median decreases by more.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Before the change, the mean is $\\\\frac{104}{7} \\\\approx 14.9$ and the median (the 4th of 7 values) is 10. After removing 45, the mean is $\\\\frac{59}{6} \\\\approx 9.8$, and the median of the 6 remaining values is $\\\\frac{9 + 10}{2} = 9.5$. Both decrease: the mean by about 5.0 and the median by 0.5, so the mean decreases by more. Removing an extreme value strongly affects the mean but changes the median only a little. Choice A forgets that with an even number of values the median is the average of the two middle values. Choices C and D misjudge how much an outlier affects each measure.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"O‘zgarishdan oldin o‘rta qiymat $\\\\frac{104}{7} \\\\approx 14.9$, mediana (7 ta qiymatning 4-si) esa 10. 45 olib tashlangach, o‘rta qiymat $\\\\frac{59}{6} \\\\approx 9.8$, qolgan 6 ta qiymatning medianasi $\\\\frac{9 + 10}{2} = 9.5$. Ikkalasi ham kamayadi: o‘rta qiymat taxminan 5.0 ga, mediana 0.5 ga, demak o‘rta qiymat ko‘proq kamayadi. Keskin farq qiluvchi qiymatni olib tashlash o‘rta qiymatga kuchli ta’sir qiladi, medianani esa ozgina o‘zgartiradi. A javob qiymatlar soni juft bo‘lganda mediana ikki o‘rta qiymatning o‘rtachasi ekanini unutgan. C va D javoblar chetdagi qiymat har bir ko‘rsatkichga qanchalik ta’sir qilishini noto‘g‘ri baholagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A data set consists of 10 numbers. The mean of the data set is 16, and the median is 14. A new data set is created by multiplying each number in the original data set by 3 and then subtracting 2 from each result. What are the mean and the median of the new data set?\",\"option_a\":\"Mean: 48; median: 42\",\"option_b\":\"Mean: 42; median: 36\",\"option_c\":\"Mean: 46; median: 40\",\"option_d\":\"Mean: 46; median: 42\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Multiplying every value by 3 multiplies the mean and the median by 3, and subtracting 2 from every value subtracts 2 from the mean and the median. New mean: $3(16) - 2 = 46$. New median: $3(14) - 2 = 40$. Choice A multiplies by 3 but forgets to subtract 2. Choice B subtracts 2 **before** multiplying: $3(16 - 2) = 42$ and $3(14 - 2) = 36$. Choice D transforms the mean correctly but only multiplies the median.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Har bir qiymatni 3 ga ko‘paytirish o‘rta qiymat va medianani 3 ga ko‘paytiradi, har bir qiymatdan 2 ni ayirish esa o‘rta qiymat va medianadan 2 ni ayiradi. Yangi o‘rta qiymat: $3(16) - 2 = 46$. Yangi mediana: $3(14) - 2 = 40$. A javob 3 ga ko‘paytirgan, lekin 2 ni ayirishni unutgan. B javob 2 ni ko‘paytirishdan **oldin** ayirgan: $3(16 - 2) = 42$ va $3(14 - 2) = 36$. D javob o‘rta qiymatni to‘g‘ri o‘zgartirgan, medianani esa faqat 3 ga ko‘paytirgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"one_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"The table shows the number of books read last month by each member of a reading club. The mean number of books read per member is 1.6. What is the value of $k$?\",\"passage\":\"A reading club recorded how many books each of its members read last month.\\n\\n| Number of books | Number of members |\\n| ---: | ---: |\\n| 0 | 4 |\\n| 1 | $k$ |\\n| 2 | 6 |\\n| 3 | 5 |\",\"spr_answers\":[\"5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The number of members is $4 + k + 6 + 5 = 15 + k$, and the total number of books is $0(4) + 1(k) + 2(6) + 3(5) = k + 27$. Since the mean is 1.6, $\\\\frac{k + 27}{15 + k} = 1.6$. Then $k + 27 = 24 + 1.6k$, so $3 = 0.6k$ and $k = 5$. Check: $\\\\frac{32}{20} = 1.6$. A common error is to divide the total by the 4 rows of the table instead of by the number of members. Enter 5.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"A’zolar soni $4 + k + 6 + 5 = 15 + k$, kitoblarning umumiy soni esa $0(4) + 1(k) + 2(6) + 3(5) = k + 27$. O‘rta qiymat 1.6 bo‘lgani uchun $\\\\frac{k + 27}{15 + k} = 1.6$. Bundan $k + 27 = 24 + 1.6k$, ya’ni $3 = 0.6k$ va $k = 5$. Tekshiruv: $\\\\frac{32}{20} = 1.6$. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — umumiy sonni a’zolar soniga emas, jadvaldagi 4 ta qatorga bo‘lish. Javob maydoniga 5 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A fruit seller had 75 kilograms of apples. Of these apples, 40% by weight were green apples. How many kilograms of green apples did the seller have?\",\"option_a\":\"$45$\",\"option_b\":\"$30$\",\"option_c\":\"$35$\",\"option_d\":\"$105$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Find 40% of 75: $0.40 \\\\times 75 = 30$ kilograms. Choice A, 45, is the weight of the apples that are **not** green (60% of 75). Choice C subtracts 40 from 75, treating the percent as a number of kilograms. Choice D increases 75 by 40% ($1.40 \\\\times 75$) instead of finding 40% of 75.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"75 ning 40% ini topamiz: $0.40 \\\\times 75 = 30$ kilogramm. A javob (45) — yashil **bo‘lmagan** olmalar og‘irligi (75 ning 60% i). C javob foizni kilogramm deb olib, 75 dan 40 ni ayirgan. D javob 75 ning 40% ini topish o‘rniga 75 ni 40% ga oshirgan ($1.40 \\\\times 75$).\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A jacket normally costs 250 thousand soums. During a sale, the price of the jacket is reduced by 20%. What is the sale price of the jacket, in thousands of soums?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"200\"],\"explanation_en\":\"A 20% decrease multiplies the price by $1 - 0.20 = 0.80$: $250 \\\\times 0.80 = 200$. (The discount itself is $0.20 \\\\times 250 = 50$ thousand soums.) Entering 50 gives only the amount of the discount, and entering 230 subtracts 20 instead of 20%. Enter 200.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"20% ga kamayish narxni $1 - 0.20 = 0.80$ ga ko‘paytiradi: $250 \\\\times 0.80 = 200$. (Chegirmaning o‘zi $0.20 \\\\times 250 = 50$ ming so‘m.) 50 deb yozsangiz, bu faqat chegirma miqdori bo‘ladi; 230 esa 20% emas, 20 ni ayirish natijasi. Javob maydoniga 200 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In a class of 25 students, 9 students wear glasses. What percent of the students in the class wear glasses?\",\"option_a\":\"$9\\\\%$\",\"option_b\":\"$16\\\\%$\",\"option_c\":\"$36\\\\%$\",\"option_d\":\"$64\\\\%$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The percent is $\\\\frac{9}{25} \\\\times 100\\\\% = 0.36 \\\\times 100\\\\% = 36\\\\%$. Choice A uses the number of students, 9, as the percent. Choice B, 16%, comes from $25 - 9 = 16$, the number of students who do not wear glasses. Choice D, 64%, is the percent of students who do **not** wear glasses.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Foiz: $\\\\frac{9}{25} \\\\times 100\\\\% = 0.36 \\\\times 100\\\\% = 36\\\\%$. A javob o‘quvchilar soni 9 ni foiz deb olgan. B javob (16%) $25 - 9 = 16$ dan kelib chiqqan — bu ko‘zoynak taqmaydigan o‘quvchilar soni. D javob (64%) — ko‘zoynak **taqmaydigan** o‘quvchilar foizi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A farm harvested 1,250 kilograms of cotton in 2024 and 1,000 kilograms of cotton in 2025. The 2025 harvest was what percent less than the 2024 harvest?\",\"option_a\":\"$20\\\\%$\",\"option_b\":\"$25\\\\%$\",\"option_c\":\"$75\\\\%$\",\"option_d\":\"$80\\\\%$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Percent decrease $= \\\\frac{\\\\text{decrease}}{\\\\text{original}} \\\\times 100\\\\%$. The decrease is $1{,}250 - 1{,}000 = 250$ kilograms, and the original amount is the 2024 harvest, so $\\\\frac{250}{1{,}250} = 0.20$, or 20%. Choice B divides by the 2025 harvest ($\\\\frac{250}{1{,}000}$), which gives the percent by which 2024 was greater than 2025. Choice D, 80%, is the 2025 harvest as a percent **of** the 2024 harvest, not the percent decrease. Choice C is $100\\\\% - 25\\\\%$, combining two errors.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Foizli kamayish $= \\\\frac{\\\\text{kamayish}}{\\\\text{dastlabki qiymat}} \\\\times 100\\\\%$. Kamayish $1{,}250 - 1{,}000 = 250$ kilogramm, dastlabki qiymat esa 2024-yilgi hosil: $\\\\frac{250}{1{,}250} = 0.20$, ya’ni 20%. B javob 2025-yilgi hosilga bo‘lgan ($\\\\frac{250}{1{,}000}$) — bu 2024-yil 2025-yildan necha foiz ko‘p ekanini bildiradi. D javob (80%) — 2025-yilgi hosilning 2024-yilgi hosilga **nisbatan** foizi, kamayish foizi emas. C javob $100\\\\% - 25\\\\%$ — ikki xato birlashgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"After a 15% discount, a pair of sneakers costs 340 thousand soums. What was the price of the sneakers before the discount, in thousands of soums?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"400\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let $x$ be the original price. After a 15% discount, the price is $0.85x$, so $0.85x = 340$ and $x = \\\\frac{340}{0.85} = 400$. A common error is to add 15% of 340 to 340: $1.15 \\\\times 340 = 391$. That is wrong because the 15% was taken of the **original** price, not of 340. Check: $0.85 \\\\times 400 = 340$. Enter 400.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Dastlabki narxni $x$ deb olamiz. 15% chegirmadan keyin narx $0.85x$ bo‘ladi, demak $0.85x = 340$ va $x = \\\\frac{340}{0.85} = 400$. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — 340 ga uning 15% ini qo‘shish: $1.15 \\\\times 340 = 391$. Bu noto‘g‘ri, chunki 15% 340 dan emas, **dastlabki** narxdan olingan. Tekshiruv: $0.85 \\\\times 400 = 340$. Javob maydoniga 400 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In a survey of 800 households in a district, 45% of the households own a car. Of the households that own a car, 30% own an electric car. How many of the surveyed households own an electric car?\",\"option_a\":\"$240$\",\"option_b\":\"$360$\",\"option_c\":\"$252$\",\"option_d\":\"$108$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"First, the number of households that own a car is $0.45 \\\\times 800 = 360$. Then 30% of these own an electric car: $0.30 \\\\times 360 = 108$. (Equivalently, $0.45 \\\\times 0.30 \\\\times 800 = 108$.) Choice A takes 30% of all 800 households, ignoring that the 30% applies only to car owners. Choice B is the number of car owners. Choice C, $360 - 108 = 252$, is the number of car owners who do **not** own an electric car.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Avval avtomobilga ega xonadonlar sonini topamiz: $0.45 \\\\times 800 = 360$. Ularning 30% ida elektromobil bor: $0.30 \\\\times 360 = 108$. (Yoki $0.45 \\\\times 0.30 \\\\times 800 = 108$.) A javob barcha 800 xonadonning 30% ini olgan, holbuki 30% faqat avtomobil egalariga tegishli. B javob — avtomobil egalari soni. C javob ($360 - 108 = 252$) — elektromobili **bo‘lmagan** avtomobil egalari soni.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A chemist has 40 liters of a salt solution that is 15% salt by volume. How many liters of pure water must be added to the solution to make a solution that is 10% salt by volume?\",\"option_a\":\"$4$\",\"option_b\":\"$6$\",\"option_c\":\"$20$\",\"option_d\":\"$60$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The amount of salt does not change when water is added: $0.15 \\\\times 40 = 6$ liters of salt. If $w$ liters of water are added, the new volume is $40 + w$, and salt must be 10% of it: $0.10(40 + w) = 6$, so $40 + w = 60$ and $w = 20$. Check: $\\\\frac{6}{60} = 10\\\\%$. Choice B, 6, is the amount of salt. Choice D, 60, is the total volume of the new solution, not the amount of water added. Choice A, 4, is 10% of the original 40 liters.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Suv qo‘shilganda tuz miqdori o‘zgarmaydi: $0.15 \\\\times 40 = 6$ litr tuz. Agar $w$ litr suv qo‘shilsa, yangi hajm $40 + w$ bo‘ladi va tuz uning 10% ini tashkil qilishi kerak: $0.10(40 + w) = 6$, demak $40 + w = 60$ va $w = 20$. Tekshiruv: $\\\\frac{6}{60} = 10\\\\%$. B javob (6) — tuz miqdori. D javob (60) — qo‘shilgan suv emas, yangi eritmaning umumiy hajmi. A javob (4) — dastlabki 40 litrning 10% i.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"percentages\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A shop buys a rug from a supplier and sets its selling price 80% higher than the amount the shop paid. During a sale, the shop sells the rug at 25% off the selling price. The shop's profit on the rug is what percent of the amount the shop paid for it?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"35\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let $c$ be the amount the shop paid. The selling price is $1.80c$, and the sale price is $0.75 \\\\times 1.80c = 1.35c$. The profit is $1.35c - c = 0.35c$, which is 35% of $c$. A common error is to subtract the percents, $80 - 25 = 55$; this is wrong because the 25% discount is taken of the larger selling price, not of $c$. Enter 35.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Do‘kon to‘lagan summani $c$ deb olamiz. Sotuv narxi $1.80c$, chegirmadagi narx esa $0.75 \\\\times 1.80c = 1.35c$. Foyda $1.35c - c = 0.35c$, ya’ni $c$ ning 35% i. Ko‘p uchraydigan xato — foizlarni ayirish: $80 - 25 = 55$. Bu noto‘g‘ri, chunki 25% chegirma $c$ dan emas, kattaroq sotuv narxidan olinadi. Javob maydoniga 35 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A bag contains 20 tiles numbered 1 through 20, with one number on each tile. If one tile is selected at random from the bag, what is the probability that the number on the tile is a multiple of 3?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{1}{3}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{3}{10}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{3}{20}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{7}{10}$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The multiples of 3 from 1 to 20 are 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, and 18, which is 6 numbers. The probability is $\\\\frac{6}{20} = \\\\frac{3}{10}$. Choice A assumes exactly one-third of the numbers are multiples of 3, but 20 is not a multiple of 3. Choice C uses 3 favorable outcomes instead of counting all 6. Choice D is the probability that the number is **not** a multiple of 3.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"1 dan 20 gacha bo‘lgan 3 ga karrali sonlar: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15 va 18 — jami 6 ta. Ehtimollik $\\\\frac{6}{20} = \\\\frac{3}{10}$. A javob sonlarning aynan uchdan biri 3 ga karrali deb hisoblagan, lekin 20 soni 3 ga karrali emas. C javob 6 ta qulay natijani sanash o‘rniga 3 ni olgan. D javob — son 3 ga karrali **bo‘lmaslik** ehtimolligi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A shipment contains 40 melons. Of these melons, 34 are ripe and the rest are not ripe. If one melon is selected at random from the shipment, what is the probability that the melon is **not** ripe?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3/20\",\".15\",\"0.15\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The number of melons that are not ripe is $40 - 34 = 6$. The probability is $\\\\frac{6}{40} = \\\\frac{3}{20} = 0.15$. Entering 34/40 (or 0.85) gives the probability that the melon **is** ripe. Enter 3/20, .15, or 0.15.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Pishmagan qovunlar soni $40 - 34 = 6$. Ehtimollik $\\\\frac{6}{40} = \\\\frac{3}{20} = 0.15$. 34/40 (yoki 0.85) deb yozish qovunning pishgan **bo‘lish** ehtimolligini beradi. Javob maydoniga 3/20, .15 yoki 0.15 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"If one of these guests is selected at random, what is the probability that the guest was **not** satisfied?\",\"passage\":\"A hotel asked 160 guests whether they were satisfied with their stay. The results, by the main purpose of each guest's trip, are shown in the table.\\n\\n| Purpose of trip | Satisfied | Not satisfied | Total |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| Business | 52 | 18 | 70 |\\n| Leisure | 74 | 16 | 90 |\\n| Total | 126 | 34 | 160 |\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{17}{80}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{9}{80}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{9}{35}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{17}{63}$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"All 160 guests can be selected, and 34 of them were not satisfied, so the probability is $\\\\frac{34}{160} = \\\\frac{17}{80}$. Choice B, $\\\\frac{18}{160}$, counts only the business guests who were not satisfied. Choice C, $\\\\frac{18}{70}$, is the probability for business guests only. Choice D, $\\\\frac{34}{126}$, divides by the number of satisfied guests instead of by all guests.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Barcha 160 nafar mehmon tanlanishi mumkin, ulardan 34 nafari mamnun bo‘lmagan, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{34}{160} = \\\\frac{17}{80}$. B javob ($\\\\frac{18}{160}$) faqat mamnun bo‘lmagan ish safaridagi mehmonlarni sanagan. C javob ($\\\\frac{18}{70}$) — faqat ish safaridagi mehmonlar uchun ehtimollik. D javob ($\\\\frac{34}{126}$) barcha mehmonlar o‘rniga mamnun bo‘lgan mehmonlar soniga bo‘lgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"If one of the seeds that did **not** sprout is selected at random, what is the probability that it was given fertilizer Q?\",\"passage\":\"A biology class planted 340 bean seeds. Each seed was given fertilizer P, fertilizer Q, or no fertilizer. The table shows how many seeds sprouted within two weeks.\\n\\n| Treatment | Sprouted | Did not sprout | Total |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| Fertilizer P | 84 | 36 | 120 |\\n| Fertilizer Q | 99 | 21 | 120 |\\n| No fertilizer | 57 | 43 | 100 |\\n| Total | 240 | 100 | 340 |\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{7}{40}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{21}{100}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{21}{340}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{33}{80}$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The selection is made only from the seeds that did not sprout, so the denominator is $36 + 21 + 43 = 100$. Of these, 21 were given fertilizer Q, so the probability is $\\\\frac{21}{100}$. Choice A, $\\\\frac{21}{120}$, reverses the condition: it is the probability that a seed given fertilizer Q did not sprout. Choice C divides by all 340 seeds. Choice D, $\\\\frac{99}{240}$, is the probability that a seed that **did** sprout was given fertilizer Q.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanlov faqat unib chiqmagan urug‘lar orasidan amalga oshiriladi, shuning uchun maxraj $36 + 21 + 43 = 100$. Ulardan 21 tasiga Q o‘g‘it berilgan, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{21}{100}$. A javob ($\\\\frac{21}{120}$) shartni teskari olgan: bu Q o‘g‘it berilgan urug‘ning unib chiqmaslik ehtimolligi. C javob barcha 340 urug‘ga bo‘lgan. D javob ($\\\\frac{99}{240}$) — unib **chiqqan** urug‘ga Q o‘g‘it berilgan bo‘lish ehtimolligi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A fair coin is flipped once, and a fair 6-sided die with faces numbered 1 through 6 is rolled once. What is the probability that the coin lands heads up **and** the die shows a number greater than 4?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"1/6\",\".1666\",\".1667\",\"0.166\",\"0.167\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The coin and the die do not affect each other, so multiply the probabilities. The probability of heads is $\\\\frac{1}{2}$. The numbers greater than 4 are 5 and 6, so that probability is $\\\\frac{2}{6} = \\\\frac{1}{3}$. The probability of both is $\\\\frac{1}{2} \\\\times \\\\frac{1}{3} = \\\\frac{1}{6}$. You can also list all 12 equally likely outcomes; exactly 2 of them (heads and 5, heads and 6) work, and $\\\\frac{2}{12} = \\\\frac{1}{6}$. Adding the probabilities, $\\\\frac{1}{2} + \\\\frac{1}{3}$, is wrong for \\\"and.\\\" Enter 1/6, .1666, .1667, 0.166, or 0.167.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tanga va o‘yin soqqasi bir-biriga ta’sir qilmaydi, shuning uchun ehtimolliklarni ko‘paytiramiz. Gerb tushish ehtimolligi $\\\\frac{1}{2}$. 4 dan katta sonlar 5 va 6, demak bu ehtimollik $\\\\frac{2}{6} = \\\\frac{1}{3}$. Ikkalasining birga ro‘y berish ehtimolligi $\\\\frac{1}{2} \\\\times \\\\frac{1}{3} = \\\\frac{1}{6}$. Teng ehtimolli barcha 12 natijani ham yozib chiqish mumkin: ulardan aynan 2 tasi (gerb va 5, gerb va 6) mos keladi, $\\\\frac{2}{12} = \\\\frac{1}{6}$. \\\"Va\\\" uchun ehtimolliklarni qo‘shish ($\\\\frac{1}{2} + \\\\frac{1}{3}$) xato. Javob maydoniga 1/6, .1666, .1667, 0.166 yoki 0.167 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A basket contains 5 red apples and 3 green apples. Two apples are taken from the basket at random, one after the other, without putting the first apple back. What is the probability that both apples are red?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{25}{64}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{15}{56}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{5}{8}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{5}{14}$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The probability that the first apple is red is $\\\\frac{5}{8}$. After one red apple is removed, 4 of the remaining 7 apples are red, so the probability that the second is red is $\\\\frac{4}{7}$. The probability that both are red is $\\\\frac{5}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{4}{7} = \\\\frac{20}{56} = \\\\frac{5}{14}$. Choice A, $\\\\frac{5}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{5}{8}$, assumes the first apple is put back. Choice B, $\\\\frac{5}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{3}{7}$, is the probability that the first is red and the second is green. Choice C is the probability for the first apple only.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi olma qizil bo‘lish ehtimolligi $\\\\frac{5}{8}$. Bitta qizil olma olingandan keyin qolgan 7 ta olmadan 4 tasi qizil, demak ikkinchisi qizil bo‘lish ehtimolligi $\\\\frac{4}{7}$. Ikkalasi ham qizil bo‘lish ehtimolligi $\\\\frac{5}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{4}{7} = \\\\frac{20}{56} = \\\\frac{5}{14}$. A javob ($\\\\frac{5}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{5}{8}$) birinchi olma qaytarib qo‘yilgan deb hisoblagan. B javob ($\\\\frac{5}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{3}{7}$) — birinchisi qizil, ikkinchisi yashil bo‘lish ehtimolligi. C javob faqat birinchi olma uchun ehtimollik.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"If one of the students who chose robotics is selected at random, the probability that the student is in grade 11 is $\\\\frac{3}{5}$. What is the value of $x$?\",\"passage\":\"The table shows the numbers of 10th-grade and 11th-grade students at a school who chose each of two clubs. Each student chose exactly one club.\\n\\n| Club | Grade 10 | Grade 11 |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Robotics | 24 | $x$ |\\n| Debate | 30 | 18 |\",\"option_a\":\"$14.4$\",\"option_b\":\"$16$\",\"option_c\":\"$36$\",\"option_d\":\"$60$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The students who chose robotics number $24 + x$, and $x$ of them are in grade 11, so $\\\\frac{x}{24 + x} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$. Cross-multiplying gives $5x = 72 + 3x$, so $2x = 72$ and $x = 36$. Check: $\\\\frac{36}{60} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$. Choice B comes from $\\\\frac{24}{24 + x} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$, which treats $\\\\frac{3}{5}$ as the probability of grade 10. Choice A comes from $\\\\frac{x}{24} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$, using the wrong denominator. Choice D, 60, is the total number of students who chose robotics.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Robototexnikani tanlagan o‘quvchilar soni $24 + x$, ulardan $x$ nafari 11-sinfda, demak $\\\\frac{x}{24 + x} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$. Ko‘paytirib chiqsak, $5x = 72 + 3x$, ya’ni $2x = 72$ va $x = 36$. Tekshiruv: $\\\\frac{36}{60} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$. B javob $\\\\frac{24}{24 + x} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$ tenglamasidan kelib chiqqan — $\\\\frac{3}{5}$ ni 10-sinf ehtimolligi deb olgan. A javob $\\\\frac{x}{24} = \\\\frac{3}{5}$ dan kelib chiqqan — maxraj noto‘g‘ri. D javob (60) — robototexnikani tanlagan o‘quvchilarning umumiy soni.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"probability_conditional\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A clinic tested 500 people for a certain condition. Of these people, 80 have the condition and 420 do not. The test was positive for 72 of the people who have the condition and for 42 of the people who do not have the condition. If one of the people whose test was positive is selected at random, what is the probability that the person has the condition?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12/19\",\".6315\",\".6316\",\"0.631\",\"0.632\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Only the people with a positive test can be selected: $72 + 42 = 114$ people. Of these, 72 have the condition, so the probability is $\\\\frac{72}{114} = \\\\frac{12}{19} \\\\approx 0.6316$. Entering $\\\\frac{72}{80} = 0.9$ reverses the condition: that is the probability that a person who has the condition tests positive. Entering $\\\\frac{72}{500}$ divides by everyone tested. Enter 12/19, .6315, .6316, 0.631, or 0.632.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Faqat testi ijobiy chiqqan odamlar tanlanishi mumkin: $72 + 42 = 114$ kishi. Ulardan 72 nafarida kasallik bor, demak ehtimollik $\\\\frac{72}{114} = \\\\frac{12}{19} \\\\approx 0.6316$. $\\\\frac{72}{80} = 0.9$ deb yozish shartni teskari olish bo‘ladi: bu kasalligi bor odamning testi ijobiy chiqish ehtimolligi. $\\\\frac{72}{500}$ esa barcha tekshirilganlarga bo‘lish. Javob maydoniga 12/19, .6315, .6316, 0.631 yoki 0.632 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A cyclist rides 54 kilometers in 3 hours. At this rate, how many kilometers will the cyclist ride in 5 hours?\",\"option_a\":\"$18$\",\"option_b\":\"$56$\",\"option_c\":\"$270$\",\"option_d\":\"$90$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The cyclist's rate is $\\\\frac{54}{3} = 18$ kilometers per hour. In 5 hours the cyclist rides $18 \\\\times 5 = 90$ kilometers. Choice A is the rate per hour, not the distance in 5 hours. Choice B adds the 2 extra hours to 54 as if they were kilometers. Choice C multiplies the 3-hour distance by 5, which is the distance for 15 hours.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Velosipedchining tezligi $\\\\frac{54}{3} = 18$ km/soat. 5 soatda u $18 \\\\times 5 = 90$ kilometr yuradi. A javob — 5 soatdagi masofa emas, bir soatlik tezlik. B javob qo‘shimcha 2 soatni kilometr deb, 54 ga qo‘shgan. C javob 3 soatlik masofani 5 ga ko‘paytirgan — bu 15 soatlik masofa.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A cook uses 1.5 kilograms of rice to make 6 servings of plov. At this rate, how many kilograms of rice are needed to make 20 servings of plov?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Each serving uses $\\\\frac{1.5}{6} = 0.25$ kilogram of rice, so 20 servings use $20 \\\\times 0.25 = 5$ kilograms. Equivalently, solve the proportion $\\\\frac{1.5}{6} = \\\\frac{x}{20}$: $6x = 30$, so $x = 5$. Setting up the proportion upside down, $\\\\frac{1.5}{6} = \\\\frac{20}{x}$, gives 80, which is not reasonable. Enter 5.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bir porsiyaga $\\\\frac{1.5}{6} = 0.25$ kilogramm guruch ketadi, demak 20 porsiyaga $20 \\\\times 0.25 = 5$ kilogramm kerak. Yoki $\\\\frac{1.5}{6} = \\\\frac{x}{20}$ proporsiyasini yechamiz: $6x = 30$, $x = 5$. Proporsiyani teskari tuzish ($\\\\frac{1.5}{6} = \\\\frac{20}{x}$) 80 ni beradi, bu mantiqsiz. Javob maydoniga 5 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A runner's average speed is 5 meters per second. What is this speed in kilometers per hour? (1 kilometer = 1,000 meters)\",\"option_a\":\"$1.8$\",\"option_b\":\"$18$\",\"option_c\":\"$300$\",\"option_d\":\"$18{,}000$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"In one hour there are $60 \\\\times 60 = 3{,}600$ seconds, so the runner covers $5 \\\\times 3{,}600 = 18{,}000$ meters per hour. Since 1 kilometer is 1,000 meters, this is $\\\\frac{18{,}000}{1{,}000} = 18$ kilometers per hour. Choice D is the speed in meters per hour; it was not converted to kilometers. Choice C multiplies by 60 only once (meters per minute). Choice A divides by 10,000 instead of 1,000.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bir soatda $60 \\\\times 60 = 3{,}600$ sekund bor, demak yuguruvchi bir soatda $5 \\\\times 3{,}600 = 18{,}000$ metr yuguradi. 1 kilometr 1,000 metr bo‘lgani uchun bu $\\\\frac{18{,}000}{1{,}000} = 18$ km/soat. D javob — metr/soatdagi tezlik, kilometrga o‘tkazilmagan. C javob faqat bir marta 60 ga ko‘paytirgan (metr/daqiqa). A javob 1,000 o‘rniga 10,000 ga bo‘lgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"On a map, 1 centimeter represents 2.5 kilometers. The actual distance between two villages is 37 kilometers. What is the distance between the two villages on the map, in centimeters?\",\"option_a\":\"$14.8$\",\"option_b\":\"$34.5$\",\"option_c\":\"$92.5$\",\"option_d\":\"$1.48$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Each centimeter on the map stands for 2.5 kilometers, so the map distance is $\\\\frac{37}{2.5} = 14.8$ centimeters. Check: $14.8 \\\\times 2.5 = 37$. Choice C multiplies 37 by 2.5, which converts in the wrong direction. Choice B subtracts 2.5 from 37. Choice D misplaces the decimal point (it divides by 25).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Xaritadagi har bir santimetr 2.5 kilometrga to‘g‘ri keladi, demak xaritadagi masofa $\\\\frac{37}{2.5} = 14.8$ santimetr. Tekshiruv: $14.8 \\\\times 2.5 = 37$. C javob 37 ni 2.5 ga ko‘paytirgan — teskari yo‘nalishda o‘tkazgan. B javob 37 dan 2.5 ni ayirgan. D javobda vergul noto‘g‘ri qo‘yilgan (25 ga bo‘lingan).\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A block of a certain metal has a mass of 540 grams and a volume of 200 cubic centimeters. A larger block of the same metal has a volume of 1,500 cubic centimeters. What is the mass of the larger block, in **kilograms**? (1 kilogram = 1,000 grams)\",\"spr_answers\":[\"4.05\",\"81/20\"],\"explanation_en\":\"The density of the metal is $\\\\frac{540}{200} = 2.7$ grams per cubic centimeter. The larger block has mass $2.7 \\\\times 1{,}500 = 4{,}050$ grams, which is $\\\\frac{4{,}050}{1{,}000} = 4.05$ kilograms. Entering 4050 gives the mass in grams, not kilograms. Enter 4.05 or 81/20.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Metallning zichligi $\\\\frac{540}{200} = 2.7$ g/sm³. Katta blokning massasi $2.7 \\\\times 1{,}500 = 4{,}050$ gramm, ya’ni $\\\\frac{4{,}050}{1{,}000} = 4.05$ kilogramm. 4050 deb yozish massani kilogrammda emas, grammda berish bo‘ladi. Javob maydoniga 4.05 yoki 81/20 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A builder mixes cement, sand, and gravel in the ratio $1 : 2 : 4$ by mass to make concrete. How many kilograms of sand are needed to make 350 kilograms of this concrete?\",\"option_a\":\"$50$\",\"option_b\":\"$175$\",\"option_c\":\"$100$\",\"option_d\":\"$200$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The ratio has $1 + 2 + 4 = 7$ parts in total, so each part is $\\\\frac{350}{7} = 50$ kilograms. Sand is 2 parts: $2 \\\\times 50 = 100$ kilograms. Choice A is the mass of cement (1 part). Choice D is the mass of gravel (4 parts). Choice B treats sand as half of the mixture, using the ratio $2 : 4$ and ignoring the cement.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Nisbatda jami $1 + 2 + 4 = 7$ ulush bor, demak bir ulush $\\\\frac{350}{7} = 50$ kilogramm. Qum 2 ulush: $2 \\\\times 50 = 100$ kilogramm. A javob — sement massasi (1 ulush). D javob — shag‘al massasi (4 ulush). B javob sementni hisobga olmay, $2 : 4$ nisbatdan qumni aralashmaning yarmi deb olgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A farmer will spread fertilizer on a rectangular field that is 120 meters long and 0.25 kilometer wide. The fertilizer is applied at a rate of 25 grams per square meter. How many **kilograms** of fertilizer are needed for the entire field? (1 kilometer = 1,000 meters; 1 kilogram = 1,000 grams)\",\"option_a\":\"$0.75$\",\"option_b\":\"$75$\",\"option_c\":\"$750$\",\"option_d\":\"$7{,}500$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"First express both sides in meters: 0.25 kilometer is 250 meters, so the area is $120 \\\\times 250 = 30{,}000$ square meters. The fertilizer needed is $25 \\\\times 30{,}000 = 750{,}000$ grams, which is $\\\\frac{750{,}000}{1{,}000} = 750$ kilograms. Choice A multiplies 120 by 0.25 without converting kilometers to meters. Choice D divides by 100 instead of 1,000 when converting grams to kilograms, and choice B divides by 10,000.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Avval ikkala tomonni metrda ifodalaymiz: 0.25 kilometr 250 metr, demak yuza $120 \\\\times 250 = 30{,}000$ kvadrat metr. Kerakli o‘g‘it $25 \\\\times 30{,}000 = 750{,}000$ gramm, ya’ni $\\\\frac{750{,}000}{1{,}000} = 750$ kilogramm. A javob kilometrni metrga o‘tkazmasdan, 120 ni 0.25 ga ko‘paytirgan. D javob grammni kilogrammga o‘tkazishda 1,000 o‘rniga 100 ga, B javob esa 10,000 ga bo‘lgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"ratios_rates_proportions_units\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Pipe A alone can fill an empty water tank in 6 hours. Pipe B alone can fill the same empty tank in 9 hours. If both pipes work together at these rates, how many hours will it take to fill the empty tank?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"3.6\",\"18/5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Pipe A fills $\\\\frac{1}{6}$ of the tank per hour and pipe B fills $\\\\frac{1}{9}$ of the tank per hour. Together they fill $\\\\frac{1}{6} + \\\\frac{1}{9} = \\\\frac{3}{18} + \\\\frac{2}{18} = \\\\frac{5}{18}$ of the tank per hour, so the time needed is $\\\\frac{18}{5} = 3.6$ hours. Averaging the two times, $\\\\frac{6 + 9}{2} = 7.5$, is wrong, because working together must be faster than either pipe alone. Adding the times (15) is also wrong. Enter 3.6 or 18/5.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"A quvur bir soatda bakning $\\\\frac{1}{6}$ qismini, B quvur esa $\\\\frac{1}{9}$ qismini to‘ldiradi. Birgalikda ular bir soatda $\\\\frac{1}{6} + \\\\frac{1}{9} = \\\\frac{3}{18} + \\\\frac{2}{18} = \\\\frac{5}{18}$ qismini to‘ldiradi, demak kerakli vaqt $\\\\frac{18}{5} = 3.6$ soat. Ikki vaqtning o‘rtachasini olish ($\\\\frac{6 + 9}{2} = 7.5$) noto‘g‘ri, chunki birga ishlaganda har bir quvurning yolg‘iz ishlashidan tezroq bo‘lishi kerak. Vaqtlarni qo‘shish (15) ham xato. Javob maydoniga 3.6 yoki 18/5 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- The axolotl is a salamander native to lakes near Mexico City.\\n- Unlike most salamanders, it keeps its feathery external gills throughout its adult life.\\n- Axolotls can regrow lost limbs, as well as parts of the heart and spinal cord.\\n- Scientists study axolotls to learn how tissue regeneration works.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to emphasize the axolotl's ability to regrow body parts. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"The axolotl is a salamander that is native to lakes near Mexico City.\",\"option_b\":\"Unlike most salamanders, the axolotl keeps its feathery external gills as an adult.\",\"option_c\":\"The axolotl can regrow not only lost limbs but also parts of its heart and spinal cord.\",\"option_d\":\"Scientists study the axolotl, a salamander native to lakes near Mexico City.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to emphasize the axolotl's ability to regrow body parts. Choice C does this directly, and the phrase “not only … but also” stresses how many different body parts the animal can regrow.\\n\\nChoice A gives the axolotl's habitat, not its ability to regrow body parts. Choice B describes its gills, a different feature. Choice D says that scientists study the axolotl but never mentions regeneration.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — aksolotlning tana a’zolarini qayta o‘stira olish qobiliyatini ta’kidlash. C buni to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri qiladi, “not only … but also” iborasi esa hayvon qanchalik ko‘p turli a’zolarni qayta o‘stira olishini alohida ta’kidlaydi.\\n\\nA — a’zolarni qayta o‘stirish haqida emas, aksolotlning yashash joyi haqida. B — uning jabralarini, ya’ni boshqa xususiyatini tasvirlaydi. D — olimlar aksolotlni o‘rganishini aytadi, lekin qayta tiklanishni umuman tilga olmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- The saxaul is a small tree that grows in the deserts of Central Asia, including the Kyzylkum.\\n- Its roots can reach groundwater more than 10 meters below the surface.\\n- Groves of saxaul help hold sand in place and reduce dust storms.\\n- Uzbekistan has planted saxaul across large areas of the dried bed of the Aral Sea.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to explain why saxaul is planted on the dried bed of the Aral Sea. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Because groves of saxaul help hold sand in place and reduce dust storms, Uzbekistan has planted the tree across large areas of the dried Aral Sea bed.\",\"option_b\":\"The saxaul, a small tree, grows in the deserts of Central Asia, such as the Kyzylkum.\",\"option_c\":\"The roots of the saxaul can reach groundwater more than 10 meters below the surface.\",\"option_d\":\"Uzbekistan has planted saxaul across large areas of the dried bed of the Aral Sea.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to explain why saxaul is planted on the dried Aral Sea bed. Choice A gives the reason, using “Because” to connect the tree's ability to hold sand and reduce dust storms with the planting.\\n\\nChoice B tells where saxaul grows naturally but not why it is planted on the seabed. Choice C describes the tree's roots without linking them to the planting. Choice D states that the tree has been planted there but gives no reason.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — saksovul nima uchun Orol dengizining qurigan tubiga ekilishini tushuntirish. A sababni beradi: “Because” so‘zi daraxtning qumni ushlab turishi va chang bo‘ronlarini kamaytirishini ekish bilan bog‘laydi.\\n\\nB — saksovul tabiiy holda qayerda o‘sishini aytadi, lekin nima uchun dengiz tubiga ekilishini emas. C — daraxt ildizlarini tasvirlaydi, ammo ularni ekish bilan bog‘lamaydi. D — daraxt u yerga ekilganini aytadi, lekin hech qanday sabab keltirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Venus is the second planet from the Sun.\\n- Venus takes about 243 Earth days to rotate once on its axis.\\n- Venus takes about 225 Earth days to complete one orbit around the Sun.\\n- Venus rotates in the opposite direction from most other planets in the solar system.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to emphasize that Venus takes longer to rotate once on its axis than to orbit the Sun once. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Venus, the second planet from the Sun, rotates in the opposite direction from most other planets.\",\"option_b\":\"Venus takes about 225 Earth days to complete one orbit around the Sun.\",\"option_c\":\"Venus is the second planet from the Sun, and it takes about 243 Earth days to rotate once.\",\"option_d\":\"Venus takes about 243 Earth days to rotate once on its axis, which is longer than the roughly 225 Earth days it takes to orbit the Sun.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to emphasize that one rotation of Venus takes longer than one orbit. Choice D gives both figures, 243 and 225 Earth days, and states directly that the rotation time is “longer.”\\n\\nChoice A is about the direction of rotation, not its length. Choice B gives only the orbit time, so no comparison is made. Choice C gives only the rotation time and adds the planet's position, so it also makes no comparison.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — Veneraning o‘z o‘qi atrofida bir marta aylanishi Quyosh atrofida bir marta aylanishidan uzoqroq davom etishini ta’kidlash. D ikkala raqamni — 243 va 225 Yer kunini — beradi va o‘z o‘qi atrofida aylanish vaqti “longer” (uzoqroq) ekanini to‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri aytadi.\\n\\nA — aylanish davomiyligi haqida emas, yo‘nalishi haqida. B — faqat orbita vaqtini beradi, shuning uchun taqqoslash yo‘q. C — faqat o‘z o‘qi atrofida aylanish vaqtini va sayyoraning o‘rnini aytadi, bu ham taqqoslash emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Great tits are small songbirds found in both European cities and forests.\\n- Biologist Elif Demir recorded the songs of great tits in 10 cities and 10 nearby forests.\\n- The city birds sang at higher pitches than the forest birds did.\\n- Traffic noise is mostly low-pitched.\\n- Demir concluded that high-pitched songs are easier to hear over traffic noise.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to explain the reason Demir gave for the difference between the songs of city and forest great tits. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Demir recorded the songs of great tits living in 10 cities and in 10 nearby forests.\",\"option_b\":\"According to Demir, city great tits sing at higher pitches than forest great tits do because high-pitched songs are easier to hear over low-pitched traffic noise.\",\"option_c\":\"Great tits living in cities sang at higher pitches than great tits living in forests did.\",\"option_d\":\"Great tits are small songbirds found in European cities, where traffic noise is mostly low-pitched.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to explain the reason Demir gave for the difference in songs. Choice B names the difference (city birds sing at higher pitches) and gives Demir's explanation (high-pitched songs are easier to hear over low-pitched traffic noise).\\n\\nChoice A describes how Demir collected her data, not her explanation. Choice C states the difference but gives no reason for it. Choice D mentions traffic noise but never mentions the difference in songs or Demir's conclusion.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — shahar va o‘rmondagi katta chittaklar (great tit) sayrashidagi farq uchun Demir keltirgan sababni tushuntirish. B farqni (shahar qushlari balandroq ohangda sayraydi) ham, Demirning izohini ham (baland ohangli sayrash past ohangli transport shovqini ustidan yaxshiroq eshitiladi) beradi.\\n\\nA — Demir ma’lumotlarni qanday yig‘ganini tasvirlaydi, uning izohini emas. C — farqni aytadi, ammo sababini bermaydi. D — transport shovqinini tilga oladi, lekin sayrashdagi farq ham, Demirning xulosasi ham aytilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- The dutar is a long-necked lute played in Uzbekistan and neighboring countries.\\n- It has two strings.\\n- The rubab is a short-necked lute that is also played in Central Asia.\\n- It usually has more strings than the dutar, and its body is often covered with animal skin.\\n- Both instruments are often played to accompany singers.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to emphasize a similarity between the dutar and the rubab. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"The dutar has only two strings, while the rubab usually has more.\",\"option_b\":\"The dutar has a long neck, but the rubab has a short one.\",\"option_c\":\"The rubab, a short-necked lute, often has a body covered with animal skin.\",\"option_d\":\"The dutar and the rubab are both Central Asian lutes that are often played to accompany singers.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to emphasize a similarity. Choice D uses “both” to point out what the instruments share: each is a Central Asian lute often played to accompany singers.\\n\\nChoices A and B each point out a difference (number of strings; length of neck), which is the opposite of the goal. Choice C describes only the rubab, so it cannot show a similarity between the two instruments.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — o‘xshashlikni ta’kidlash. D “both” (ikkalasi ham) so‘zi orqali cholg‘ularning umumiy jihatini ko‘rsatadi: ikkalasi ham Markaziy Osiyo cholg‘usi bo‘lib, ko‘pincha xonandalarga jo‘r bo‘lish uchun chalinadi.\\n\\nA va B farqni ko‘rsatadi (torlar soni; dastaning uzunligi) — bu maqsadga teskari. C faqat rubob haqida, shuning uchun ikki cholg‘u o‘rtasidagi o‘xshashlikni ko‘rsata olmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- A windcatcher is a tall tower built on top of a house in hot, dry regions such as central Iran.\\n- Openings near the top of the tower face the wind.\\n- Wind entering the openings is pushed down the tower into the rooms below.\\n- As this moving air enters, warm indoor air is forced out through windows and doors.\\n- Some windcatchers are more than 30 meters tall.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to explain how a windcatcher cools a house. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Wind entering openings near the top of a windcatcher is pushed down into the rooms below, forcing warm indoor air out through windows and doors.\",\"option_b\":\"A windcatcher is a tall tower built on top of a house in a hot, dry region such as central Iran.\",\"option_c\":\"Some windcatchers, which are built in hot, dry regions, are more than 30 meters tall.\",\"option_d\":\"The openings near the top of a windcatcher face the wind.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to explain how a windcatcher cools a house, which requires describing the process. Choice A traces the whole process: wind enters at the top, is pushed down into the rooms, and forces warm air out.\\n\\nChoice B defines what a windcatcher is and where it is found but not how it works. Choice C gives the height of some windcatchers, which does not explain cooling. Choice D describes only the first part of the process and never says how the house is cooled.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — shamol ushlagich (badgir) uyni qanday sovitishini tushuntirish, buning uchun jarayonni tasvirlash kerak. A butun jarayonni ko‘rsatadi: shamol tepadan kiradi, xonalarga pastga yo‘naltiriladi va issiq havoni tashqariga chiqarib yuboradi.\\n\\nB — shamol ushlagich nima ekanini va qayerda uchrashini aytadi, lekin qanday ishlashini emas. C — ba’zi shamol ushlagichlarning balandligini beradi, bu sovitishni tushuntirmaydi. D — jarayonning faqat birinchi qismini tasvirlaydi va uy qanday sovishini aytmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- Desert ants of the genus Cataglyphis search for food far from their nests in the Sahara.\\n- Researchers once assumed that these ants found their way home mainly by following scent trails.\\n- However, scent trails evaporate quickly on hot sand.\\n- In experiments, ants whose legs had been lengthened with tiny stilts walked past their nest, while ants with shortened legs stopped before reaching it.\\n- These results suggest that the ants measure distance by counting their steps.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to contrast the earlier assumption about how Cataglyphis ants find their way home with what the experiments suggest. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"Because scent trails evaporate quickly on hot sand, Cataglyphis ants search for food far from their nests.\",\"option_b\":\"Although researchers once assumed that Cataglyphis ants found their way home by following scent trails, experiments suggest that the ants instead measure distance by counting their steps.\",\"option_c\":\"In experiments, Cataglyphis ants with lengthened legs walked past their nest, while those with shortened legs stopped before reaching it.\",\"option_d\":\"Cataglyphis ants search for food far from their nests in the Sahara and find their way home by counting their steps.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal requires two parts: the earlier assumption and what the experiments suggest, set against each other. Choice B presents both, using “Although” and “instead” to make the contrast clear.\\n\\nChoice A creates a cause-and-effect link that the notes do not support and mentions neither the assumption nor the experiments' conclusion. Choice C reports the experimental results but leaves out the earlier assumption, so there is no contrast. Choice D gives the newer explanation but omits the earlier assumption, so it also makes no contrast.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad ikki qismni talab qiladi: avvalgi taxmin va tajribalar ko‘rsatgan natija, bir-biriga qarama-qarshi qo‘yilgan holda. B ikkalasini ham beradi, “Although” va “instead” so‘zlari esa qarama-qarshilikni aniq ko‘rsatadi.\\n\\nA — eslatmalarda tasdiqlanmagan sabab-oqibat bog‘lanishini yaratadi va na taxminni, na tajribalar xulosasini aytadi. C — tajriba natijalarini beradi, ammo avvalgi taxminni tushirib qoldiradi, shuning uchun qarama-qarshilik yo‘q. D — yangi izohni beradi, lekin avvalgi taxmin yo‘q, demak bu ham qarama-qarshilik emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"rhetorical_synthesis\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\\n\\n- The Svalbard Global Seed Vault is located on a Norwegian island about 1,300 kilometers from the North Pole.\\n- It stores backup copies of seeds from gene banks around the world.\\n- The vault can hold up to 4.5 million seed samples.\\n- It is built deep inside a mountain, where the surrounding permafrost helps keep the seeds frozen even if the power fails.\\n- In 2015, researchers withdrew seeds from the vault to replace collections lost during the war in Syria.\",\"stem\":\"The student wants to explain how the vault's design helps protect the seeds it stores. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\",\"option_a\":\"The Svalbard Global Seed Vault, which can hold up to 4.5 million seed samples, stores backup copies of seeds from gene banks around the world.\",\"option_b\":\"Located on a Norwegian island about 1,300 kilometers from the North Pole, the Svalbard Global Seed Vault stores backup copies of seeds from around the world.\",\"option_c\":\"Because the Svalbard Global Seed Vault is built deep inside a mountain, the surrounding permafrost helps keep its seeds frozen even if the power fails.\",\"option_d\":\"In 2015, researchers withdrew seeds from the Svalbard Global Seed Vault to replace collections lost during the war in Syria.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The goal is to explain how the vault's design protects the seeds. Choice C describes a design feature (being built deep inside a mountain) and explains its protective effect (permafrost keeps the seeds frozen even during a power failure).\\n\\nChoice A gives the vault's capacity and purpose but not how it protects the seeds. Choice B gives the vault's location, which is tempting, but it never explains how that location or the building's design protects anything. Choice D describes one use of the stored seeds, not how they are protected.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Maqsad — omborning tuzilishi (dizayni) undagi urug‘larni qanday himoya qilishini tushuntirish. C dizayn xususiyatini (tog‘ ichida chuqur qurilgani) va uning himoya ta’sirini (abadiy muzloq urug‘larni hatto elektr o‘chganda ham muzlagan holda saqlaydi) tushuntiradi.\\n\\nA — omborning sig‘imi va vazifasini beradi, lekin urug‘lar qanday himoyalanishini emas. B — omborning joylashuvini aytadi, bu jozibali tuyuladi, ammo bu joylashuv yoki bino tuzilishi qanday himoya qilishini tushuntirmaydi. D — saqlangan urug‘lardan bir marta foydalanilganini tasvirlaydi, ular qanday himoyalanishini emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In right triangle $DEF$, angle $E$ is the right angle, $DE = 20$, $EF = 21$, and $DF = 29$. What is the value of $\\\\cos F$?\",\"option_a\":\"$\\\\frac{20}{29}$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{20}{21}$\",\"option_c\":\"$\\\\frac{21}{29}$\",\"option_d\":\"$\\\\frac{21}{20}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The hypotenuse is $\\\\overline{DF}$, opposite the right angle $E$. The leg adjacent to angle $F$ is $\\\\overline{EF}$. So $\\\\cos F = \\\\frac{\\\\text{adjacent}}{\\\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\\\frac{EF}{DF} = \\\\frac{21}{29}$. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($\\\\frac{20}{29}$) is $\\\\sin F$, which uses the opposite leg. Choice B ($\\\\frac{20}{21}$) is $\\\\tan F$. Choice D ($\\\\frac{21}{20}$) is $\\\\tan D$, the reciprocal of $\\\\tan F$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gipotenuza — to‘g‘ri burchak $E$ qarshisidagi $\\\\overline{DF}$. $F$ burchakka yopishgan katet $\\\\overline{EF}$. Demak $\\\\cos F = \\\\frac{\\\\text{yopishgan katet}}{\\\\text{gipotenuza}} = \\\\frac{EF}{DF} = \\\\frac{21}{29}$. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($\\\\frac{20}{29}$) — bu $\\\\sin F$, qarshidagi katet olingan. B ($\\\\frac{20}{21}$) — bu $\\\\tan F$. D ($\\\\frac{21}{20}$) — bu $\\\\tan D$, ya’ni $\\\\tan F$ ning teskarisi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A right triangle has a hypotenuse of length 26 and one leg of length 10. What is the length of the other leg?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"24\"],\"explanation_en\":\"By the Pythagorean theorem, $10^2 + b^2 = 26^2$, so $b^2 = 676 - 100 = 576$ and $b = 24$.\\n\\nIf you got about 27.86 (that is, $\\\\sqrt{776}$), you added the squares as if 26 were a leg instead of the hypotenuse. If you got 16, you subtracted the lengths without squaring.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Pifagor teoremasiga ko‘ra $10^2 + b^2 = 26^2$, demak $b^2 = 676 - 100 = 576$ va $b = 24$.\\n\\nAgar taxminan 27.86 (ya’ni $\\\\sqrt{776}$) chiqqan bo‘lsa, 26 gipotenuza emas, katet deb olinib kvadratlar qo‘shilgan. Agar 16 chiqqan bo‘lsa, uzunliklar kvadratga ko‘tarilmasdan ayirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"An isosceles right triangle has two legs that are each 7 centimeters long. What is the length, in centimeters, of the hypotenuse?\",\"option_a\":\"$7\\\\sqrt{2}$\",\"option_b\":\"$7\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$14$\",\"option_d\":\"$49$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"In a $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangle the hypotenuse is $\\\\sqrt{2}$ times a leg, so it is $7\\\\sqrt{2}$. Using the Pythagorean theorem: $\\\\sqrt{7^2 + 7^2} = \\\\sqrt{98} = 7\\\\sqrt{2}$. Choice A is correct.\\n\\nChoice B ($7\\\\sqrt{3}$) uses the $30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ ratio. Choice C ($14$) adds the legs. Choice D ($49$) is $7^2$, the square of one leg.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ uchburchakda gipotenuza katetdan $\\\\sqrt{2}$ marta uzun, ya’ni $7\\\\sqrt{2}$. Pifagor teoremasi bilan: $\\\\sqrt{7^2 + 7^2} = \\\\sqrt{98} = 7\\\\sqrt{2}$. To‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB ($7\\\\sqrt{3}$) — $30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ nisbati ishlatilgan. C ($14$) — katetlar qo‘shilgan. D ($49$) — bitta katetning kvadrati, $7^2$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"An equilateral triangle has sides of length 10. What is the height of the triangle (the length of the perpendicular segment from one vertex to the opposite side)?\",\"option_a\":\"$5$\",\"option_b\":\"$5\\\\sqrt{2}$\",\"option_c\":\"$5\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"option_d\":\"$10\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The height splits the equilateral triangle into two $30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ triangles, each with hypotenuse 10 and shorter leg $\\\\frac{10}{2} = 5$. The height is the longer leg: $5\\\\sqrt{3}$. Check: $\\\\sqrt{10^2 - 5^2} = \\\\sqrt{75} = 5\\\\sqrt{3}$. Choice C is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($5$) is the shorter leg, half the base. Choice B ($5\\\\sqrt{2}$) uses the $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ ratio. Choice D ($10\\\\sqrt{3}$) multiplies the full side, instead of half of it, by $\\\\sqrt{3}$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Balandlik teng tomonli uchburchakni ikkita $30^\\\\circ$-$60^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ uchburchakka bo‘ladi; har birining gipotenuzasi 10, qisqa kateti $\\\\frac{10}{2} = 5$. Balandlik uzun katet: $5\\\\sqrt{3}$. Tekshiruv: $\\\\sqrt{10^2 - 5^2} = \\\\sqrt{75} = 5\\\\sqrt{3}$. To‘g‘ri javob C.\\n\\nA ($5$) — qisqa katet, asosning yarmi. B ($5\\\\sqrt{2}$) — $45^\\\\circ$-$45^\\\\circ$-$90^\\\\circ$ nisbati ishlatilgan. D ($10\\\\sqrt{3}$) — tomonning yarmi emas, butuni $\\\\sqrt{3}$ ga ko‘paytirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In right triangle $RST$, angle $T$ is the right angle and $\\\\sin R = \\\\frac{5}{13}$. What is the value of $\\\\tan S$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12/5\",\"2.4\"],\"explanation_en\":\"$\\\\sin R = \\\\frac{\\\\text{opposite}}{\\\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\\\frac{ST}{RS} = \\\\frac{5}{13}$, so we can take $ST = 5$ and $RS = 13$. By the Pythagorean theorem, $RT = \\\\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = 12$. For angle $S$, the opposite leg is $RT$ and the adjacent leg is $ST$, so $\\\\tan S = \\\\frac{RT}{ST} = \\\\frac{12}{5}$. Enter 12/5 or 2.4.\\n\\nIf you got $\\\\frac{5}{12}$, you found $\\\\tan R$ instead of $\\\\tan S$. If you got $\\\\frac{12}{13}$, you found $\\\\cos R$ (which equals $\\\\sin S$).\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$\\\\sin R = \\\\frac{\\\\text{qarshidagi katet}}{\\\\text{gipotenuza}} = \\\\frac{ST}{RS} = \\\\frac{5}{13}$, demak $ST = 5$ va $RS = 13$ deb olish mumkin. Pifagor teoremasiga ko‘ra $RT = \\\\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = 12$. $S$ burchak uchun qarshidagi katet $RT$, yopishgan katet $ST$, shuning uchun $\\\\tan S = \\\\frac{RT}{ST} = \\\\frac{12}{5}$. 12/5 yoki 2.4 kiriting.\\n\\nAgar $\\\\frac{5}{12}$ chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz $\\\\tan S$ o‘rniga $\\\\tan R$ ni topgansiz. Agar $\\\\frac{12}{13}$ chiqqan bo‘lsa, bu $\\\\cos R$ (u $\\\\sin S$ ga teng).\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A surveyor stands on level ground 40 meters from the base of a vertical tower. The angle of elevation from the ground at the surveyor’s position to the top of the tower is $30^\\\\circ$. What is the height, in meters, of the tower?\",\"option_a\":\"$20$\",\"option_b\":\"$\\\\frac{40\\\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\",\"option_c\":\"$20\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"option_d\":\"$40\\\\sqrt{3}$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The tower, the ground, and the line of sight form a right triangle. The 40-meter distance is the leg adjacent to the $30^\\\\circ$ angle, and the height $h$ is the opposite leg. So $\\\\tan 30^\\\\circ = \\\\frac{h}{40}$, and $h = 40 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{3}} = \\\\frac{40\\\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ meters (about 23.1 meters). Choice B is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($20$) is $40 \\\\sin 30^\\\\circ$, which treats 40 as the hypotenuse. Choice C ($20\\\\sqrt{3}$) is $40 \\\\cos 30^\\\\circ$, also treating 40 as the hypotenuse. Choice D ($40\\\\sqrt{3}$) is $40 \\\\tan 60^\\\\circ$, using the wrong angle.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Minora, yer va ko‘rish chizig‘i to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchak hosil qiladi. 40 metrlik masofa $30^\\\\circ$ burchakka yopishgan katet, balandlik $h$ esa qarshidagi katet. Demak $\\\\tan 30^\\\\circ = \\\\frac{h}{40}$ va $h = 40 \\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{3}} = \\\\frac{40\\\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ metr (taxminan 23.1 metr). To‘g‘ri javob B.\\n\\nA ($20$) — bu $40 \\\\sin 30^\\\\circ$, 40 gipotenuza deb olingan. C ($20\\\\sqrt{3}$) — bu $40 \\\\cos 30^\\\\circ$, bunda ham 40 gipotenuza deb olingan. D ($40\\\\sqrt{3}$) — bu $40 \\\\tan 60^\\\\circ$, noto‘g‘ri burchak olingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"In right triangle $ABC$, angle $C$ is the right angle. The altitude from $C$ meets hypotenuse $\\\\overline{AB}$ at point $D$, with $AD = 4$ and $DB = 9$. What is the length of $\\\\overline{BC}$?\",\"option_a\":\"$6$\",\"option_b\":\"$2\\\\sqrt{13}$\",\"option_c\":\"$9$\",\"option_d\":\"$3\\\\sqrt{13}$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The altitude to the hypotenuse creates triangles similar to the original triangle. Triangle $CBD$ is similar to triangle $ABC$ (they share angle $B$ and each has a right angle), so $\\\\frac{BC}{AB} = \\\\frac{DB}{BC}$, which gives $BC^2 = DB \\\\cdot AB = 9 \\\\cdot 13 = 117$. So $BC = \\\\sqrt{117} = 3\\\\sqrt{13}$. Check: $CD = \\\\sqrt{4 \\\\cdot 9} = 6$, and $CD^2 + DB^2 = 36 + 81 = 117$. Choice D is correct.\\n\\nChoice A ($6$) is the altitude $CD$. Choice B ($2\\\\sqrt{13}$) is $AC$, the other leg, from $AC^2 = AD \\\\cdot AB = 52$. Choice C ($9$) is $DB$, which is only part of the hypotenuse, not a side of triangle $ABC$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gipotenuzaga tushirilgan balandlik dastlabki uchburchakka o‘xshash uchburchaklar hosil qiladi. $CBD$ uchburchak $ABC$ uchburchakka o‘xshash ($B$ burchak umumiy va ikkalasida to‘g‘ri burchak bor), demak $\\\\frac{BC}{AB} = \\\\frac{DB}{BC}$, ya’ni $BC^2 = DB \\\\cdot AB = 9 \\\\cdot 13 = 117$. Shuning uchun $BC = \\\\sqrt{117} = 3\\\\sqrt{13}$. Tekshiruv: $CD = \\\\sqrt{4 \\\\cdot 9} = 6$ va $CD^2 + DB^2 = 36 + 81 = 117$. To‘g‘ri javob D.\\n\\nA ($6$) — bu $CD$ balandlik. B ($2\\\\sqrt{13}$) — bu boshqa katet $AC$, $AC^2 = AD \\\\cdot AB = 52$ dan. C ($9$) — bu $DB$, gipotenuzaning faqat bir qismi, $ABC$ uchburchakning tomoni emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"right_triangles_trigonometry\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In triangle $ABC$, $AB = AC = 17$ and $BC = 16$. What is the value of $\\\\tan B$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"15/8\",\"1.875\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Draw the altitude from $A$ to $\\\\overline{BC}$, meeting it at $M$. Because the triangle is isosceles with $AB = AC$, this altitude bisects $\\\\overline{BC}$, so $BM = 8$. In right triangle $ABM$, $AM = \\\\sqrt{17^2 - 8^2} = \\\\sqrt{225} = 15$. Then $\\\\tan B = \\\\frac{\\\\text{opposite}}{\\\\text{adjacent}} = \\\\frac{AM}{BM} = \\\\frac{15}{8}$. Enter 15/8 or 1.875.\\n\\nIf you got $\\\\frac{8}{15}$, you inverted the ratio (that is $\\\\tan \\\\angle BAM$). If you got $\\\\frac{15}{16}$, you used all of $\\\\overline{BC}$ as the adjacent side even though the right angle is at $M$, the midpoint. If you got $\\\\frac{8}{17}$, you found $\\\\cos B$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$A$ dan $\\\\overline{BC}$ ga balandlik tushiramiz, u $\\\\overline{BC}$ ni $M$ nuqtada kesadi. Uchburchak teng yonli ($AB = AC$) bo‘lgani uchun bu balandlik $\\\\overline{BC}$ ni teng ikkiga bo‘ladi, ya’ni $BM = 8$. $ABM$ to‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchakda $AM = \\\\sqrt{17^2 - 8^2} = \\\\sqrt{225} = 15$. U holda $\\\\tan B = \\\\frac{\\\\text{qarshidagi katet}}{\\\\text{yopishgan katet}} = \\\\frac{AM}{BM} = \\\\frac{15}{8}$. 15/8 yoki 1.875 kiriting.\\n\\nAgar $\\\\frac{8}{15}$ chiqqan bo‘lsa, nisbat teskari olingan (bu $\\\\tan \\\\angle BAM$). Agar $\\\\frac{15}{16}$ chiqqan bo‘lsa, to‘g‘ri burchak o‘rtadagi $M$ nuqtada bo‘lsa ham yopishgan katet sifatida butun $\\\\overline{BC}$ olingan. Agar $\\\\frac{8}{17}$ chiqqan bo‘lsa, siz $\\\\cos B$ ni topgansiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} x &= 3y \\\\\\\\ 2x + y &= 35 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nWhat is the solution $(x, y)$ to the given system of equations?\",\"option_a\":\"$(5, 15)$\",\"option_b\":\"$(7, 21)$\",\"option_c\":\"$(10, 15)$\",\"option_d\":\"$(15, 5)$\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"Substitute $x = 3y$ into the second equation: $2(3y) + y = 35$, so $7y = 35$ and $y = 5$. Then $x = 3(5) = 15$. The solution is $(15, 5)$.\\n\\nChoice A swaps $x$ and $y$. Choices B and C satisfy $2x + y = 35$ but not $x = 3y$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x = 3y$ ni ikkinchi tenglamaga qo‘yamiz: $2(3y) + y = 35$, ya’ni $7y = 35$ va $y = 5$. U holda $x = 3(5) = 15$. Yechim: $(15, 5)$.\\n\\nA variantda $x$ va $y$ o‘rni almashtirilgan. B va C variantlar $2x + y = 35$ ni qanoatlantiradi, lekin $x = 3y$ ni qanoatlantirmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A puppet theater in Tashkent sells adult tickets for 30,000 soums each and child tickets for 15,000 soums each. A family bought 9 tickets for a total of 195,000 soums. How many adult tickets did the family buy?\",\"option_a\":\"$4$\",\"option_b\":\"$5$\",\"option_c\":\"$6$\",\"option_d\":\"$13$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $a$ be the number of adult tickets and $c$ the number of child tickets: $a + c = 9$ and $30{,}000a + 15{,}000c = 195{,}000$.\\n\\nFrom the first equation, $c = 9 - a$. Substitute: $30{,}000a + 15{,}000(9 - a) = 195{,}000$, so $15{,}000a + 135{,}000 = 195{,}000$, $15{,}000a = 60{,}000$ and $a = 4$. Check: $4$ adult and $5$ child tickets cost $120{,}000 + 75{,}000 = 195{,}000$ soums.\\n\\nChoice B is the number of child tickets. Choice D divides the total by the child price as if every ticket were a child ticket. Choice C divides the total by the adult price and ignores the child tickets.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$a$ — kattalar chiptalari, $c$ — bolalar chiptalari soni bo‘lsin: $a + c = 9$ va $30{,}000a + 15{,}000c = 195{,}000$.\\n\\nBirinchi tenglamadan $c = 9 - a$. Qo‘yamiz: $30{,}000a + 15{,}000(9 - a) = 195{,}000$, ya’ni $15{,}000a + 135{,}000 = 195{,}000$, $15{,}000a = 60{,}000$ va $a = 4$. Tekshiruv: $4$ ta kattalar va $5$ ta bolalar chiptasi $120{,}000 + 75{,}000 = 195{,}000$ so‘m.\\n\\nB variant — bolalar chiptalari soni. D variantda umumiy summa bolalar chiptasi narxiga bo‘lingan, go‘yo hamma chipta bolalar uchun bo‘lgandek. C variantda umumiy summa kattalar chiptasi narxiga bo‘lingan va bolalar chiptalari hisobga olinmagan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} 4x + 3y &= 26 \\\\\\\\ 4x - 3y &= 2 \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIf $(x, y)$ is the solution to the given system of equations, what is the value of $x$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"7/2\",\"3.5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Add the two equations to eliminate $y$: $8x = 28$, so $x = \\\\frac{28}{8} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$. Enter 7/2 or 3.5. (Then $3y = 26 - 14 = 12$, so $y = 4$.)\\n\\nA common mistake is subtracting the equations, which eliminates $x$ instead and gives $6y = 24$; the value $4$ is $y$, not $x$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y$ ni yo‘qotish uchun tenglamalarni qo‘shamiz: $8x = 28$, demak $x = \\\\frac{28}{8} = \\\\frac{7}{2}$. Javobni 7/2 yoki 3.5 shaklida kiriting. (Keyin $3y = 26 - 14 = 12$, ya’ni $y = 4$.)\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: tenglamalarni ayirish. Bunda $x$ yo‘qolib, $6y = 24$ hosil bo‘ladi; $4$ esa $x$ emas, $y$ ning qiymati.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"At a market, 3 kilograms of apples and 2 kilograms of grapes cost a total of 63,000 soums. At the same prices, 1 kilogram of apples and 4 kilograms of grapes cost a total of 76,000 soums. What is the price, in soums, of 1 kilogram of grapes?\",\"option_a\":\"$10{,}000$\",\"option_b\":\"$16{,}500$\",\"option_c\":\"$19{,}000$\",\"option_d\":\"$21{,}000$\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $a$ and $g$ be the prices, in soums, of $1$ kilogram of apples and grapes: $3a + 2g = 63{,}000$ and $a + 4g = 76{,}000$.\\n\\nFrom the second equation, $a = 76{,}000 - 4g$. Substitute: $3(76{,}000 - 4g) + 2g = 63{,}000$, so $228{,}000 - 10g = 63{,}000$, $10g = 165{,}000$ and $g = 16{,}500$. Then $a = 10{,}000$.\\n\\nChoice A is the price of apples. Choice C divides $76{,}000$ by $4$, ignoring the apples. Choice D divides $63{,}000$ by $3$, which ignores the grapes in the first purchase.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$a$ va $g$ — $1$ kilogramm olma va uzum narxi (so‘mda) bo‘lsin: $3a + 2g = 63{,}000$ va $a + 4g = 76{,}000$.\\n\\nIkkinchi tenglamadan $a = 76{,}000 - 4g$. Qo‘yamiz: $3(76{,}000 - 4g) + 2g = 63{,}000$, ya’ni $228{,}000 - 10g = 63{,}000$, $10g = 165{,}000$ va $g = 16{,}500$. U holda $a = 10{,}000$.\\n\\nA variant — olma narxi. C variantda olma e’tiborga olinmay, $76{,}000$ $4$ ga bo‘lingan. D variantda birinchi xariddagi uzum e’tiborga olinmay, $63{,}000$ $3$ ga bo‘lingan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":100,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"In the $xy$-plane, the graphs of $y = 2x - 3$ and $y = -x + 9$ intersect at the point $(a, b)$. What is the value of $a + b$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"9\"],\"explanation_en\":\"At the intersection the $y$-values are equal: $2x - 3 = -x + 9$, so $3x = 12$ and $x = 4$. Then $y = 2(4) - 3 = 5$. So $a = 4$, $b = 5$ and $a + b = 9$.\\n\\nA common mistake is stopping after finding $a = 4$, or writing $x = 2$ from $3x = 6$ by subtracting $3$ instead of adding it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Kesishish nuqtasida $y$ qiymatlari teng: $2x - 3 = -x + 9$, ya’ni $3x = 12$ va $x = 4$. U holda $y = 2(4) - 3 = 5$. Demak $a = 4$, $b = 5$ va $a + b = 9$.\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xato: $a = 4$ ni topib to‘xtab qolish yoki $3$ ni qo‘shish o‘rniga ayirib, $3x = 6$ va $x = 2$ deb yozish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"$$\\\\begin{aligned} 2x - 5y &= 8 \\\\\\\\ 6x - 15y &= c \\\\end{aligned}$$\\n\\nIn the given system of equations, $c$ is a constant. For what value of $c$ does the system have infinitely many solutions?\",\"option_a\":\"$-24$\",\"option_b\":\"$8$\",\"option_c\":\"$24$\",\"option_d\":\"$40$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"A system of two linear equations has infinitely many solutions when one equation is a multiple of the other. Multiplying $2x - 5y = 8$ by $3$ gives $6x - 15y = 24$, so $c = 24$.\\n\\nFor any other value of $c$, the lines are parallel and distinct, and the system has no solution.\\n\\nChoice A uses the factor $-3$, but $6x - 15y$ is $+3$ times $2x - 5y$. Choice B keeps the right side unchanged. Choice D multiplies $8$ by $5$, the coefficient of $y$, instead of by the scale factor $3$.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikki chiziqli tenglamalar sistemasi bir tenglama ikkinchisiga karrali bo‘lganda cheksiz ko‘p yechimga ega bo‘ladi. $2x - 5y = 8$ ni $3$ ga ko‘paytirsak, $6x - 15y = 24$ hosil bo‘ladi, demak $c = 24$.\\n\\n$c$ ning boshqa har qanday qiymatida to‘g‘ri chiziqlar parallel va har xil bo‘ladi, sistema esa yechimga ega bo‘lmaydi.\\n\\nA variantda ko‘paytuvchi $-3$ olingan, lekin $6x - 15y$ ifoda $2x - 5y$ ning $+3$ barobari. B variantda o‘ng tomon o‘zgartirilmagan. D variantda $8$ ko‘paytuvchi $3$ ga emas, $y$ oldidagi koeffitsiyent $5$ ga ko‘paytirilgan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A boat travels 48 kilometers downstream (with the current) in 2 hours. The return trip of 48 kilometers upstream (against the current) takes 3 hours. The speed of the boat in still water and the speed of the current are both constant. What is the speed of the current, in kilometers per hour?\",\"option_a\":\"$4$\",\"option_b\":\"$8$\",\"option_c\":\"$16$\",\"option_d\":\"$20$\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Let $b$ be the boat's speed in still water and $w$ the speed of the current, both in km/h. Downstream speed: $b + w = \\\\frac{48}{2} = 24$. Upstream speed: $b - w = \\\\frac{48}{3} = 16$.\\n\\nSubtract the equations: $2w = 8$, so $w = 4$. (Adding them gives $2b = 40$, so $b = 20$.)\\n\\nChoice B is $24 - 16$, which equals $2w$, not $w$. Choice C is the upstream speed. Choice D is the speed of the boat in still water.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$b$ — qayiqning turg‘un suvdagi tezligi, $w$ — oqim tezligi (km/soat) bo‘lsin. Oqim bo‘ylab tezlik: $b + w = \\\\frac{48}{2} = 24$. Oqimga qarshi tezlik: $b - w = \\\\frac{48}{3} = 16$.\\n\\nTenglamalarni ayiramiz: $2w = 8$, demak $w = 4$. (Qo‘shsak, $2b = 40$, ya’ni $b = 20$.)\\n\\nB variant — $24 - 16$, bu $w$ emas, $2w$ ga teng. C variant — oqimga qarshi tezlik. D variant — qayiqning turg‘un suvdagi tezligi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"systems_linear_equations\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"Two pipes, A and B, each deliver water to a reservoir at its own constant rate. When both pipes are open for 4 hours, they deliver a total of 1,040 liters. When pipe A is open for 3 hours and pipe B is open for 5 hours, they deliver a total of 1,100 liters. At what rate, in liters per hour, does pipe A deliver water?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"100\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Let $a$ and $b$ be the rates of pipes A and B, in liters per hour. Then $4a + 4b = 1{,}040$, so $a + b = 260$, and $3a + 5b = 1{,}100$.\\n\\nSubstitute $b = 260 - a$: $3a + 5(260 - a) = 1{,}100$, so $1{,}300 - 2a = 1{,}100$, $2a = 200$ and $a = 100$. (Then $b = 160$. Check: $3(100) + 5(160) = 1{,}100$.)\\n\\nCommon mistakes: forgetting to divide $1{,}040$ by $4$ (using $a + b = 1{,}040$), or giving $160$, the rate of pipe B.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$a$ va $b$ — A va B quvurlarning tezligi (litr/soat) bo‘lsin. U holda $4a + 4b = 1{,}040$, ya’ni $a + b = 260$, va $3a + 5b = 1{,}100$.\\n\\n$b = 260 - a$ ni qo‘yamiz: $3a + 5(260 - a) = 1{,}100$, ya’ni $1{,}300 - 2a = 1{,}100$, $2a = 200$ va $a = 100$. (U holda $b = 160$. Tekshiruv: $3(100) + 5(160) = 1{,}100$.)\\n\\nKo‘p uchraydigan xatolar: $1{,}040$ ni $4$ ga bo‘lishni unutish ($a + b = 1{,}040$ deb olish) yoki B quvurning tezligi $160$ ni javob qilib yozish.\",\"estimated_seconds\":130,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Long before electric refrigerators, people in the deserts of Iran kept ice through the summer in structures called yakhchals. In winter, water was channeled into shallow pools, where it froze during the cold nights. The ice was cut into blocks and packed into a deep pit beneath a tall dome. The dome's thick walls, made of a special heat-resistant mortar, kept the ice frozen for months.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"To argue that yakhchals work better than modern refrigerators\",\"option_b\":\"To describe how a traditional structure allowed people to keep ice through hot summers\",\"option_c\":\"To explain why nights in the deserts of Iran are cold in winter\",\"option_d\":\"To compare several building materials used in desert architecture\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text introduces yakhchals and walks through how they worked: freezing water in winter, storing the blocks in a deep pit and keeping them cold beneath a thick-walled dome. Choice B states this purpose.\\n\\nChoice A is wrong because the text makes no comparison with modern refrigerators beyond noting that yakhchals came earlier. Choice C is wrong because the text mentions cold nights without explaining their cause. Choice D is wrong because the text mentions only one material, the mortar, and compares nothing.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn yaxchollarni tanishtiradi va ular qanday ishlaganini bosqichma-bosqich tushuntiradi: qishda suvni muzlatish, muz bo‘laklarini chuqur o‘raga joylash va qalin devorli gumbaz ostida sovuq saqlash. B javob shu maqsadni ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA noto‘g‘ri: matnda yaxchollar zamonaviy muzlatgichlardan oldin bo‘lgani aytiladi, xolos, ular solishtirilmaydi. C noto‘g‘ri: matnda sovuq tunlar tilga olinadi, lekin ularning sababi tushuntirilmaydi. D noto‘g‘ri: matnda faqat bitta material — qorishma tilga olinadi va hech narsa solishtirilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"At high altitudes, the air contains less oxygen, and mountain climbers often suffer headaches and shortness of breath. __Yet the bar-headed goose regularly flies over the Himalayas at heights above 7,000 meters, where the air is thinner still.__ Researchers have found that the goose's blood picks up oxygen unusually efficiently and that its flight muscles are packed with tiny blood vessels that deliver oxygen quickly.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It explains why mountain climbers suffer headaches at high altitudes.\",\"option_b\":\"It argues that bar-headed geese fly higher than any other bird.\",\"option_c\":\"It describes the methods researchers used to study bar-headed geese.\",\"option_d\":\"It introduces an animal that thrives in conditions that cause humans difficulty, setting up the explanation that follows.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence describes how thin air affects people. The underlined sentence, beginning with \\\"Yet,\\\" introduces a goose that flies in even thinner air, and the final sentence explains how the goose manages this. Choice D describes this function.\\n\\nChoice A describes the first sentence, not the underlined one. Choice B is wrong because the text never compares the goose with other birds. Choice C is wrong because the underlined sentence says nothing about research methods; the final sentence reports findings, not methods.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi jumla siyrak havo odamlarga qanday ta’sir qilishini tasvirlaydi. “Yet” bilan boshlangan tagiga chizilgan jumla bundan ham siyrak havoda uchadigan g‘ozni tanishtiradi, oxirgi jumla esa g‘oz buni qanday uddalashini tushuntiradi. D javob shu vazifani ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA tagiga chizilgan jumlani emas, birinchi jumlani tasvirlaydi. B noto‘g‘ri: matnda g‘oz boshqa qushlar bilan solishtirilmaydi. C noto‘g‘ri: tagiga chizilgan jumlada tadqiqot usullari haqida gap yo‘q; oxirgi jumlada ham usullar emas, natijalar keltiriladi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is adapted from a short story.\\n\\nShahlo checked her phone again. Nothing. She set it face down on the table, picked up her tea and put the cup back down without drinking. Through the window she watched a bus pull up, open its doors and drive away. Then she turned the phone over once more. The university had promised to announce its decisions by noon, and the clock on the wall said 11:52.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"To portray a character's restless anticipation as she waits to learn a decision\",\"option_b\":\"To explain why a character chose to apply to a particular university\",\"option_c\":\"To describe a character's usual morning routine\",\"option_d\":\"To contrast a character's calm mood with the busy street outside\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Shahlo repeatedly checks her phone, puts it down, picks up her tea without drinking, and watches the clock as the university's noon deadline approaches. These details portray her restless waiting, as choice A says.\\n\\nChoice B is wrong because the text never explains why she applied. Choice C is wrong because the scene shows a particular, tense morning, not a usual routine. Choice D is wrong because Shahlo is not calm, and the street is not described as busy; a single bus passes.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Shahlo telefonini qayta-qayta tekshiradi, uni yuzini pastga qilib qo‘yadi, choyini olib, ichmasdan joyiga qo‘yadi va universitet e’lon qiladigan peshin yaqinlashayotganida soatga qaraydi. Bu tafsilotlar uning bezovta kutishini tasvirlaydi — to‘g‘ri javob A.\\n\\nB noto‘g‘ri: matnda u nega hujjat topshirgani tushuntirilmaydi. C noto‘g‘ri: sahnada odatiy kun tartibi emas, o‘ziga xos, hayajonli tong tasvirlangan. D noto‘g‘ri: Shahlo xotirjam emas, ko‘cha ham gavjum deb tasvirlanmagan — faqat bitta avtobus o‘tadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Many people assume that trees produce the bright colors of autumn leaves only when the weather turns cool. In fact, the yellow and orange pigments in many leaves are present all summer, hidden by green chlorophyll. As the days shorten, trees stop making chlorophyll, and the hidden colors appear. Red colors are a different matter: the red pigments are newly produced in autumn, and scientists still debate why trees spend energy making them just before the leaves fall.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"It describes a scientific debate and then explains how that debate was finally settled.\",\"option_b\":\"It explains a natural process and then argues that one popular explanation of it is fully correct.\",\"option_c\":\"It presents a common assumption, explains why it is largely mistaken, and then identifies an exception whose cause is not yet understood.\",\"option_d\":\"It compares the leaves of trees in two regions and explains why they change color differently.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text opens with a common assumption about autumn colors, explains that yellow and orange pigments are actually present all summer, and then notes that red pigments are an exception, newly made in autumn for reasons scientists \\\"still debate.\\\" Choice C follows this sequence.\\n\\nChoice A is wrong because the debate mentioned at the end is unresolved. Choice B is wrong because the text corrects the popular assumption rather than defending it. Choice D is wrong because the text does not discuss different regions.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn kuz ranglari haqidagi keng tarqalgan tasavvur bilan boshlanadi, so‘ng sariq va to‘q sariq pigmentlar aslida butun yoz davomida barglarda bo‘lishini tushuntiradi va oxirida qizil pigmentlar istisno ekanini qayd etadi: ular kuzda yangidan hosil bo‘ladi, buning sababi esa hali ham bahsli (“still debate”). C javob shu ketma-ketlikka mos.\\n\\nA noto‘g‘ri: oxirida tilga olingan bahs hal qilinmagan. B noto‘g‘ri: matn keng tarqalgan tasavvurni himoya qilmaydi, balki uni tuzatadi. D noto‘g‘ri: matnda turli hududlar muhokama qilinmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"When the city of Vardo installed its first public water fountains in 1878, officials expected residents to use them mainly for drinking. __Within a year, however, more complaints were filed about people washing laundry in the fountains than about any other problem.__ In response, the city built public washhouses next to several of the fountains, and the washhouses soon became gathering places where neighbors exchanged news.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It describes an unexpected use of the fountains that led to the city's later decision to build washhouses.\",\"option_b\":\"It shows that residents rarely used the fountains that the city installed.\",\"option_c\":\"It explains why city officials decided to install the fountains.\",\"option_d\":\"It suggests that residents disliked the washhouses that the city built.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence states what officials expected the fountains to be used for. The underlined sentence, signaled by \\\"however,\\\" reveals a different use, washing laundry, and the next sentence describes the city's response: building washhouses. Choice A captures this role.\\n\\nChoice B contradicts the underlined sentence, which shows heavy use of the fountains. Choice C is wrong because the reason for installing the fountains appears in the first sentence and concerns drinking. Choice D is wrong because the washhouses became popular gathering places.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi jumlada rasmiylar favvoralardan nima maqsadda foydalanilishini kutgani aytiladi. “However” bilan ajratilgan tagiga chizilgan jumla boshqa foydalanish usulini — kir yuvishni ochib beradi, keyingi jumla esa shaharning javobini — kir yuvish uylari qurilganini tasvirlaydi. A javob shu vazifani ifodalaydi.\\n\\nB tagiga chizilgan jumlaga zid: unda favvoralardan faol foydalanilgani ko‘rinadi. C noto‘g‘ri: favvoralarni o‘rnatish sababi birinchi jumlada keltirilgan va u ichimlik suvi bilan bog‘liq. D noto‘g‘ri: kir yuvish uylari odamlar yig‘iladigan mashhur joylarga aylangan.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is from a poem. The speaker addresses a river.\\n\\nRiver, you never kept a single thing—\\nnot the leaf, not the light, not the moon's white coin\\nI watched you carry once beneath the bridge.\\nYou give back nothing, yet you are never empty.\\nTeach me that: to let the days go by\\nand still be full.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?\",\"option_a\":\"To warn of the dangers of crossing a river at night\",\"option_b\":\"To criticize the river for carrying away things the speaker valued\",\"option_c\":\"To recall in detail a particular childhood evening spent near the river\",\"option_d\":\"To express the speaker's wish to learn from the river how to let things pass without feeling empty\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The speaker observes that the river keeps nothing yet is \\\"never empty\\\" and then asks the river to \\\"teach me that: to let the days go by / and still be full.\\\" Choice D states this purpose.\\n\\nChoice A is wrong because the poem mentions no danger. Choice B is wrong because the speaker admires the river's way of letting things go rather than criticizing it. Choice C is wrong because the brief memory of the moon's reflection serves as an example of what the river does not keep; the poem does not recount a childhood evening in detail.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Shoir daryo hech narsani ushlab qolmasligini, ammo hech qachon bo‘sh bo‘lmasligini (“never empty”) kuzatadi va undan “menga shuni o‘rgat: kunlarni o‘tkazib yuborib, baribir to‘la bo‘lishni” deb so‘raydi. D javob shu maqsadni ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA noto‘g‘ri: she’rda hech qanday xavf tilga olinmaydi. B noto‘g‘ri: shoir daryoni tanqid qilmaydi, aksincha, uning narsalarni qo‘yib yuborishiga havas qiladi. C noto‘g‘ri: oyning aksi haqidagi qisqa xotira daryo ushlab qolmaydigan narsalarga misol sifatida keltirilgan; she’rda bolalikdagi oqshom batafsil hikoya qilinmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":72,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Surveys consistently find that people who own dogs are more physically active than people who do not. __But people who are already active may simply be more likely to get a dog in the first place.__ To find out, researchers tracked the daily step counts of adults for a year before and a year after they adopted dogs. On average, the new owners walked about 2,000 more steps a day after adopting than they had before.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It states the conclusion that the study described later in the text ultimately supports.\",\"option_b\":\"It provides evidence that owning a dog increases a person's physical activity.\",\"option_c\":\"It raises a possible alternative explanation for an observed pattern, which the study described next was designed to test.\",\"option_d\":\"It explains why the researchers' findings surprised other scientists.\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence reports a pattern: dog owners are more active. The underlined sentence offers another way to explain that pattern (active people may be the ones who get dogs), and the researchers then track the same people before and after adoption \\\"to find out.\\\" Choice C describes this function.\\n\\nChoice A is wrong because the study's result, an increase after adoption, points to dogs raising activity, not to the alternative explanation in the underlined sentence. Choice B is wrong because the underlined sentence questions that conclusion rather than supporting it. Choice D is wrong because the text never mentions other scientists' reactions.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi jumla qonuniyatni bayon qiladi: it egalari faolroq. Tagiga chizilgan jumla bu qonuniyatni boshqacha izohlaydi (faol odamlar it olishga ko‘proq moyil bo‘lishi mumkin), keyin esa tadqiqotchilar buni aniqlash uchun (“to find out”) o‘sha odamlarni it olishdan oldin va keyin kuzatadi. C javob shu vazifani ifodalaydi.\\n\\nA noto‘g‘ri: tadqiqot natijasi — it olgandan keyingi o‘sish — tagiga chizilgan jumladagi muqobil izohni emas, itlar faollikni oshirishini ko‘rsatadi. B noto‘g‘ri: tagiga chizilgan jumla bu xulosani tasdiqlamaydi, aksincha, unga shubha bildiradi. D noto‘g‘ri: matnda boshqa olimlarning munosabati haqida gap yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"text_structure_purpose\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The following text is adapted from a novel. Rustam works as a clerk in a shipping office.\\n\\nMr. Avery praised Rustam's handwriting, his punctuality, the neatness of his ledgers. He praised them every Friday, in the same words, as he handed out the week's wages. __Rustam had begun to suspect that the praise was a kind of wage too, paid in place of the raise he had asked for in March.__ Still, he thanked Mr. Avery each time, and each time Mr. Avery nodded, satisfied, as though a debt had been settled.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?\",\"option_a\":\"It shows that Rustam values Mr. Avery's praise more than he values his wages.\",\"option_b\":\"It reveals Rustam's growing belief that his employer's compliments are meant to substitute for higher pay.\",\"option_c\":\"It explains why Mr. Avery admires the quality of Rustam's work.\",\"option_d\":\"It indicates that Rustam has decided to leave his job at the shipping office.\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The underlined sentence tells us that Rustam suspects the weekly praise is \\\"a kind of wage,\\\" given \\\"in place of the raise he had asked for.\\\" This reveals his growing belief that the compliments replace better pay, as choice B says, and it prepares the final image of Mr. Avery acting \\\"as though a debt had been settled.\\\"\\n\\nChoice A misreads the sentence: Rustam thanks Mr. Avery, but the underlined sentence shows suspicion about the praise, not that he values it above money. Choice C is wrong because the sentence concerns Rustam's view of the praise, not the reasons for it. Choice D is unsupported: nothing suggests that Rustam plans to leave, and he keeps thanking Mr. Avery.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Tagiga chizilgan jumla Rustam haftalik maqtovni o‘zi so‘ragan maosh oshirish o‘rniga (“in place of the raise”) beriladigan o‘ziga xos “ish haqi” deb gumon qila boshlaganini aytadi. Bu uning maqtovlar yuqoriroq maosh o‘rnini bosish uchun aytilmoqda degan ishonchi kuchayib borayotganini ochib beradi — to‘g‘ri javob B. Shu bilan birga, u Mr. Averyning go‘yo qarz uzilgandek mamnun bosh irg‘ashi haqidagi yakuniy manzaraga zamin hozirlaydi.\\n\\nA jumlani noto‘g‘ri talqin qiladi: Rustam minnatdorchilik bildiradi, lekin tagiga chizilgan jumla maqtovga nisbatan gumonni ko‘rsatadi, uni puldan ustun qo‘yishini emas. C noto‘g‘ri: jumla maqtov sabablari haqida emas, Rustamning maqtovga qarashi haqida. D asossiz: Rustam ishdan ketmoqchi ekani haqida ishora yo‘q, u Mr. Averyga minnatdorchilik bildirishda davom etadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":88,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Octopuses have no bones; the only hard part of an octopus's body is its small, parrot-like beak. ______ an octopus can squeeze through almost any opening that is larger than its beak.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"As a result,\",\"option_b\":\"However,\",\"option_c\":\"For example,\",\"option_d\":\"In contrast,\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence explains that an octopus has no bones and only one small hard part. The second sentence describes a consequence of that body structure: it can squeeze through almost any opening larger than its beak. “As a result” correctly signals this cause-and-effect relationship.\\n\\n“However” and “In contrast” signal a contrast, but the second sentence follows from the first rather than opposing it. “For example” would introduce an example of the first sentence's claim, but squeezing through openings is a consequence of having no bones, not an example of it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap sakkizoyoqning suyaklari yo‘qligini va faqat bitta kichik qattiq a’zosi borligini tushuntiradi. Ikkinchi gap shu tana tuzilishining oqibatini tasvirlaydi: u tumshug‘idan kattaroq deyarli har qanday teshikdan o‘ta oladi. “As a result” (natijada) bu sabab-oqibat munosabatini to‘g‘ri ifodalaydi.\\n\\n“However” va “In contrast” qarama-qarshilikni bildiradi, lekin ikkinchi gap birinchisiga zid emas, undan kelib chiqadi. “For example” birinchi gapdagi fikrga misol keltiradi, ammo teshikdan o‘tish suyaksizlikning misoli emas, oqibatidir.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Most bats hunt at night and rely on echolocation, bouncing sounds off objects to locate insects in the dark. ______ many fruit bats find their food mainly by sight and smell, using large eyes and a keen sense of smell to locate ripe fruit.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Similarly,\",\"option_b\":\"Therefore,\",\"option_c\":\"By contrast,\",\"option_d\":\"For instance,\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence says most bats find food by echolocation. The second sentence says many fruit bats instead use sight and smell. Because the second sentence describes a different method, “By contrast” is the logical transition.\\n\\n“Similarly” would suggest that fruit bats find food in the same way as most bats, which is not what the text says. “Therefore” would mean that fruit bats use sight and smell because most bats use echolocation, which makes no sense. “For instance” would present fruit bats as an example of bats that use echolocation, but they are an exception.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gapda ko‘pchilik ko‘rshapalaklar ovqatni exolokatsiya orqali topishi aytiladi. Ikkinchi gapda esa ko‘plab mevaxo‘r ko‘rshapalaklar buning o‘rniga ko‘rish va hid bilish sezgisidan foydalanishi aytiladi. Ikkinchi gap boshqa usulni tasvirlagani uchun “By contrast” (aksincha) mantiqiy bog‘lovchi bo‘ladi.\\n\\n“Similarly” (xuddi shunday) mevaxo‘r ko‘rshapalaklar ham boshqalar kabi ovqat topadi degan ma’noni beradi, bu matnga zid. “Therefore” (shuning uchun) ko‘pchilik exolokatsiyadan foydalangani uchun mevaxo‘rlar ko‘z va hiddan foydalanadi degan ma’noni beradi — bu mantiqsiz. “For instance” mevaxo‘rlarni exolokatsiyadan foydalanuvchilarga misol qilib ko‘rsatadi, holbuki ular istisno.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"To make plov, cooks first heat oil in a heavy pot called a kazan and fry pieces of meat until they are brown. ______ they add sliced onions and carrots, which cook together with the meat before the rice is layered on top.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"In contrast,\",\"option_b\":\"Next,\",\"option_c\":\"For instance,\",\"option_d\":\"Nevertheless,\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text describes the steps of making plov in order: first the meat is fried, then onions and carrots are added, and finally the rice is layered on top. “Next” correctly signals the following step in this sequence.\\n\\n“In contrast” and “Nevertheless” signal opposition, but adding vegetables does not contrast with frying meat. “For instance” would present the vegetables as an example of frying meat, which is illogical.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn palov tayyorlash bosqichlarini tartib bilan tasvirlaydi: avval go‘sht qovuriladi, keyin piyoz va sabzi qo‘shiladi, oxirida ustidan guruch solinadi. “Next” (keyin) bu ketma-ketlikdagi navbatdagi bosqichni to‘g‘ri bildiradi.\\n\\n“In contrast” va “Nevertheless” qarama-qarshilikni bildiradi, ammo sabzavot qo‘shish go‘sht qovurishga zid emas. “For instance” sabzavotlarni go‘sht qovurishning misoli sifatida ko‘rsatadi, bu mantiqsiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Many shoppers assume that the palest honey on the shelf will always have the mildest flavor. Color, ______ is a poor guide to taste: some very light honeys, such as those made from linden blossoms, have a sharp, almost minty flavor.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"for example,\",\"option_b\":\"in other words,\",\"option_c\":\"similarly,\",\"option_d\":\"however,\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence describes an assumption that pale honey is always mild. The second sentence contradicts it: color is a poor guide, and some light honeys taste sharp. “However” correctly signals this contrast between the assumption and reality.\\n\\n“For example” would present the second sentence as an example of the assumption, but it disproves the assumption. “In other words” would mean the second sentence restates the first, yet it says the opposite. “Similarly” would suggest the two sentences make parallel points, which they do not.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gapda och rangli asal har doim yumshoq ta’mli bo‘ladi degan taxmin tasvirlanadi. Ikkinchi gap unga zid: rang ta’mni aniqlash uchun yomon ko‘rsatkich, ba’zi och rangli asallar o‘tkir ta’mga ega. “However” (biroq) taxmin va haqiqat o‘rtasidagi bu qarama-qarshilikni to‘g‘ri ifodalaydi.\\n\\n“For example” ikkinchi gapni taxminga misol sifatida ko‘rsatadi, holbuki u taxminni rad etadi. “In other words” (boshqacha aytganda) ikkinchi gap birinchisini qayta ifodalaydi degan ma’noni beradi, ammo u aksini aytadi. “Similarly” ikkala gap bir xil fikrni bildiradi degan ma’no beradi, bu noto‘g‘ri.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Itchan Kala, the inner town of Khiva, is enclosed by mud-brick walls about 10 meters high that have stood for centuries. ______ the town contains more than fifty historic monuments, including mosques, madrasas, and palaces, within an area that can be crossed on foot in about fifteen minutes.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Moreover,\",\"option_b\":\"Instead,\",\"option_c\":\"Consequently,\",\"option_d\":\"Regardless,\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"Both sentences describe impressive features of Itchan Kala: its ancient walls and its many monuments packed into a small area. The second sentence adds further information supporting the same picture, so “Moreover” is the logical choice.\\n\\n“Instead” would suggest that the monuments replace the walls, which makes no sense. “Consequently” would mean the walls caused the town to contain many monuments, a relationship the text does not suggest. “Regardless” would imply that the second fact holds despite the first, but nothing about the walls works against the monuments.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ikkala gap ham Ichan qal’aning ta’sirli jihatlarini tasvirlaydi: qadimiy devorlari va kichik hududga jamlangan ko‘plab yodgorliklari. Ikkinchi gap xuddi shu manzarani to‘ldiruvchi qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi, shuning uchun “Moreover” (bundan tashqari) mantiqiy tanlov.\\n\\n“Instead” (o‘rniga) yodgorliklar devorlar o‘rnini egallaydi degan ma’noni beradi, bu mantiqsiz. “Consequently” (natijada) devorlar sababli shaharda ko‘p yodgorlik bor degan ma’noni beradi — matn bunday bog‘liqlikni ko‘rsatmaydi. “Regardless” (qaramay) ikkinchi fakt birinchisiga qaramay to‘g‘ri degan ma’noni beradi, ammo devorlar yodgorliklarga hech qanday to‘sqinlik qilmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Some plants have evolved surprising ways of spreading their seeds far from the parent plant. ______ when the fruit of the squirting cucumber ripens, pressure builds up inside it until the fruit bursts off its stem, spraying seeds several meters away.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Nonetheless,\",\"option_b\":\"Likewise,\",\"option_c\":\"For example,\",\"option_d\":\"In summary,\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The first sentence makes a general claim: some plants have surprising ways of spreading seeds. The second sentence describes one specific plant, the squirting cucumber, that does this. “For example” correctly introduces a specific example of the general claim.\\n\\n“Nonetheless” signals a contrast, but the second sentence supports the first. “Likewise” would introduce a separate, similar point rather than an instance of the first claim. “In summary” would introduce a restatement of earlier points, but the second sentence adds a new, specific detail.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Birinchi gap umumiy fikr bildiradi: ba’zi o‘simliklar urug‘larini tarqatishning hayratlanarli usullariga ega. Ikkinchi gap buni qiladigan bitta aniq o‘simlik — sapchiydigan bodringni tasvirlaydi. “For example” (masalan) umumiy fikrga aniq misolni to‘g‘ri kiritadi.\\n\\n“Nonetheless” qarama-qarshilikni bildiradi, ammo ikkinchi gap birinchisini qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi. “Likewise” (xuddi shuningdek) birinchi fikrning misolini emas, alohida o‘xshash fikrni kiritadi. “In summary” (xulosa qilib aytganda) avvalgi fikrlarni umumlashtiradi, ikkinchi gap esa yangi, aniq tafsilot qo‘shadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Agronomists expected that adding more fertilizer to their test fields would steadily increase the cotton harvest. Up to a point, it did: yields rose as fertilizer use climbed to moderate levels. Beyond that point, ______ extra fertilizer brought no further gain and in some fields even lowered yields, as excess nitrogen encouraged leafy growth at the expense of cotton bolls.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"for instance,\",\"option_b\":\"similarly,\",\"option_c\":\"therefore,\",\"option_d\":\"however,\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text first says that yields rose as fertilizer use increased to moderate levels. The final sentence describes what happened beyond that point: extra fertilizer brought no gain and sometimes lowered yields. This outcome contrasts with both the expectation of a steady increase and the earlier rise, so “however” is the logical transition.\\n\\n“For instance” would present the final sentence as an example of yields rising, but it describes the opposite. “Similarly” would suggest that the results beyond the point matched the earlier rise. “Therefore” would mean that the earlier rise caused the later decline, a relationship the text does not claim; the text gives a different cause, excess nitrogen.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda avval o‘g‘it miqdori o‘rtacha darajagacha oshirilganda hosil ortgani aytiladi. Oxirgi gap esa o‘sha nuqtadan keyin nima bo‘lganini tasvirlaydi: qo‘shimcha o‘g‘it foyda bermagan, ba’zan hatto hosilni kamaytirgan. Bu natija ham hosil doimiy o‘sadi degan kutishga, ham avvalgi o‘sishga zid, shuning uchun “however” (biroq) mantiqiy bog‘lovchi.\\n\\n“For instance” oxirgi gapni hosil o‘sishiga misol qilib ko‘rsatadi, holbuki u aksini tasvirlaydi. “Similarly” o‘sha nuqtadan keyingi natijalar avvalgi o‘sishga o‘xshash degan ma’no beradi. “Therefore” avvalgi o‘sish keyingi pasayishga sabab bo‘lgan degan ma’no beradi — matn bunday demaydi, u boshqa sababni, ortiqcha azotni ko‘rsatadi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"transitions\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Critics of the city's plan to plant 10,000 street trees pointed out that the young trees would need years of regular watering before they provided any real shade. The plan's supporters did not dispute this point. ______ they argued that the cost of watering was small compared with the long-term benefits, since mature trees can lower nearby street temperatures by several degrees.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?\",\"option_a\":\"Similarly,\",\"option_b\":\"Instead,\",\"option_c\":\"As a result,\",\"option_d\":\"For example,\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text says the supporters “did not dispute” the critics' point. The next sentence describes what they did in place of disputing it: they argued that the benefits outweighed the cost. “Instead” correctly signals this alternative response.\\n\\n“Similarly” would suggest the supporters made the same argument as the critics, but they reached the opposite conclusion about the plan. “As a result” would mean the supporters argued for the plan because they did not dispute the point, which is not a cause-and-effect relationship. “For example” would present the argument as an example of not disputing the point, which is illogical.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda tarafdorlar tanqidchilarning fikrini “did not dispute” — rad etmagani aytiladi. Keyingi gap ular rad etish o‘rniga nima qilganini tasvirlaydi: foydasi xarajatdan ko‘p ekanini ta’kidlashgan. “Instead” (buning o‘rniga) bu muqobil javobni to‘g‘ri bildiradi.\\n\\n“Similarly” tarafdorlar tanqidchilar bilan bir xil dalil keltirgan degan ma’noni beradi, holbuki ular reja haqida qarama-qarshi xulosaga kelgan. “As a result” tarafdorlar fikrni rad etmagani uchun reja foydasiga gapirgan degan ma’noni beradi, bu sabab-oqibat emas. “For example” dalilni rad etmaslikning misoli sifatida ko‘rsatadi — bu mantiqsiz.\",\"estimated_seconds\":75,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A teacher collected data from 30 students on the number of hours each student studied per week, $x$, and each student's score on a final exam, $y$. The line of best fit for the data is $y = 2.5x + 58$. Which of the following is the best interpretation of 2.5 in this context?\",\"option_a\":\"The predicted exam score of a student who does not study\",\"option_b\":\"The predicted increase in exam score for each additional hour studied per week\",\"option_c\":\"The predicted number of hours studied per week by a student who scores 58\",\"option_d\":\"The actual exam score of every student who studies 1 hour per week\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"In a linear model $y = mx + b$, the slope $m$ is the change in $y$ for each increase of 1 in $x$. Here the slope is 2.5, so the model predicts that a student's exam score increases by 2.5 points for each additional hour studied per week. Choice A describes the $y$-intercept, 58. Choice C confuses the variables. Choice D is wrong because a line of best fit gives **predicted** values, not actual scores, and the predicted score at $x = 1$ is $60.5$, not 2.5.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$y = mx + b$ chiziqli modelida $m$ qiyalik — $x$ 1 ga ortganda $y$ ning o‘zgarishi. Bu yerda qiyalik 2.5, demak model bo‘yicha haftalik o‘qish vaqti har 1 soatga ortganda imtihon bali 2.5 ballga oshadi. A javob $y$ o‘qi bilan kesishish nuqtasi 58 ni tasvirlaydi. C javob o‘zgaruvchilarni chalkashtirgan. D javob noto‘g‘ri, chunki eng yaxshi moslik chizig‘i haqiqiy emas, **bashorat qilingan** qiymatlarni beradi; bundan tashqari, $x = 1$ dagi bashorat 2.5 emas, $60.5$.\",\"estimated_seconds\":60,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A scientist measured the air temperature at different altitudes on a mountain at the same time of day. The line of best fit for the data is $y = -0.65x + 31$, where $y$ is the predicted temperature, in degrees Celsius, and $x$ is the altitude, in hundreds of meters. According to the line of best fit, what is the predicted temperature, in degrees Celsius, at an altitude of 1,200 meters?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"23.2\",\"116/5\"],\"explanation_en\":\"Because $x$ is measured in hundreds of meters, an altitude of 1,200 meters corresponds to $x = 12$. Then $y = -0.65(12) + 31 = -7.8 + 31 = 23.2$. Substituting $x = 1{,}200$ directly gives $-749$, a temperature that makes no sense here; always check the units of $x$. Enter 23.2 or 116/5.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x$ yuzlab metrlarda o‘lchangani uchun 1,200 metr balandlik $x = 12$ ga mos keladi. U holda $y = -0.65(12) + 31 = -7.8 + 31 = 23.2$. To‘g‘ridan-to‘g‘ri $x = 1{,}200$ ni qo‘yish $-749$ ni beradi — bu yerda mantiqsiz harorat; har doim $x$ ning birliklarini tekshiring. Javob maydoniga 23.2 yoki 116/5 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following best describes the relationship between the age and the price of the cars in the table?\",\"passage\":\"The table shows the age, in years, and the price, in millions of soums, of 8 used cars of the same model.\\n\\n| Age (years) | Price (millions of soums) |\\n| ---: | ---: |\\n| 1 | 178 |\\n| 2 | 160 |\\n| 3 | 149 |\\n| 4 | 131 |\\n| 5 | 120 |\\n| 6 | 104 |\\n| 7 | 92 |\\n| 8 | 77 |\",\"option_a\":\"A positive linear association\",\"option_b\":\"An exponential growth relationship\",\"option_c\":\"No association\",\"option_d\":\"A negative linear association\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"As the age increases, the price decreases, so the association is negative. The price drops by roughly the same amount (between 11 and 18 million soums) for each additional year, so the pattern is approximately linear. Choice A would mean that older cars tend to cost more. Choice B would require the prices to increase, and by a growing amount each year. Choice C is wrong because the prices follow a clear downward pattern.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Yosh ortgan sari narx kamayadi, demak bog‘liqlik manfiy. Har bir qo‘shimcha yil uchun narx taxminan bir xil miqdorga (11 dan 18 million so‘mgacha) tushadi, demak bog‘liqlik taxminan chiziqli. A javob eski avtomobillar qimmatroq bo‘lishini anglatardi. B javob uchun narxlar o‘sishi, har yili esa tobora ko‘proq o‘sishi kerak edi. C javob noto‘g‘ri, chunki narxlar aniq kamayish tendensiyasiga ega.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"A scatterplot shows the number of hours, $x$, that each of 20 workers spent on training and the number of products, $y$, each worker assembled in one day. The line of best fit for the data is $y = 4x + 20$. One worker spent 6 hours on training and assembled 41 products in one day. Which of the following is true about this worker's data point?\",\"option_a\":\"The actual number of products is 3 less than the number predicted by the line of best fit.\",\"option_b\":\"The actual number of products is 3 greater than the number predicted by the line of best fit.\",\"option_c\":\"The actual number of products is 17 greater than the number predicted by the line of best fit.\",\"option_d\":\"The actual number of products is equal to the number predicted by the line of best fit.\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The predicted number of products for $x = 6$ is $4(6) + 20 = 44$. The worker actually assembled 41 products, and $41 - 44 = -3$, so the actual number is 3 **less** than predicted (the point lies below the line). Choice B has the right size of difference but the wrong direction. Choice C compares 41 with $4(6) = 24$, forgetting to add 20: $41 - 24 = 17$. Choice D would require the point to lie on the line.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x = 6$ uchun bashorat qilingan mahsulotlar soni $4(6) + 20 = 44$. Ishchi aslida 41 ta mahsulot yig‘gan, $41 - 44 = -3$, demak haqiqiy son bashoratdan 3 ta **kam** (nuqta chiziqdan pastda). B javobda farq miqdori to‘g‘ri, lekin yo‘nalishi teskari. C javob 20 ni qo‘shishni unutib, 41 ni $4(6) = 24$ bilan solishtirgan: $41 - 24 = 17$. D javob nuqta chiziq ustida yotishini talab qilardi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A model predicts the value of a laptop $x$ years after it is bought. According to the model, the value $V$, in thousands of soums, is $V = 9{,}600(0.88)^x$. According to the model, the value of the laptop decreases by what percent each year?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"12\"],\"explanation_en\":\"In an exponential model $V = a(b)^x$ with $0 < b < 1$, the value is multiplied by $b$ each year, so it decreases by $(1 - b) \\\\times 100\\\\%$ each year. Here $b = 0.88$, so the value decreases by $(1 - 0.88) \\\\times 100\\\\% = 12\\\\%$ per year. Entering 88 confuses the percent that **remains** each year with the percent lost. Enter 12.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$0 < b < 1$ bo‘lgan $V = a(b)^x$ eksponensial modelida qiymat har yili $b$ ga ko‘paytiriladi, demak har yili $(1 - b) \\\\times 100\\\\%$ ga kamayadi. Bu yerda $b = 0.88$, shuning uchun qiymat har yili $(1 - 0.88) \\\\times 100\\\\% = 12\\\\%$ ga kamayadi. 88 deb yozish har yili **qoladigan** foizni yo‘qotilgan foiz bilan chalkashtirishdir. Javob maydoniga 12 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following equations best models the data in the table?\",\"passage\":\"The table shows the amount of water $y$, in liters, remaining in a tank $x$ minutes after a valve was opened.\\n\\n| $x$ (minutes) | $y$ (liters) |\\n| ---: | ---: |\\n| 0 | 80 |\\n| 2 | 71 |\\n| 4 | 62 |\\n| 6 | 53 |\",\"option_a\":\"$y = 80 - 9x$\",\"option_b\":\"$y = 80(0.89)^x$\",\"option_c\":\"$y = 80 - 4.5x$\",\"option_d\":\"$y = 53 + 4.5x$\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Each time $x$ increases by 2, $y$ decreases by 9, so the data are linear with slope $\\\\frac{-9}{2} = -4.5$. At $x = 0$, $y = 80$, so the model is $y = 80 - 4.5x$. Check: at $x = 6$, $80 - 4.5(6) = 53$. Choice A uses the change in $y$ per 2 units of $x$ as the slope. Choice B is exponential, but the data decrease by a constant **difference**, not a constant ratio. Choice D has a positive slope and starts at the last value, so it predicts increasing values.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"$x$ har safar 2 ga ortganda $y$ 9 ga kamayadi, demak ma’lumotlar chiziqli va qiyalik $\\\\frac{-9}{2} = -4.5$. $x = 0$ da $y = 80$, demak model $y = 80 - 4.5x$. Tekshiruv: $x = 6$ da $80 - 4.5(6) = 53$. A javob $x$ ning 2 birlik o‘zgarishiga mos $y$ o‘zgarishini qiyalik deb olgan. B javob eksponensial, lekin ma’lumotlar o‘zgarmas nisbat bilan emas, o‘zgarmas **ayirma** bilan kamayadi. D javobning qiyaligi musbat va u oxirgi qiymatdan boshlanadi, shuning uchun o‘suvchi qiymatlarni beradi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":90,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stem\":\"For each of two cities, a researcher made a scatterplot of the number of years since 2015, $x$, and the number of electric buses in service, $y$. The line of best fit for City A is $y = 1.2x + 5$, and the line of best fit for City B is $y = 0.8x + 9$. Which of the following statements is true according to the lines of best fit?\",\"option_a\":\"For every value of $x$, City B is predicted to have more electric buses than City A.\",\"option_b\":\"City A and City B are predicted to have the same number of electric buses when $x = 14$.\",\"option_c\":\"For every value of $x$ less than 10, City A is predicted to have more electric buses than City B.\",\"option_d\":\"For every value of $x$ greater than 10, City A is predicted to have more electric buses than City B.\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The predictions are equal when $1.2x + 5 = 0.8x + 9$, so $0.4x = 4$ and $x = 10$ (both predict 17 buses). Because City A's line has the greater slope (1.2 versus 0.8), City A's predicted number grows faster, so for $x > 10$ City A's prediction is greater. For example, at $x = 15$: City A, $23$; City B, $21$. Choice C reverses the inequality: for $x < 10$, City B's prediction is greater. Choice A ignores that the lines cross. Choice B comes from an error in solving the equation; at $x = 14$ the predictions are 21.8 and 20.2.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Bashoratlar $1.2x + 5 = 0.8x + 9$ bo‘lganda teng, ya’ni $0.4x = 4$ va $x = 10$ (ikkalasi ham 17 ta avtobusni bashorat qiladi). A shahar chizig‘ining qiyaligi kattaroq (1.2 va 0.8), shuning uchun A shahar bashorati tezroq o‘sadi va $x > 10$ da A shaharniki katta bo‘ladi. Masalan, $x = 15$ da: A shahar — $23$, B shahar — $21$. C javob tengsizlikni teskari olgan: $x < 10$ da B shahar bashorati katta. A javob chiziqlar kesishishini e’tiborsiz qoldirgan. B javob tenglamani yechishdagi xatodan kelib chiqqan; $x = 14$ da bashoratlar 21.8 va 20.2.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"two_variable_data\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"spr\",\"stem\":\"A line of best fit for a data set is $y = ax + 15$, where $a$ is a constant. The line of best fit predicts a $y$-value of 51 when $x = 8$. The data set includes the point $(12, 66)$. What is the actual $y$-value of this point minus the $y$-value predicted by the line of best fit when $x = 12$?\",\"spr_answers\":[\"-3\"],\"explanation_en\":\"First find $a$: $8a + 15 = 51$, so $8a = 36$ and $a = 4.5$. The predicted $y$-value when $x = 12$ is $4.5(12) + 15 = 54 + 15 = 69$. The actual value is 66, so actual minus predicted is $66 - 69 = -3$. The negative sign shows that the point lies below the line. Entering 3 reverses the subtraction (predicted minus actual). Enter -3.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Avval $a$ ni topamiz: $8a + 15 = 51$, demak $8a = 36$ va $a = 4.5$. $x = 12$ da bashorat qilingan qiymat $4.5(12) + 15 = 54 + 15 = 69$. Haqiqiy qiymat 66, demak haqiqiy minus bashorat $66 - 69 = -3$. Manfiy ishora nuqta chiziqdan pastda yotishini ko‘rsatadi. 3 deb yozish ayirishni teskari bajarish (bashorat minus haqiqiy) bo‘ladi. Javob maydoniga -3 deb yozing.\",\"estimated_seconds\":120,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Chess coach Rustam Aliev is famously ______ with praise. Former students say that in ten years of lessons, they heard him call a move “excellent” only a handful of times, and most of his comments pointed out what could have been played better.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"generous\",\"option_b\":\"sparing\",\"option_c\":\"careless\",\"option_d\":\"quick\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text says Aliev called a move “excellent” only a handful of times in ten years and usually pointed out mistakes, so he gives praise rarely: he is “sparing” with it. “Generous” means the opposite, giving praise freely. “Careless” suggests he praises without thinking, which the text does not describe. “Quick” with praise would mean he praises readily, which also contradicts the text.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnga ko‘ra, Aliev o‘n yil ichida biror yurishni atigi bir necha marta “excellent” deb atagan va ko‘pincha xatolarni ko‘rsatgan. Demak, u maqtovni juda kam beradi — bu “sparing” (tejamkor, xasis) so‘zining ma’nosi. “Generous” (saxiy) buning aksini bildiradi: maqtovni ko‘p berish. “Careless” (beparvo) — o‘ylamasdan maqtash degani, matnda bunday gap yo‘q. “Quick” with praise — tez-tez, osonlik bilan maqtash degani, bu ham matnga zid.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"The museum's exhibit on desert insects proved so popular that the curators decided to let it run for another three months. Schoolchildren in particular kept coming back to watch the live beetles and ants, and ticket sales stayed high long after the opening week.\",\"stem\":\"As used in the text, what does the word “run” most nearly mean?\",\"option_a\":\"continue\",\"option_b\":\"hurry\",\"option_c\":\"manage\",\"option_d\":\"flow\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The exhibit was popular, so the curators let it “run” for three more months, meaning they let it go on being shown: “continue.” “Hurry” fits “run to the bus,” not an exhibit that stays open. “Manage” fits “run a business,” but the curators already manage the exhibit; the point is how long it stays open. “Flow” fits liquids, as in “water runs downhill,” not an exhibit.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Ko‘rgazma mashhur bo‘lgani uchun kuratorlar uni yana uch oy “run” qilishga ruxsat berishgan, ya’ni ko‘rgazma davom etadi — “continue” (davom etmoq). “Hurry” (shoshilmoq) “run to the bus” kabi iboralarga mos, ochiq turgan ko‘rgazmaga emas. “Manage” (boshqarmoq) “run a business” ma’nosiga mos, ammo bu yerda gap ko‘rgazma qancha vaqt ochiq turishi haqida. “Flow” (oqmoq) suyuqliklarga tegishli, ko‘rgazmaga emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":50,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Glaciers can look perfectly still, but most of them are anything but ______. Using GPS markers placed on the ice, researchers found that one glacier in Alaska slid nearly 40 meters downhill in a single year.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"massive\",\"option_b\":\"frozen\",\"option_c\":\"ancient\",\"option_d\":\"stationary\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text contrasts how glaciers look (“perfectly still”) with what the GPS data show: a glacier slid nearly 40 meters in a year. So glaciers are “anything but stationary,” meaning they are not motionless. “Massive,” “frozen” and “ancient” may all describe glaciers, but saying glaciers are “anything but” massive, frozen or ancient would contradict facts about glaciers, and none of these words connects to the evidence about movement.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matn muzliklarning tashqi ko‘rinishini (“perfectly still” — butunlay harakatsiz) GPS ma’lumotlari bilan qarama-qarshi qo‘yadi: bir muzlik bir yilda deyarli 40 metr pastga siljigan. Demak, muzliklar “anything but stationary”, ya’ni umuman harakatsiz emas. “Massive” (ulkan), “frozen” (muzlagan) va “ancient” (qadimiy) muzliklarni tasvirlashi mumkin, lekin muzliklar bularning “aksi” deyish faktlarga zid bo‘lardi va bu so‘zlarning hech biri harakat haqidagi dalilga bog‘lanmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":55,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Early reactions to the city's redesigned bus routes were ______. Some riders praised the shorter waits at downtown stops, while others complained that the changes had left their neighborhoods with fewer direct connections to the center.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"unanimous\",\"option_b\":\"scathing\",\"option_c\":\"mixed\",\"option_d\":\"delayed\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text describes two opposite reactions: some riders praised the new routes and others complained. Reactions that include both praise and criticism are “mixed.” “Unanimous” means everyone agreed, which contradicts the split. “Scathing” means harshly critical, which ignores the riders who praised the routes. “Delayed” means late, but nothing in the text suggests the reactions came slowly.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda ikki qarama-qarshi munosabat bor: ba’zi yo‘lovchilar yangi yo‘nalishlarni maqtagan, boshqalari esa shikoyat qilgan. Ham maqtov, ham tanqidni o‘z ichiga olgan munosabat — “mixed” (aralash). “Unanimous” (bir ovozdan) hamma bir fikrda bo‘lganini bildiradi, bu esa fikrlar bo‘linganiga zid. “Scathing” (keskin tanqidiy) maqtagan yo‘lovchilarni inobatga olmaydi. “Delayed” (kechikkan) — matnda munosabatlar kech bildirilgani haqida hech narsa yo‘q.\",\"estimated_seconds\":65,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Marine biologist Teo Lindqvist argues that some coral reefs have survived warming seas because of their ability to host new kinds of algae. Corals that cannot take in heat-tolerant algae, he notes, are far more likely to bleach and die when water temperatures rise.\",\"stem\":\"As used in the text, what does the word “host” most nearly mean?\",\"option_a\":\"accommodate\",\"option_b\":\"entertain\",\"option_c\":\"present\",\"option_d\":\"organize\",\"correct\":\"A\",\"explanation_en\":\"The text explains that surviving corals can “host” new algae, and the next sentence restates this as being able to “take in” heat-tolerant algae. So “host” means to provide a place for something to live: “accommodate.” “Entertain” fits hosting guests at a party, not algae living in coral. “Present” fits hosting a television show. “Organize” fits hosting an event, which does not describe corals taking in algae.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Matnda omon qolgan marjonlar yangi suvo‘tlarni “host” qila olishi aytiladi, keyingi gapda esa bu issiqqa chidamli suvo‘tlarni “take in” — o‘ziga qabul qilish deb qayta ifodalanadi. Demak, “host” bu yerda biror narsaga yashash joyi berish — “accommodate” (joylashtirmoq, sig‘dirmoq). “Entertain” (mehmon kutmoq, ko‘ngil ochmoq) ziyofatga mos, marjondagi suvo‘tlarga emas. “Present” (olib bormoq) teleko‘rsatuvga mos. “Organize” (tashkil qilmoq) tadbirga mos va marjonning suvo‘tlarni qabul qilishini tasvirlamaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"medium\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Historian Ilhom Saidov argues that the merchants of medieval Bukhara were not ______ go-betweens who simply moved goods from East to West. Their surviving letters show that they actively shaped demand, for instance by ordering textiles in colors and patterns they knew would sell well in distant markets.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"ambitious\",\"option_b\":\"prosperous\",\"option_c\":\"skilled\",\"option_d\":\"passive\",\"correct\":\"D\",\"explanation_en\":\"The sentence says the merchants were not go-betweens who “simply moved goods,” and the next sentence shows them “actively” shaping demand. The missing word must therefore be the opposite of active: “passive.” “Ambitious” and “skilled” describe traits that the letters actually support, so saying the merchants were “not” ambitious or skilled would contradict the evidence. “Prosperous” is about wealth, which the text does not discuss.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Gapda savdogarlar tovarlarni “shunchaki” tashuvchi vositachilar bo‘lmagani aytiladi, keyingi gap esa ular talabni “faol” shakllantirganini ko‘rsatadi. Demak, bo‘sh joyga “faol” so‘zining aksi kerak — “passive” (sust, passiv). “Ambitious” (shuhratparast, intiluvchan) va “skilled” (mohir) xatlar tasdiqlaydigan xususiyatlar, shuning uchun savdogarlar bunday “emas edi” deyish dalilga zid bo‘ladi. “Prosperous” (badavlat) boylik haqida, matnda esa bu muhokama qilinmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":70,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Physicist Lena Moroz admits that she once entertained the idea that a strange signal in her detector came from a distant, previously unknown star. Months of testing, however, traced the signal to a faulty cable, and she now tells the story to warn students against reaching dramatic conclusions too quickly.\",\"stem\":\"As used in the text, what does the word “entertained” most nearly mean?\",\"option_a\":\"amused\",\"option_b\":\"hosted\",\"option_c\":\"considered\",\"option_d\":\"celebrated\",\"correct\":\"C\",\"explanation_en\":\"Moroz “entertained the idea” that the signal came from a star before testing showed it came from a faulty cable. She thought about the idea as a possibility, so “entertained” means “considered.” “Amused” uses the sense of entertaining an audience, which makes no sense with “the idea.” “Hosted” uses the sense of entertaining guests. “Celebrated” goes too far: the text says only that she thought the idea possible, and she now warns against reaching dramatic conclusions, not that she publicly rejoiced over it.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"Moroz sinovlar signal nosoz kabeldan kelganini ko‘rsatmasdan oldin signal yulduzdan keladi degan g‘oyani “entertained” qilgan. U bu g‘oyani ehtimol sifatida ko‘rib chiqqan, demak “entertained” bu yerda “considered” (ko‘rib chiqmoq, o‘ylab ko‘rmoq) ma’nosida. “Amused” (kuldirmoq) tomoshabinlarni xursand qilish ma’nosidan olingan va “the idea” bilan mos kelmaydi. “Hosted” (mehmon qilmoq) mehmon kutish ma’nosidan olingan. “Celebrated” (nishonlamoq) haddan oshib ketadi: matnda u faqat bu g‘oyani mumkin deb o‘ylagani aytilgan, uni tantana qilgani emas.\",\"estimated_seconds\":80,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]},{\"skill_code\":\"words_in_context\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"question_type\":\"mc\",\"stimulus_type\":\"passage\",\"passage\":\"Critics have long praised novelist Kenji Arata for his spare, unadorned prose. His latest book, however, marks a striking departure from that style: its sentences are ______, crowded with long lists, elaborate metaphors, and clause after clause of description.\",\"stem\":\"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?\",\"option_a\":\"laconic\",\"option_b\":\"florid\",\"option_c\":\"candid\",\"option_d\":\"halting\",\"correct\":\"B\",\"explanation_en\":\"The word “however” signals that the new book differs from Arata's usual “spare, unadorned” prose, and the colon introduces a description of sentences crowded with lists, metaphors and description. Such heavily decorated writing is “florid.” “Laconic” means using very few words, which describes his old spare style, not the new one. “Candid” means frank or open, which says nothing about how decorated the sentences are. “Halting” means hesitant or broken, which does not match long, flowing, crowded sentences.\",\"explanation_uz\":\"“However” so‘zi yangi kitob Arataning odatiy “spare, unadorned” (sodda, bezaksiz) uslubidan farq qilishini bildiradi, ikki nuqtadan keyin esa ro‘yxatlar, murakkab metaforalar va tasvirlarga to‘la gaplar tasvirlanadi. Bunday ortiqcha bezakli uslub — “florid” (dabdabali, jimjimador). “Laconic” (qisqa, lo‘nda) uning eski sodda uslubini tasvirlaydi, yangisini emas. “Candid” (ochiq, samimiy) gaplarning bezakdorligi haqida hech narsa demaydi. “Halting” (duduqlanuvchi, uzuq-yuluq) uzun, to‘lib-toshgan gaplarga mos kelmaydi.\",\"estimated_seconds\":85,\"source\":\"original\",\"tags\":[\"core-v2\"]}]" }
